0x40000C08 C   FIELD 00w03 SMS (=TIM2.SMCR.SMS) (rw): Slave mode selection When external signals are selected the active edge of the trigger signal (tim_trgi) is linked to the polarity selected on the external input (see Input Control register and Control Register description. Note: The gated mode must not be used if tim_ti1f_ed is selected as the trigger input (TS=00100). Indeed, tim_ti1f_ed outputs 1 pulse for each transition on tim_ti1f, whereas the gated mode checks the level of the trigger signal. Note: The clock of the slave peripherals (timer, ADC, ...) receiving the tim_trgo signal must be enabled prior to receive events from the master timer, and the clock frequency (prescaler) must not be changed on-the-fly while triggers are received from the master timer.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 03w01 OCCS (=TIM2.SMCR.OCCS) (rw): OCREF clear selection This bit is used to select the OCREF clear source Note: If the OCREF clear selection feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and forced by hardware to '0'. .
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 04w03 TS (rw): Trigger selection (see bits 21:20 for TS[4:3]) This bit-field selects the trigger input to be used to synchronize the counter. Others: Reserved See for product specific implementation details. Note: These bits must be changed only when they are not used (e.g. when SMS=000) to avoid wrong edge detections at the transition.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 07w01 MSM (=TIM2.SMCR.MSM) (rw): Master/Slave mode
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 08w04 ETF (=TIM2.SMCR.ETF) (rw): External trigger filter This bit-field then defines the frequency used to sample tim_etrp signal and the length of the digital filter applied to tim_etrp. The digital filter is made of an event counter in which N consecutive events are needed to validate a transition on the output:
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 12w02 ETPS (=TIM2.SMCR.ETPS) (rw): External trigger prescaler External trigger signal tim_etrp frequency must be at most 1/4 of tim_ker_ck frequency. A prescaler can be enabled to reduce tim_etrp frequency. It is useful when inputting fast external clocks on tim_etr_in.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 14w01 ECE (=TIM2.SMCR.ECE) (rw): External clock enable This bit enables External clock mode 2. Note: Setting the ECE bit has the same effect as selecting external clock mode 1 with tim_trgi connected to tim_etrf (SMS=111 and TS=00111). It is possible to simultaneously use external clock mode 2 with the following slave modes: reset mode, gated mode and trigger mode. Nevertheless, tim_trgi must not be connected to tim_etrf in this case (TS bits must not be 00111). If external clock mode 1 and external clock mode 2 are enabled at the same time, the external clock input is tim_etrf.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 15w01 ETP (=TIM2.SMCR.ETP) (rw): External trigger polarity This bit selects whether tim_etr_in or tim_etr_in is used for trigger operations
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 16w01 SMS_3 (=TIM2.SMCR.SMS_3) (rw): Slave mode selection When external signals are selected the active edge of the trigger signal (tim_trgi) is linked to the polarity selected on the external input (see Input Control register and Control Register description. Note: The gated mode must not be used if tim_ti1f_ed is selected as the trigger input (TS=00100). Indeed, tim_ti1f_ed outputs 1 pulse for each transition on tim_ti1f, whereas the gated mode checks the level of the trigger signal. Note: The clock of the slave peripherals (timer, ADC, ...) receiving the tim_trgo signal must be enabled prior to receive events from the master timer, and the clock frequency (prescaler) must not be changed on-the-fly while triggers are received from the master timer.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 20w02 TS2 (rw): Trigger selection (see bits 21:20 for TS[4:3]) This bit-field selects the trigger input to be used to synchronize the counter. Others: Reserved See for product specific implementation details. Note: These bits must be changed only when they are not used (e.g. when SMS=000) to avoid wrong edge detections at the transition.
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 24w01 SMSPE (=TIM2.SMCR.SMSPE) (rw): SMS preload enable This bit selects whether the SMS[3:0] bitfield is preloaded
0x40000C08 C   FIELD 25w01 SMSPS (=TIM2.SMCR.SMSPS) (rw): SMS preload source This bit selects whether the events that triggers the SMS[3:0] bitfield transfer from preload to active
0x40000C0C B  REGISTER DIER (=TIM2.DIER): TIM5 DMA/Interrupt enable register
0x40000C10 B  REGISTER SR (=TIM2.SR): TIM5 status register
0x40000C14 B  REGISTER EGR (=TIM2.EGR): TIM5 event generation register
