0x40031400 A PERIPHERAL DCACHE
0x40031400 B  REGISTER CR: DCACHE control register
0x40031400 C   FIELD 00w01 EN (rw): enable
0x40031400 C   FIELD 01w01 CACHEINV (wo): full cache invalidation Can be set by software, only when EN = 1. Cleared by hardware when the BUSYF flag is set (during full cache invalidation operation). Writing 0 has no effect.
0x40031400 C   FIELD 08w03 CACHECMD (rw): cache command maintenance operation (cleans and/or invalidates an address range) Can be set and cleared by software, only when no maintenance command is ongoing (BUSYCMDF = 0). others: reserved
0x40031400 C   FIELD 11w01 STARTCMD (wo): starts maintenance command (maintenance operation defined in CACHECMD). Can be set by software, only when EN = 1, BUSYCMDF = 0, BUSYF = 0 and CACHECMD = 0b001, 0b010 or 0b011. Cleared by hardware when the BUSYCMDF flag is set (during cache maintenance operation). Writing 0 has no effect.
0x40031400 C   FIELD 16w01 RHITMEN (rw): read-hit monitor enable
0x40031400 C   FIELD 17w01 RMISSMEN (rw): read-miss monitor enable
0x40031400 C   FIELD 18w01 RHITMRST (rw): read-hit monitor reset
0x40031400 C   FIELD 19w01 RMISSMRST (rw): read-miss monitor reset
0x40031400 C   FIELD 20w01 WHITMEN (rw): write-hit monitor enable
0x40031400 C   FIELD 21w01 WMISSMEN (rw): write-miss monitor enable
0x40031400 C   FIELD 22w01 WHITMRST (rw): write-hit monitor reset
0x40031400 C   FIELD 23w01 WMISSMRST (rw): write-miss monitor reset
0x40031400 C   FIELD 31w01 HBURST (rw): output burst type for cache master port read accesses Write access is always done in INCR burst type.
0x40031404 B  REGISTER SR: DCACHE status register
0x40031404 C   FIELD 00w01 BUSYF (ro): full invalidate busy flag
0x40031404 C   FIELD 01w01 BSYENDF (ro): full invalidate busy end flag Cleared by writing DCACHE_FCR.CBSYENDF = 1.
0x40031404 C   FIELD 02w01 ERRF (ro): cache error flag Cleared by writing DCACHE_FCR.CERRF = 1.
0x40031404 C   FIELD 03w01 BUSYCMDF (ro): command busy flag
0x40031404 C   FIELD 04w01 CMDENDF (ro): command end flag Cleared by writing DCACHE_FCR.CCMDENDF = 1.
0x40031408 B  REGISTER IER: DCACHE interrupt enable register
0x40031408 C   FIELD 01w01 BSYENDIE (rw): interrupt enable on busy end Set by SW to enable an interrupt generation at the end of a cache full invalidate operation.
0x40031408 C   FIELD 02w01 ERRIE (rw): interrupt enable on cache error Set by software to enable an interrupt generation in case of cache functional error (eviction or clean operation write-back error)
0x40031408 C   FIELD 04w01 CMDENDIE (rw): interrupt enable on command end Set by software to enable an interrupt generation at the end of a cache command (clean and/or invalidate an address range)
0x4003140C B  REGISTER FCR: DCACHE flag clear register
0x4003140C C   FIELD 01w01 CBSYENDF (wo): clear full invalidate busy end flag Set by software.
0x4003140C C   FIELD 02w01 CERRF (wo): clear cache error flag Set by software.
0x4003140C C   FIELD 04w01 CCMDENDF (wo): clear command end flag Set by software.
0x40031410 B  REGISTER RHMONR: DCACHE read-hit monitor register
0x40031410 C   FIELD 00w32 RHITMON (ro): cache read-hit monitor counter
0x40031414 B  REGISTER RMMONR: DCACHE read-miss monitor register
0x40031414 C   FIELD 00w16 RMISSMON (ro): cache read-miss monitor counter
0x40031420 B  REGISTER WHMONR: DCACHE write-hit monitor register
0x40031420 C   FIELD 00w32 WHITMON (ro): cache write-hit monitor counter
0x40031424 B  REGISTER WMMONR: DCACHE write-miss monitor register
0x40031424 C   FIELD 00w16 WMISSMON (ro): cache write-miss monitor counter
0x40031428 B  REGISTER CMDRSADDRR: DCACHE command range start address register
0x40031428 C   FIELD 04w28 CMDSTARTADDR (rw): start address of range to which the cache maintenance command specified in DCACHE_CR.CACHECMD field applies This register must be set before DCACHE_CR.CACHECMD is written. .
0x4003142C B  REGISTER CMDREADDRR: DCACHE command range end address register
0x4003142C C   FIELD 04w28 CMDENDADDR (rw): end address of range to which the cache maintenance command specified in DCACHE_CR.CACHECMD field applies This register must be set before DCACHE_CR.CACHECMD is written.
