0x40032440 B  REGISTER MPCWM1ACFGR: GTZC1 TZSC memory 1 sub-region A watermark configuration register
0x40032440 C   FIELD 00w01 SREN (rw): Sub-region z enable Note: External memories that are watermark controlled start fully non-secure/unprivileged at reset when TZEN = 0xC3. When TZEN = 0xB4, external memories start fully secure/fully privileged (inverted reset-value).
0x40032440 C   FIELD 01w01 SRLOCK (rw): Sub-region A lock This bit, once set, can be cleared only by a system reset.
0x40032440 C   FIELD 08w01 SEC (rw): Secure sub-region A of base region x This bit is taken into account only if SREN is set.
0x40032440 C   FIELD 09w01 PRIV (rw): Privileged sub-region A of base region x This bit is taken into account only if SREN is set.
0x40032444 B  REGISTER MPCWM1AR: GTZC1 TZSC memory 1 sub-region A watermark register
0x40032444 C   FIELD 00w11 SUBA_START (rw): Start of sub-region A in region x This field defines the address offset of the sub-region A, to be multiplied by the granularity defined in Table30, versus the start of the region x. External memories that are watermark controlled, start fully non-secure at reset when TZEN=0xC3. When TZEN=0xB4, external memories start fully secure (inverted reset value).
0x40032444 C   FIELD 16w12 SUBA_LENGTH (rw): Length of sub-region A in region x This field defines the length of the sub-region A, to be multiplied by the granularity defined in Table30. When SUBA_START + SUBA_LENGTH is higher than the maximum size allowed for the memory, a saturation of SUBA_LENGTH is applied automatically. If SUBA_LENGTH = 0, the sub-region A is disabled.(SREN bit in GTZC1_TZSC_MPCMWxACFGR is cleared).
0x40032448 B  REGISTER MPCWM1BCFGR: GTZC1 TZSC memory 1 sub-region B watermark configuration register
0x40032448 C   FIELD 00w01 SREN (rw): Sub-region B enable Note: External memories that are watermark controlled start fully non-secure/unprivileged at reset when TZEN = 0xC3. When TZEN = 0xB4, external memories start fully secure/fully privileged (inverted reset-value).
0x40032448 C   FIELD 01w01 SRLOCK (rw): Sub-region B lock This bit, once set, can be cleared only by a system reset.
0x40032448 C   FIELD 08w01 SEC (rw): Secure sub-region B of base region x This bit is taken into account only if SREN is set.
0x40032448 C   FIELD 09w01 PRIV (rw): Privileged sub-region B of base region x This bit is taken into account only if SREN is set.
0x4003244C B  REGISTER MPCWM1BR: GTZC1 TZSC memory 1 sub-region B watermark register
0x4003244C C   FIELD 00w11 SUBB_START (rw): Start of sub-region B in region x This field defines the address offset of the sub-region B, to be multiplied by the granularity defined in Table30, versus the start of the region x. External memories that are watermark controlled, start fully non-secure at reset when TZEN=0xC3. When TZEN=0xB4, external memories start fully secure (inverted reset value).
