0x440240FC B  REGISTER SR: DBGMCU status register
0x440240FC C   FIELD 00w16 AP_PRESENT (wo): Bit n identifies whether access port AP n is present in device Bit n = 0: APn absent Bit n = 1: APn present
0x440240FC C   FIELD 16w16 AP_ENABLED (wo): Bit n identifies whether access port AP n is open (can be accessed via the debug port) or locked (debug access to the AP is blocked) Bit n = 0: APn locked Bit n = 1: APn enabled
0x44024100 B  REGISTER DBG_AUTH_HOST: DBGMCU debug authentication mailbox host register
0x44024100 C   FIELD 00w32 MESSAGE (rw): Debug host to device mailbox message. During debug authentication the debug host communicates with the device via this register.
0x44024104 B  REGISTER DBG_AUTH_DEVICE: DBGMCU debug authentication mailbox device register
0x44024104 C   FIELD 00w32 MESSAGE (ro): Device to debug host mailbox message. During debug authentication the device communicates with the debug host via this register.
0x44024108 B  REGISTER DBG_AUTH_ACK: DBGMCU debug authentication mailbox acknowledge register
0x44024108 C   FIELD 00w01 HOST_ACK (rw): Host to device acknowledge. The device sets this bit to indicate that it has placed a message in the DBGMCU_DBG_AUTH_DEVICE register. It should be reset by the host after reading the message
0x44024108 C   FIELD 01w01 DEV_ACK (rw): Device to device acknowledge. The host sets this bit to indicate that it has placed a message in the DBGMCU_DBG_AUTH_HOST register. It is reset by the device after reading the message
0x44024FD0 B  REGISTER PIDR4: DBGMCU CoreSight peripheral identity register 4
0x44024FD0 C   FIELD 00w04 JEP106CON (ro): JEP106 continuation code
0x44024FD0 C   FIELD 04w04 SIZE (ro): register file size
0x44024FE0 B  REGISTER PIDR0: DBGMCU CoreSight peripheral identity register 0
0x44024FE0 C   FIELD 00w08 PARTNUM (ro): part number bits [7:0]
0x44024FE4 B  REGISTER PIDR1: DBGMCU CoreSight peripheral identity register 1
0x44024FE4 C   FIELD 00w04 PARTNUM (ro): part number bits [11:8]
0x44024FE4 C   FIELD 04w04 JEP106ID (ro): JEP106 identity code bits [3:0]
0x44024FE8 B  REGISTER PIDR2: DBGMCU CoreSight peripheral identity register 2
0x44024FE8 C   FIELD 00w03 JEP106ID (ro): JEP106 identity code bits [6:4]
0x44024FE8 C   FIELD 03w01 JEDEC (ro): JEDEC assigned value
0x44024FE8 C   FIELD 04w04 REVISION (ro): component revision number
0x44024FEC B  REGISTER PIDR3: DBGMCU CoreSight peripheral identity register 3
0x44024FEC C   FIELD 00w04 CMOD (ro): customer modified
0x44024FEC C   FIELD 04w04 REVAND (ro): metal fix version
0x44024FF0 B  REGISTER CIDR0: DBGMCU CoreSight component identity register 0
0x44024FF0 C   FIELD 00w08 PREAMBLE (ro): component identification bits [7:0]
0x44024FF4 B  REGISTER CIDR1: DBGMCU CoreSight component identity register 1
0x44024FF4 C   FIELD 00w04 PREAMBLE (ro): component identification bits [11:8]
0x44024FF4 C   FIELD 04w04 CLASS (ro): component identification bits [15:12]component class
0x44024FF8 B  REGISTER CIDR2: DBGMCU CoreSight component identity register 2
0x44024FF8 C   FIELD 00w08 PREAMBLE (ro): component identification bits [23:16]
0x44024FFC B  REGISTER CIDR3: DBGMCU CoreSight component identity register 3
0x44024FFC C   FIELD 00w08 PREAMBLE (ro): component identification bits [31:24]
0x46008000 A PERIPHERAL SDMMC1
0x46008000 B  REGISTER POWER: SDMMC_POWER
0x46008000 C   FIELD 00w02 PWRCTRL (rw): SDMMC state control bits These bits can only be written when the SDMMC is not in the power-on state (PWRCTRL different 11). These bits are used to define the functional state of the SDMMC signals: stopped, SDMMC_D[7:0], SDMMC_CMD and SDMMC_CK are driven high. Any further write is ignored, PWRCTRL value keeps 11.
0x46008000 C   FIELD 02w01 VSWITCH (rw): Voltage switch sequence start This bit is used to start the timing critical section of the voltage switch sequence:
0x46008000 C   FIELD 03w01 VSWITCHEN (rw): Voltage switch procedure enable This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). This bit is used to stop the SDMMC_CK after the voltage switch command response:
0x46008000 C   FIELD 04w01 DIRPOL (rw): Data and command direction signals polarity selection This bit can only be written when the SDMMC is in the power-off state (PWRCTRL = 00).
0x46008004 B  REGISTER CLKCR: SDMMC clock control register
0x46008004 C   FIELD 00w10 CLKDIV (rw): Clock divide factor This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). This field defines the divide factor between the input clock (sdmmc_ker_ck) and the output clock (SDMMC_CK): SDMMC_CK frequency = sdmmc_ker_ck / [2 * CLKDIV]. 0x0XX: etc.. 0xXXX: etc..
0x46008004 C   FIELD 12w01 PWRSAV (rw): Power saving configuration bit This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) For power saving, the SDMMC_CK clock output can be disabled when the bus is idle by setting PWRSAV:
0x46008004 C   FIELD 14w02 WIDBUS (rw): Wide bus mode enable bit This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008004 C   FIELD 16w01 NEGEDGE (rw): SDMMC_CK dephasing selection bit for data and command This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). When clock division = 1 (CLKDIV = 0), this bit has no effect. Data and Command change on SDMMC_CK falling edge. Command and data changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding the rising edge of SDMMC_CK. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge. When clock division 1 (CLKDIV 0) & DDR = 1: Command changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding the rising edge of SDMMC_CK. Data changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding a SDMMC_CK edge. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge. Command and data changed on the same sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge generating the SDMMC_CK falling edge. When clock division 1 (CLKDIV 0) & DDR = 1: Command changed on the same sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge generating the SDMMC_CK falling edge. Data changed on the SDMMC_CK falling edge succeeding a SDMMC_CK edge. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge.
0x46008004 C   FIELD 17w01 HWFC_EN (rw): Hardware flow control enable This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) When Hardware flow control is enabled, the meaning of the TXFIFOE and RXFIFOF flags change, please see SDMMC status register definition in .
0x46008004 C   FIELD 18w01 DDR (rw): Data rate signaling selection This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) DDR rate must only be selected with 4-bit or 8-bit wide bus mode. (WIDBUS 00). DDR = 1 has no effect when WIDBUS = 00 (1-bit wide bus). DDR rate must only be selected with clock division 1. (CLKDIV 0)
0x46008004 C   FIELD 19w01 BUSSPEED (rw): Bus speed for selection of SDMMC operating modes This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008004 C   FIELD 20w02 SELCLKRX (rw): Receive clock selection These bits can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008008 B  REGISTER ARGR: SDMMC argument register
0x46008008 C   FIELD 00w32 CMDARG (rw): Command argument These bits can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). Command argument sent to a card as part of a command message. If a command contains an argument, it must be loaded into this register before writing a command to the command register.
0x4600800C B  REGISTER CMDR: SDMMC command register
0x4600800C C   FIELD 00w06 CMDINDEX (rw): Command index This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). The command index is sent to the card as part of a command message.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 06w01 CMDTRANS (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a data transfer command, stops the interrupt period, and signals DataEnable to the DPSM This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). If this bit is set, the CPSM issues an end of interrupt period and issues DataEnable signal to the DPSM when the command is sent.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSTOP (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a Stop Transmission command and signals abort to the DPSM This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). If this bit is set, the CPSM issues the abort signal to the DPSM when the command is sent.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 08w02 WAITRESP (rw): Wait for response bits This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). They are used to configure whether the CPSM is to wait for a response, and if yes, which kind of response.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 10w01 WAITINT (rw): CPSM waits for interrupt request If this bit is set, the CPSM disables command timeout and waits for an card interrupt request (Response). If this bit is cleared in the CPSM Wait state, it causes the abort of the interrupt mode.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 11w01 WAITPEND (rw): CPSM waits for end of data transfer (CmdPend internal signal) from DPSM This bit when set, the CPSM waits for the end of data transfer trigger before it starts sending a command. WAITPEND is only taken into account when DTMODE = eMMC stream data transfer, WIDBUS = 1-bit wide bus mode, DPSMACT = 1 and DTDIR = from host to card.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 12w01 CPSMEN (rw): Command path state machine (CPSM) enable bit This bit is written 1 by firmware, and cleared by hardware when the CPSM enters the Idle state. If this bit is set, the CPSM is enabled. When DTEN = 1, no command is transfered nor boot procedure is started. CPSMEN is cleared to 0. During Read Wait with SDMMC_CK stopped no command is sent and CPSMEN is kept 0.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 13w01 DTHOLD (rw): Hold new data block transmission and reception in the DPSM If this bit is set, the DPSM does not move from the Wait_S state to the Send state or from the Wait_R state to the Receive state.
0x4600800C C   FIELD 14w01 BOOTMODE (rw): Select the boot mode procedure to be used This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0)
0x4600800C C   FIELD 15w01 BOOTEN (rw): Enable boot mode procedure
0x4600800C C   FIELD 16w01 CMDSUSPEND (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a Suspend or Resume command and signals interrupt period start/end This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). CMDSUSPEND = 1 and CMDTRANS = 0 Suspend command, start interrupt period when response bit BS=0. CMDSUSPEND = 1 and CMDTRANS = 1 Resume command with data, end interrupt period when response bit DF=1.
0x46008010 B  REGISTER RESPCMDR: SDMMC command response register
0x46008010 C   FIELD 00w06 RESPCMD (ro): Response command index Read-only bit field. Contains the command index of the last command response received.
0x46008014 B  REGISTER RESP1R: SDMMC response 1 register
0x46008014 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008018 B  REGISTER RESP2R: SDMMC response 2 register
0x46008018 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x4600801C B  REGISTER RESP3R: SDMMC response 3 register
0x4600801C C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008020 B  REGISTER RESP4R: SDMMC response 4 register
0x46008020 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008024 B  REGISTER DTIMER: SDMMC data timer register
0x46008024 C   FIELD 00w32 DATATIME (rw): Data and R1b busy timeout period This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). Data and R1b busy timeout period expressed in card bus clock periods.
0x46008028 B  REGISTER DLENR: SDMMC data length register
0x46008028 C   FIELD 00w25 DATALENGTH (rw): Data length value This register can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). Number of data bytes to be transferred. When DDR = 1 DATALENGTH is truncated to a multiple of 2. (The last odd byte is not transfered) When DATALENGTH = 0 no data are transfered, when requested by a CPSMEN and CMDTRANS = 1 also no command is transfered. DTEN and CPSMEN are cleared to 0.
0x4600802C B  REGISTER DCTRL: SDMMC data control register
0x4600802C C   FIELD 00w01 DTEN (rw): Data transfer enable bit This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). This bit is cleared by Hardware when data transfer completes. This bit must only be used to transfer data when no associated data transfer command is used, i.e. must not be used with SD or eMMC cards.
0x4600802C C   FIELD 01w01 DTDIR (rw): Data transfer direction selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x4600802C C   FIELD 02w02 DTMODE (rw): Data transfer mode selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x4600802C C   FIELD 04w04 DBLOCKSIZE (rw): Data block size This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). Define the data block length when the block data transfer mode is selected: When DATALENGTH is not a multiple of DBLOCKSIZE, the transfered data is truncated at a multiple of DBLOCKSIZE. (None of the remaining data are transfered.) When DDR = 1, DBLOCKSIZE = 0000 must not be used. (No data are transfered)
0x4600802C C   FIELD 08w01 RWSTART (rw): Read Wait start If this bit is set, Read Wait operation starts.
0x4600802C C   FIELD 09w01 RWSTOP (rw): Read Wait stop This bit is written by firmware and auto cleared by hardware when the DPSM moves from the R_W state to the Wait_R or Idle state.
0x4600802C C   FIELD 10w01 RWMOD (rw): Read Wait mode This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x4600802C C   FIELD 11w01 SDIOEN (rw): SD I/O interrupt enable functions This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). If this bit is set, the DPSM enables the SD I/O card specific interrupt operation.
0x4600802C C   FIELD 12w01 BOOTACKEN (rw): Enable the reception of the boot acknowledgment This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x4600802C C   FIELD 13w01 FIFORST (rw): FIFO reset, flushes any remaining data This bit can only be written by firmware when IDMAEN= 0 and DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). This bit only takes effect when a transfer error or transfer hold occurs.
0x46008030 B  REGISTER DCNTR: SDMMC data counter register
0x46008030 C   FIELD 00w25 DATACOUNT (ro): Data count value When read, the number of remaining data bytes to be transferred is returned. Write has no effect.
0x46008034 B  REGISTER STAR: SDMMC status register
0x46008034 C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAIL (ro): Command response received (CRC check failed) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAIL (ro): Data block sent/received (CRC check failed) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUT (ro): Command response timeout Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR. The Command Timeout period has a fixed value of 64 SDMMC_CK clock periods.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUT (ro): Data timeout Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERR (ro): Transmit FIFO underrun error (masked by hardware when IDMA is enabled) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERR (ro): Received FIFO overrun error (masked by hardware when IDMA is enabled) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 06w01 CMDREND (ro): Command response received (CRC check passed, or no CRC) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENT (ro): Command sent (no response required) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 08w01 DATAEND (ro): Data transfer ended correctly DATAEND is set if data counter DATACOUNT is zero and no errors occur, and no transmit data transfer hold. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLD (ro): Data transfer Hold Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKEND (ro): Data block sent/received DBCKEND is set when: - CRC check passed and DPSM moves to the R_W state or - IDMAEN = 0 and transmit data transfer hold and DATACOUNT 0 and DPSM moves to Wait_S. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 11w01 DABORT (ro): Data transfer aborted by CMD12 Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 12w01 DPSMACT (ro): Data path state machine active, i.e. not in Idle state This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 13w01 CPSMACT (ro): Command path state machine active, i.e. not in Idle state This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 14w01 TXFIFOHE (ro): Transmit FIFO half empty At least half the number of words can be written into the FIFO. This bit is cleared when the FIFO becomes half+1 full.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 15w01 RXFIFOHF (ro): Receive FIFO half full There are at least half the number of words in the FIFO. This bit is cleared when the FIFO becomes half+1 empty.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 16w01 TXFIFOF (ro): Transmit FIFO full This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt. This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes empty.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 17w01 RXFIFOF (ro): Receive FIFO full This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes empty.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 18w01 TXFIFOE (ro): Transmit FIFO empty This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes full.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 19w01 RXFIFOE (ro): Receive FIFO empty This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt. This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes full.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 20w01 BUSYD0 (ro): Inverted value of SDMMC_D0 line (Busy), sampled at the end of a CMD response and a second time 2 SDMMC_CK cycles after the CMD response This bit is reset to not busy when the SDMMCD0 line changes from busy to not busy. This bit does not signal busy due to data transfer. This is a hardware status flag only, it does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0END (ro): end of SDMMC_D0 Busy following a CMD response detected This indicates only end of busy following a CMD response. This bit does not signal busy due to data transfer. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOIT (ro): SDIO interrupt received The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAIL (ro): Boot acknowledgment received (boot acknowledgment check fail) The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUT (ro): Boot acknowledgment timeout The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 25w01 VSWEND (ro): Voltage switch critical timing section completion The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOP (ro): SDMMC_CK stopped in Voltage switch procedure The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 27w01 IDMATE (ro): IDMA transfer error The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008034 C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTC (ro): IDMA buffer transfer complete The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008038 B  REGISTER ICR: SDMMC interrupt clear register
0x46008038 C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAILC (rw): CCRCFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CCRCFAIL flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAILC (rw): DCRCFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DCRCFAIL flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUTC (rw): CTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUTC (rw): DTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERRC (rw): TXUNDERR flag clear bit Set by software to clear TXUNDERR flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERRC (rw): RXOVERR flag clear bit Set by software to clear the RXOVERR flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 06w01 CMDRENDC (rw): CMDREND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CMDREND flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENTC (rw): CMDSENT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CMDSENT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 08w01 DATAENDC (rw): DATAEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DATAEND flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLDC (rw): DHOLD flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DHOLD flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKENDC (rw): DBCKEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DBCKEND flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 11w01 DABORTC (rw): DABORT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DABORT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0ENDC (rw): BUSYD0END flag clear bit Set by software to clear the BUSYD0END flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOITC (rw): SDIOIT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the SDIOIT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAILC (rw): ACKFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the ACKFAIL flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUTC (rw): ACKTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the ACKTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 25w01 VSWENDC (rw): VSWEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the VSWEND flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOPC (rw): CKSTOP flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CKSTOP flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 27w01 IDMATEC (rw): IDMA transfer error clear bit Set by software to clear the IDMATE flag.
0x46008038 C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTCC (rw): IDMA buffer transfer complete clear bit Set by software to clear the IDMABTC flag.
0x4600803C B  REGISTER MASKR: SDMMC mask register
0x4600803C C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAILIE (rw): Command CRC fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by command CRC failure.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAILIE (rw): Data CRC fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data CRC failure.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUTIE (rw): Command timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by command timeout.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUTIE (rw): Data timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data timeout.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERRIE (rw): Tx FIFO underrun error interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO underrun error.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERRIE (rw): Rx FIFO overrun error interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO overrun error.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 06w01 CMDRENDIE (rw): Command response received interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by receiving command response.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENTIE (rw): Command sent interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by sending command.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 08w01 DATAENDIE (rw): Data end interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data end.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLDIE (rw): Data hold interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when sending new data is hold in the DPSM Wait_S state.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKENDIE (rw): Data block end interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data block end.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 11w01 DABORTIE (rw): Data transfer aborted interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by a data transfer being aborted.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 14w01 TXFIFOHEIE (rw): Tx FIFO half empty interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO half empty.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 15w01 RXFIFOHFIE (rw): Rx FIFO half full interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO half full.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 17w01 RXFIFOFIE (rw): Rx FIFO full interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO full.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 18w01 TXFIFOEIE (rw): Tx FIFO empty interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO empty.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0ENDIE (rw): BUSYD0END interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when SDMMC_D0 signal changes from busy to NOT busy following a CMD response.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOITIE (rw): SDIO mode interrupt received interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when receiving the SDIO mode interrupt.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAILIE (rw): Acknowledgment Fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by acknowledgment Fail.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUTIE (rw): Acknowledgment timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by acknowledgment timeout.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 25w01 VSWENDIE (rw): Voltage switch critical timing section completion interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when voltage switch critical timing section completion.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOPIE (rw): Voltage Switch clock stopped interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Voltage Switch clock stopped.
0x4600803C C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTCIE (rw): IDMA buffer transfer complete interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when the IDMA has transferred all data belonging to a memory buffer.
0x46008040 B  REGISTER ACKTIMER: SDMMC acknowledgment timer register
0x46008040 C   FIELD 00w25 ACKTIME (rw): Boot acknowledgment timeout period This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). Boot acknowledgment timeout period expressed in card bus clock periods.
0x46008050 B  REGISTER IDMACTRLR: SDMMC DMA control register
0x46008050 C   FIELD 00w01 IDMAEN (rw): IDMA enable This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008050 C   FIELD 01w01 IDMABMODE (rw): Buffer mode selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008054 B  REGISTER IDMABSIZER: SDMMC IDMA buffer size register
0x46008054 C   FIELD 05w12 IDMABNDT (rw): Number of bytes per buffer This 12-bit value must be multiplied by 8 to get the size of the buffer in 32-bit words and by 32 to get the size of the buffer in bytes. Example: IDMABNDT = 0x001: buffer size = 8 words = 32 bytes. Example: IDMABNDT = 0x800: buffer size = 16384 words = 64 Kbyte. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008058 B  REGISTER IDMABASER: SDMMC IDMA buffer base address register
0x46008058 C   FIELD 00w32 IDMABASE (rw): Buffer memory base address bits [31:2], must be word aligned (bit [1:0] are always 0 and read only) This register can be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0), and can dynamically be written by firmware when DPSM active (DPSMACT = 1).
0x46008064 B  REGISTER IDMALAR: SDMMC_IDMALAR
0x46008064 C   FIELD 02w14 IDMALA (rw): Word aligned linked list item address offset Linked list item offset pointer to the base of the next linked list item structure. Linked list item base address is IDMABA + IDMALA. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008064 C   FIELD 29w01 ABR (rw): Acknowledge linked list buffer ready This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). This bit is not taken into account when starting the first linked list buffer from the software programmed register information. ABR is only taken into account on subsequent loaded linked list items.
0x46008064 C   FIELD 30w01 ULS (rw): Update SDMMC_IDMABSIZE from the next linked list when in linked list mode (SDMMC_IDMACTRLR.IDMABMODE select linked list mode and ULA = 1) This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008064 C   FIELD 31w01 ULA (rw): Update SDMMC_IDMALAR from linked list when in linked list mode (SDMMC_IDMACTRLR.IDMABMODE select linked list mode) This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008068 B  REGISTER IDMABAR: SDMMC_IDMABAR
0x46008068 C   FIELD 02w30 IDMABA (rw): Word aligned Linked list memory base address Linked list memory base pointer. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008080 B  REGISTER FIFOR0: SDMMC data FIFO registers 0
0x46008080 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008084 B  REGISTER FIFOR1: SDMMC data FIFO registers 1
0x46008084 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008088 B  REGISTER FIFOR2: SDMMC data FIFO registers 2
0x46008088 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x4600808C B  REGISTER FIFOR3: SDMMC data FIFO registers 3
0x4600808C C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008090 B  REGISTER FIFOR4: SDMMC data FIFO registers 4
0x46008090 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008094 B  REGISTER FIFOR5: SDMMC data FIFO registers 5
0x46008094 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008098 B  REGISTER FIFOR6: SDMMC data FIFO registers 6
0x46008098 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x4600809C B  REGISTER FIFOR7: SDMMC data FIFO registers 7
0x4600809C C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080A0 B  REGISTER FIFOR8: SDMMC data FIFO registers 8
0x460080A0 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080A4 B  REGISTER FIFOR9: SDMMC data FIFO registers 9
0x460080A4 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080A8 B  REGISTER FIFOR10: SDMMC data FIFO registers 10
0x460080A8 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080AC B  REGISTER FIFOR11: SDMMC data FIFO registers 11
0x460080AC C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080B0 B  REGISTER FIFOR12: SDMMC data FIFO registers 12
0x460080B0 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080B4 B  REGISTER FIFOR13: SDMMC data FIFO registers 13
0x460080B4 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080B8 B  REGISTER FIFOR14: SDMMC data FIFO registers 14
0x460080B8 C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x460080BC B  REGISTER FIFOR15: SDMMC data FIFO registers 15
0x460080BC C   FIELD 00w32 FIFODATA (rw): Receive and transmit FIFO data This register can only be read or written by firmware when the DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). The FIFO data occupies 16 entries of 32-bit words.
0x46008400 A PERIPHERAL DLYBSD1
0x46008400 B  REGISTER CR (rw): control register
0x46008400 C   FIELD 00w01 DEN: Operational amplifier Enable
0x46008400 C   FIELD 01w01 SEN: OPALPM
0x46008404 B  REGISTER CFGR: configuration register
0x46008404 C   FIELD 00w04 SEL (rw): SEL
0x46008404 C   FIELD 08w07 UNIT (rw): UNIT
0x46008404 C   FIELD 16w12 LNG (ro): LNG
0x46008404 C   FIELD 31w01 LNGF (ro): LNGF
0x46008800 A PERIPHERAL DLYBSD2
0x46008800 B  REGISTER CR (rw): control register
0x46008800 C   FIELD 00w01 DEN: Operational amplifier Enable
0x46008800 C   FIELD 01w01 SEN: OPALPM
0x46008804 B  REGISTER CFGR: configuration register
0x46008804 C   FIELD 00w04 SEL (rw): SEL
0x46008804 C   FIELD 08w07 UNIT (rw): UNIT
0x46008804 C   FIELD 16w12 LNG (ro): LNG
0x46008804 C   FIELD 31w01 LNGF (ro): LNGF
0x46008C00 A PERIPHERAL SDMMC2
0x46008C00 B  REGISTER POWER: SDMMC_POWER
0x46008C00 C   FIELD 00w02 PWRCTRL (rw): SDMMC state control bits These bits can only be written when the SDMMC is not in the power-on state (PWRCTRL different 11). These bits are used to define the functional state of the SDMMC signals: stopped, SDMMC_D[7:0], SDMMC_CMD and SDMMC_CK are driven high. Any further write is ignored, PWRCTRL value keeps 11.
0x46008C00 C   FIELD 02w01 VSWITCH (rw): Voltage switch sequence start This bit is used to start the timing critical section of the voltage switch sequence:
0x46008C00 C   FIELD 03w01 VSWITCHEN (rw): Voltage switch procedure enable This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). This bit is used to stop the SDMMC_CK after the voltage switch command response:
0x46008C00 C   FIELD 04w01 DIRPOL (rw): Data and command direction signals polarity selection This bit can only be written when the SDMMC is in the power-off state (PWRCTRL = 00).
0x46008C04 B  REGISTER CLKCR: SDMMC clock control register
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 00w10 CLKDIV (rw): Clock divide factor This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). This field defines the divide factor between the input clock (sdmmc_ker_ck) and the output clock (SDMMC_CK): SDMMC_CK frequency = sdmmc_ker_ck / [2 * CLKDIV]. 0x0XX: etc.. 0xXXX: etc..
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 12w01 PWRSAV (rw): Power saving configuration bit This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) For power saving, the SDMMC_CK clock output can be disabled when the bus is idle by setting PWRSAV:
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 14w02 WIDBUS (rw): Wide bus mode enable bit This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 16w01 NEGEDGE (rw): SDMMC_CK dephasing selection bit for data and command This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). When clock division = 1 (CLKDIV = 0), this bit has no effect. Data and Command change on SDMMC_CK falling edge. Command and data changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding the rising edge of SDMMC_CK. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge. When clock division 1 (CLKDIV 0) & DDR = 1: Command changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding the rising edge of SDMMC_CK. Data changed on the sdmmc_ker_ck falling edge succeeding a SDMMC_CK edge. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge. Command and data changed on the same sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge generating the SDMMC_CK falling edge. When clock division 1 (CLKDIV 0) & DDR = 1: Command changed on the same sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge generating the SDMMC_CK falling edge. Data changed on the SDMMC_CK falling edge succeeding a SDMMC_CK edge. SDMMC_CK edge occurs on sdmmc_ker_ck rising edge.
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 17w01 HWFC_EN (rw): Hardware flow control enable This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) When Hardware flow control is enabled, the meaning of the TXFIFOE and RXFIFOF flags change, please see SDMMC status register definition in .
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 18w01 DDR (rw): Data rate signaling selection This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0) DDR rate must only be selected with 4-bit or 8-bit wide bus mode. (WIDBUS 00). DDR = 1 has no effect when WIDBUS = 00 (1-bit wide bus). DDR rate must only be selected with clock division 1. (CLKDIV 0)
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 19w01 BUSSPEED (rw): Bus speed for selection of SDMMC operating modes This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008C04 C   FIELD 20w02 SELCLKRX (rw): Receive clock selection These bits can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0)
0x46008C08 B  REGISTER ARGR: SDMMC argument register
0x46008C08 C   FIELD 00w32 CMDARG (rw): Command argument These bits can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). Command argument sent to a card as part of a command message. If a command contains an argument, it must be loaded into this register before writing a command to the command register.
0x46008C0C B  REGISTER CMDR: SDMMC command register
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 00w06 CMDINDEX (rw): Command index This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). The command index is sent to the card as part of a command message.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 06w01 CMDTRANS (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a data transfer command, stops the interrupt period, and signals DataEnable to the DPSM This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). If this bit is set, the CPSM issues an end of interrupt period and issues DataEnable signal to the DPSM when the command is sent.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSTOP (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a Stop Transmission command and signals abort to the DPSM This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). If this bit is set, the CPSM issues the abort signal to the DPSM when the command is sent.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 08w02 WAITRESP (rw): Wait for response bits This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). They are used to configure whether the CPSM is to wait for a response, and if yes, which kind of response.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 10w01 WAITINT (rw): CPSM waits for interrupt request If this bit is set, the CPSM disables command timeout and waits for an card interrupt request (Response). If this bit is cleared in the CPSM Wait state, it causes the abort of the interrupt mode.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 11w01 WAITPEND (rw): CPSM waits for end of data transfer (CmdPend internal signal) from DPSM This bit when set, the CPSM waits for the end of data transfer trigger before it starts sending a command. WAITPEND is only taken into account when DTMODE = eMMC stream data transfer, WIDBUS = 1-bit wide bus mode, DPSMACT = 1 and DTDIR = from host to card.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 12w01 CPSMEN (rw): Command path state machine (CPSM) enable bit This bit is written 1 by firmware, and cleared by hardware when the CPSM enters the Idle state. If this bit is set, the CPSM is enabled. When DTEN = 1, no command is transfered nor boot procedure is started. CPSMEN is cleared to 0. During Read Wait with SDMMC_CK stopped no command is sent and CPSMEN is kept 0.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 13w01 DTHOLD (rw): Hold new data block transmission and reception in the DPSM If this bit is set, the DPSM does not move from the Wait_S state to the Send state or from the Wait_R state to the Receive state.
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 14w01 BOOTMODE (rw): Select the boot mode procedure to be used This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0)
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 15w01 BOOTEN (rw): Enable boot mode procedure
0x46008C0C C   FIELD 16w01 CMDSUSPEND (rw): The CPSM treats the command as a Suspend or Resume command and signals interrupt period start/end This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). CMDSUSPEND = 1 and CMDTRANS = 0 Suspend command, start interrupt period when response bit BS=0. CMDSUSPEND = 1 and CMDTRANS = 1 Resume command with data, end interrupt period when response bit DF=1.
0x46008C10 B  REGISTER RESPCMDR: SDMMC command response register
0x46008C10 C   FIELD 00w06 RESPCMD (ro): Response command index Read-only bit field. Contains the command index of the last command response received.
0x46008C14 B  REGISTER RESP1R: SDMMC response 1 register
0x46008C14 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008C18 B  REGISTER RESP2R: SDMMC response 2 register
0x46008C18 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008C1C B  REGISTER RESP3R: SDMMC response 3 register
0x46008C1C C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008C20 B  REGISTER RESP4R: SDMMC response 4 register
0x46008C20 C   FIELD 00w32 CARDSTATUSx (ro): Card status x See .
0x46008C24 B  REGISTER DTIMER: SDMMC data timer register
0x46008C24 C   FIELD 00w32 DATATIME (rw): Data and R1b busy timeout period This bit can only be written when the CPSM and DPSM are not active (CPSMACT = 0 and DPSMACT = 0). Data and R1b busy timeout period expressed in card bus clock periods.
0x46008C28 B  REGISTER DLENR: SDMMC data length register
0x46008C28 C   FIELD 00w25 DATALENGTH (rw): Data length value This register can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). Number of data bytes to be transferred. When DDR = 1 DATALENGTH is truncated to a multiple of 2. (The last odd byte is not transfered) When DATALENGTH = 0 no data are transfered, when requested by a CPSMEN and CMDTRANS = 1 also no command is transfered. DTEN and CPSMEN are cleared to 0.
0x46008C2C B  REGISTER DCTRL: SDMMC data control register
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 00w01 DTEN (rw): Data transfer enable bit This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). This bit is cleared by Hardware when data transfer completes. This bit must only be used to transfer data when no associated data transfer command is used, i.e. must not be used with SD or eMMC cards.
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 01w01 DTDIR (rw): Data transfer direction selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 02w02 DTMODE (rw): Data transfer mode selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 04w04 DBLOCKSIZE (rw): Data block size This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). Define the data block length when the block data transfer mode is selected: When DATALENGTH is not a multiple of DBLOCKSIZE, the transfered data is truncated at a multiple of DBLOCKSIZE. (None of the remaining data are transfered.) When DDR = 1, DBLOCKSIZE = 0000 must not be used. (No data are transfered)
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 08w01 RWSTART (rw): Read Wait start If this bit is set, Read Wait operation starts.
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 09w01 RWSTOP (rw): Read Wait stop This bit is written by firmware and auto cleared by hardware when the DPSM moves from the R_W state to the Wait_R or Idle state.
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 10w01 RWMOD (rw): Read Wait mode This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 11w01 SDIOEN (rw): SD I/O interrupt enable functions This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). If this bit is set, the DPSM enables the SD I/O card specific interrupt operation.
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 12w01 BOOTACKEN (rw): Enable the reception of the boot acknowledgment This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C2C C   FIELD 13w01 FIFORST (rw): FIFO reset, flushes any remaining data This bit can only be written by firmware when IDMAEN= 0 and DPSM is active (DPSMACT = 1). This bit only takes effect when a transfer error or transfer hold occurs.
0x46008C30 B  REGISTER DCNTR: SDMMC data counter register
0x46008C30 C   FIELD 00w25 DATACOUNT (ro): Data count value When read, the number of remaining data bytes to be transferred is returned. Write has no effect.
0x46008C34 B  REGISTER STAR: SDMMC status register
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAIL (ro): Command response received (CRC check failed) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAIL (ro): Data block sent/received (CRC check failed) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUT (ro): Command response timeout Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR. The Command Timeout period has a fixed value of 64 SDMMC_CK clock periods.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUT (ro): Data timeout Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERR (ro): Transmit FIFO underrun error (masked by hardware when IDMA is enabled) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERR (ro): Received FIFO overrun error (masked by hardware when IDMA is enabled) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 06w01 CMDREND (ro): Command response received (CRC check passed, or no CRC) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENT (ro): Command sent (no response required) Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 08w01 DATAEND (ro): Data transfer ended correctly DATAEND is set if data counter DATACOUNT is zero and no errors occur, and no transmit data transfer hold. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLD (ro): Data transfer Hold Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKEND (ro): Data block sent/received DBCKEND is set when: - CRC check passed and DPSM moves to the R_W state or - IDMAEN = 0 and transmit data transfer hold and DATACOUNT 0 and DPSM moves to Wait_S. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 11w01 DABORT (ro): Data transfer aborted by CMD12 Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 12w01 DPSMACT (ro): Data path state machine active, i.e. not in Idle state This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 13w01 CPSMACT (ro): Command path state machine active, i.e. not in Idle state This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 14w01 TXFIFOHE (ro): Transmit FIFO half empty At least half the number of words can be written into the FIFO. This bit is cleared when the FIFO becomes half+1 full.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 15w01 RXFIFOHF (ro): Receive FIFO half full There are at least half the number of words in the FIFO. This bit is cleared when the FIFO becomes half+1 empty.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 16w01 TXFIFOF (ro): Transmit FIFO full This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt. This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes empty.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 17w01 RXFIFOF (ro): Receive FIFO full This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes empty.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 18w01 TXFIFOE (ro): Transmit FIFO empty This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes full.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 19w01 RXFIFOE (ro): Receive FIFO empty This is a hardware status flag only, does not generate an interrupt. This bit is cleared when one FIFO location becomes full.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 20w01 BUSYD0 (ro): Inverted value of SDMMC_D0 line (Busy), sampled at the end of a CMD response and a second time 2 SDMMC_CK cycles after the CMD response This bit is reset to not busy when the SDMMCD0 line changes from busy to not busy. This bit does not signal busy due to data transfer. This is a hardware status flag only, it does not generate an interrupt.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0END (ro): end of SDMMC_D0 Busy following a CMD response detected This indicates only end of busy following a CMD response. This bit does not signal busy due to data transfer. Interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOIT (ro): SDIO interrupt received The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAIL (ro): Boot acknowledgment received (boot acknowledgment check fail) The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUT (ro): Boot acknowledgment timeout The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 25w01 VSWEND (ro): Voltage switch critical timing section completion The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOP (ro): SDMMC_CK stopped in Voltage switch procedure The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 27w01 IDMATE (ro): IDMA transfer error The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C34 C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTC (ro): IDMA buffer transfer complete The interrupt flag is cleared by writing corresponding interrupt clear bit in SDMMC_ICR.
0x46008C38 B  REGISTER ICR: SDMMC interrupt clear register
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAILC (rw): CCRCFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CCRCFAIL flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAILC (rw): DCRCFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DCRCFAIL flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUTC (rw): CTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUTC (rw): DTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERRC (rw): TXUNDERR flag clear bit Set by software to clear TXUNDERR flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERRC (rw): RXOVERR flag clear bit Set by software to clear the RXOVERR flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 06w01 CMDRENDC (rw): CMDREND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CMDREND flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENTC (rw): CMDSENT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CMDSENT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 08w01 DATAENDC (rw): DATAEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DATAEND flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLDC (rw): DHOLD flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DHOLD flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKENDC (rw): DBCKEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DBCKEND flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 11w01 DABORTC (rw): DABORT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the DABORT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0ENDC (rw): BUSYD0END flag clear bit Set by software to clear the BUSYD0END flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOITC (rw): SDIOIT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the SDIOIT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAILC (rw): ACKFAIL flag clear bit Set by software to clear the ACKFAIL flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUTC (rw): ACKTIMEOUT flag clear bit Set by software to clear the ACKTIMEOUT flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 25w01 VSWENDC (rw): VSWEND flag clear bit Set by software to clear the VSWEND flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOPC (rw): CKSTOP flag clear bit Set by software to clear the CKSTOP flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 27w01 IDMATEC (rw): IDMA transfer error clear bit Set by software to clear the IDMATE flag.
0x46008C38 C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTCC (rw): IDMA buffer transfer complete clear bit Set by software to clear the IDMABTC flag.
0x46008C3C B  REGISTER MASKR: SDMMC mask register
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 00w01 CCRCFAILIE (rw): Command CRC fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by command CRC failure.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 01w01 DCRCFAILIE (rw): Data CRC fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data CRC failure.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 02w01 CTIMEOUTIE (rw): Command timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by command timeout.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 03w01 DTIMEOUTIE (rw): Data timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data timeout.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 04w01 TXUNDERRIE (rw): Tx FIFO underrun error interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO underrun error.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 05w01 RXOVERRIE (rw): Rx FIFO overrun error interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO overrun error.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 06w01 CMDRENDIE (rw): Command response received interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by receiving command response.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 07w01 CMDSENTIE (rw): Command sent interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by sending command.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 08w01 DATAENDIE (rw): Data end interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data end.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 09w01 DHOLDIE (rw): Data hold interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when sending new data is hold in the DPSM Wait_S state.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 10w01 DBCKENDIE (rw): Data block end interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by data block end.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 11w01 DABORTIE (rw): Data transfer aborted interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by a data transfer being aborted.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 14w01 TXFIFOHEIE (rw): Tx FIFO half empty interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO half empty.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 15w01 RXFIFOHFIE (rw): Rx FIFO half full interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO half full.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 17w01 RXFIFOFIE (rw): Rx FIFO full interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Rx FIFO full.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 18w01 TXFIFOEIE (rw): Tx FIFO empty interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Tx FIFO empty.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 21w01 BUSYD0ENDIE (rw): BUSYD0END interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when SDMMC_D0 signal changes from busy to NOT busy following a CMD response.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 22w01 SDIOITIE (rw): SDIO mode interrupt received interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when receiving the SDIO mode interrupt.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 23w01 ACKFAILIE (rw): Acknowledgment Fail interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by acknowledgment Fail.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 24w01 ACKTIMEOUTIE (rw): Acknowledgment timeout interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by acknowledgment timeout.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 25w01 VSWENDIE (rw): Voltage switch critical timing section completion interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when voltage switch critical timing section completion.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 26w01 CKSTOPIE (rw): Voltage Switch clock stopped interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable interrupt caused by Voltage Switch clock stopped.
0x46008C3C C   FIELD 28w01 IDMABTCIE (rw): IDMA buffer transfer complete interrupt enable Set and cleared by software to enable/disable the interrupt generated when the IDMA has transferred all data belonging to a memory buffer.
0x46008C40 B  REGISTER ACKTIMER: SDMMC acknowledgment timer register
0x46008C40 C   FIELD 00w25 ACKTIME (rw): Boot acknowledgment timeout period This bit can only be written by firmware when CPSM is disabled (CPSMEN = 0). Boot acknowledgment timeout period expressed in card bus clock periods.
0x46008C50 B  REGISTER IDMACTRLR: SDMMC DMA control register
0x46008C50 C   FIELD 00w01 IDMAEN (rw): IDMA enable This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C50 C   FIELD 01w01 IDMABMODE (rw): Buffer mode selection This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C54 B  REGISTER IDMABSIZER: SDMMC IDMA buffer size register
0x46008C54 C   FIELD 05w12 IDMABNDT (rw): Number of bytes per buffer This 12-bit value must be multiplied by 8 to get the size of the buffer in 32-bit words and by 32 to get the size of the buffer in bytes. Example: IDMABNDT = 0x001: buffer size = 8 words = 32 bytes. Example: IDMABNDT = 0x800: buffer size = 16384 words = 64 Kbyte. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C58 B  REGISTER IDMABASER: SDMMC IDMA buffer base address register
0x46008C58 C   FIELD 00w32 IDMABASE (rw): Buffer memory base address bits [31:2], must be word aligned (bit [1:0] are always 0 and read only) This register can be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0), and can dynamically be written by firmware when DPSM active (DPSMACT = 1).
0x46008C64 B  REGISTER IDMALAR: SDMMC_IDMALAR
0x46008C64 C   FIELD 02w14 IDMALA (rw): Word aligned linked list item address offset Linked list item offset pointer to the base of the next linked list item structure. Linked list item base address is IDMABA + IDMALA. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C64 C   FIELD 29w01 ABR (rw): Acknowledge linked list buffer ready This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0). This bit is not taken into account when starting the first linked list buffer from the software programmed register information. ABR is only taken into account on subsequent loaded linked list items.
0x46008C64 C   FIELD 30w01 ULS (rw): Update SDMMC_IDMABSIZE from the next linked list when in linked list mode (SDMMC_IDMACTRLR.IDMABMODE select linked list mode and ULA = 1) This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C64 C   FIELD 31w01 ULA (rw): Update SDMMC_IDMALAR from linked list when in linked list mode (SDMMC_IDMACTRLR.IDMABMODE select linked list mode) This bit can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
0x46008C68 B  REGISTER IDMABAR: SDMMC_IDMABAR
0x46008C68 C   FIELD 02w30 IDMABA (rw): Word aligned Linked list memory base address Linked list memory base pointer. These bits can only be written by firmware when DPSM is inactive (DPSMACT = 0).
