0x47000540 C   FIELD 10w02 SDCLK (rw): SDRAM clock configuration These bits define the SDRAM clock period for both SDRAM banks and allow disabling the clock before changing the frequency. In this case the SDRAM must be re-initialized. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are don't care.
0x47000540 C   FIELD 12w01 RBURST (rw): Burst read This bit enables Burst read mode. The SDRAM controller anticipates the next read commands during the CAS latency and stores data in the Read FIFO. Note: The corresponding bit in the FMC_SDCR2 register is don't care.
0x47000540 C   FIELD 13w02 RPIPE (rw): Read pipe These bits define the delay, in clock cycles, for reading data after CAS latency. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register is read only.
