0x50001000 A PERIPHERAL SEC_TIM6
0x50001000 B  REGISTER CR1: TIM6 control register 1
0x50001000 C   FIELD 00w01 CEN (rw): Counter enable CEN is cleared automatically in one-pulse mode, when an update event occurs.
0x50001000 C   FIELD 01w01 UDIS (rw): Update disable This bit is set and cleared by software to enable/disable UEV event generation. Counter overflow/underflow Setting the UG bit Update generation through the slave mode controller Buffered registers are then loaded with their preload values.
0x50001000 C   FIELD 02w01 URS (rw): Update request source This bit is set and cleared by software to select the UEV event sources. Counter overflow/underflow Setting the UG bit Update generation through the slave mode controller
0x50001000 C   FIELD 03w01 OPM (rw): One-pulse mode
0x50001000 C   FIELD 07w01 ARPE (rw): Auto-reload preload enable
0x50001000 C   FIELD 11w01 UIFREMAP (rw): UIF status bit remapping
0x50001000 C   FIELD 12w01 DITHEN (rw): Dithering enable Note: The DITHEN bit can only be modified when CEN bit is reset.
0x50001004 B  REGISTER CR2: TIM6 control register 2
0x50001004 C   FIELD 04w03 MMS (rw): Master mode selection These bits are used to select the information to be sent in master mode to slave timers for synchronization (TRGO). The combination is as follows: Note: The clock of the slave timer or he peripheral receiving the tim_trgo must be enabled prior to receive events from the master timer, and must not be changed on-the-fly while triggers are received from the master timer.
0x5000100C B  REGISTER DIER: TIM6 DMA/Interrupt enable register
0x5000100C C   FIELD 00w01 UIE (rw): Update interrupt enable
0x5000100C C   FIELD 08w01 UDE (rw): Update DMA request enable
0x50001010 B  REGISTER SR: TIM6 status register
0x50001010 C   FIELD 00w01 UIF (rw): Update interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware on an update event. It is cleared by software. On counter overflow if UDIS = 0 in the TIMx_CR1 register. When CNT is reinitialized by software using the UG bit in the TIMx_EGR register, if URS = 0 and UDIS = 0 in the TIMx_CR1 register.
0x50001014 B  REGISTER EGR: TIM6 event generation register
0x50001014 C   FIELD 00w01 UG (wo): Update generation This bit can be set by software, it is automatically cleared by hardware.
0x50001024 B  REGISTER CNT: TIM6 counter
0x50001024 C   FIELD 00w16 CNT (rw): Counter value Non-dithering mode (DITHEN = 0) The register holds the counter value. Dithering mode (DITHEN = 1) The register only holds the non-dithered part in CNT[15:0]. The fractional part is not available.
0x50001024 C   FIELD 31w01 UIFCPY (ro): UIF copy This bit is a read-only copy of the UIF bit of the TIMx_ISR register. If the UIFREMAP bit in TIMx_CR1 is reset, bit 31 is reserved and read as 0.
0x50001028 B  REGISTER PSC: TIM6 prescaler
0x50001028 C   FIELD 00w16 PSC (rw): Prescaler value The counter clock frequency ftim_cnt_ck is equal to ftim_psc_ck / (PSC[15:0] + 1). PSC contains the value to be loaded into the active prescaler register at each update event. (including when the counter is cleared through UG bit of TIMx_EGR register.
0x5000102C B  REGISTER ARR: TIM6 auto-reload register
0x5000102C C   FIELD 00w20 ARR (rw): Auto-reload value ARR is the value to be loaded into the actual auto-reload register. Refer to for more details about ARR update and behavior. The counter is blocked while the auto-reload value is null. Non-dithering mode (DITHEN = 0) The register holds the auto-reload value in ARR[15:0]. The ARR[19:16] bits are reserved. Dithering mode (DITHEN = 1) The register holds the integer part in ARR[19:4]. The ARR[3:0] bitfield contains the dithered part.
0x50001400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_TIM7
0x50001400 B  REGISTER CR1: TIM6 control register 1
0x50001400 C   FIELD 00w01 CEN (rw): Counter enable CEN is cleared automatically in one-pulse mode, when an update event occurs.
0x50001400 C   FIELD 01w01 UDIS (rw): Update disable This bit is set and cleared by software to enable/disable UEV event generation. Counter overflow/underflow Setting the UG bit Update generation through the slave mode controller Buffered registers are then loaded with their preload values.
0x50001400 C   FIELD 02w01 URS (rw): Update request source This bit is set and cleared by software to select the UEV event sources. Counter overflow/underflow Setting the UG bit Update generation through the slave mode controller
