0x50005C90 B  REGISTER MAXRLR: I3C maximum read length register
0x50005C90 C   FIELD 00w16 MRL (rw): maximum data read length (when I3C is acting as target) This field is initially written by software when I3C_CFGR.EN=0 and updated by hardware on the reception of SETMRL command (with potentially also updated IBIP[2:0]). Software is notified of a MRL update by the I3C_EVR.MRLUPF and the corresponding interrupt if enabled. This field is used by hardware to return the value on the I3C bus when the target receives a GETMRL CCC.
0x50005C90 C   FIELD 16w03 IBIP (rw): IBI payload data size, in bytes (when I3C is acting as target) This field is initially written by software when I3C_CFGR.EN=0 to set the number of data bytes to be sent to the controller after an IBI request has been acknowledged.This field may be updated by hardware on the reception of SETMRL command (which potentially also updated IBIP[2:0]). Software is notified of a MRL update by the I3C_EVR.MRLUPF and the corresponding interrupt if enabled. others: same as 100
0x50005C94 B  REGISTER MAXWLR: I3C maximum write length register
0x50005C94 C   FIELD 00w16 MWL (rw): maximum data write length (when I3C is acting as target) This field is initially written by software when I3C_CFGR.EN=0 and updated by hardware on the reception of SETMWL command. Software is notified of a MWL update by the I3C_EVR.MWLUPF and the corresponding interrupt if enabled. This field is used by hardware to return the value on the I3C bus when the target receives a GETMWL CCC.
0x50005CA0 B  REGISTER TIMINGR0: I3C timing register 0
0x50005CA0 C   FIELD 00w08 SCLL_PP (rw): SCL low duration in I3C push-pull phases, in number of kernel clocks cycles: tSCLL_PP = (SCLL_PP + 1) x tI3CCLK SCLL_PP is used to generate tLOW (I3C) timing.
0x50005CA0 C   FIELD 08w08 SCLH_I3C (rw): SCL high duration, used for I3C messages (both in push-pull and open-drain phases), in number of kernel clocks cycles: tSCLH_I3C = (SCLH_I3C + 1) x tI3CCLK SCLH_I3C is used to generate both tHIGH (I3C) and tHIGH_MIXED timings.
0x50005CA0 C   FIELD 16w08 SCLL_OD (rw): SCL low duration in open-drain phases, used for legacy I2C commands and for I3C open-drain phases (address header phase following a START, not a Repeated START), in number of kernel clocks cycles: tSCLL_OD = (SCLL_OD + 1) x tI3CCLK SCLL_OD is used to generate both tLOW (I2C) and tLOW_OD timings (max. of the two).
0x50005CA0 C   FIELD 24w08 SCLH_I2C (rw): SCL high duration, used for legacy I2C commands, in number of kernel clocks cycles: tSCLH_I2C = (SCLH_I2C + 1) x tI3CCLK SCLH_I2C is used to generate tHIGH (I2C) timing.
0x50005CA4 B  REGISTER TIMINGR1: I3C timing register 1
0x50005CA4 C   FIELD 00w08 AVAL (rw): number of kernel clock cycles, that is used whatever I3C is acting as controller or target, to set the following MIPI I3C timings, like bus available condition time: When the I3C is acting as target: for bus available condition time: it must wait for (bus available condition) time to be elapsed after a stop and before issuing a start request for an IBI or a controller-role request (i.e. bus free condition is sustained for at least tAVAL). refer to MIPI timing tAVAL = 1 s. This timing is defined by: tAVAL = (AVAL[7:0] + 2) x tI3CCLK for bus idle condition time: it must wait for (bus idle condition) time to be elapsed after that both SDA and SCL are continuously high and stable before issuing a hot-join event. Refer to MIPI v1.1 timing tIDLE = 200 s . This timing is defined by: tIDLE = (AVAL[7:0] + 2) x 200 x tI3CCLK When the I3C is acting as controller, it can not stall the clock beyond a maximum stall time (i.e. stall the SCL clock low), as follows: on first bit of assigned address during dynamic address assignment: it can not stall the clock beyond the MIPI timing tSTALLDAA = 15 ms. This timing is defined by: tSTALLDAA = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x 15000 x tI3CCLK on ACK/NACK phase of I3C/I2C transfer, on parity bit of write data transfer, on transition bit of I3C read transfer: it can not stall the clock beyond the MIPI timing tSTALL = 100 s. This timing is defined by: tSTALL = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x 100 x tI3CCLK Whatever the I3C is acting as controller or as (controller-capable) target, during a controller-role hand-off procedure: The new controller must wait for a time (refer to MIPI timing tNEWCRLock) before pulling SDA low (i.e. issuing a start). And the active controller must wait for the same time while monitoring new controller and before testing the new controller by pulling SDA low. This time to wait is dependent on the defined I3C_TIMINGR1.ANSCR[1:0], as follows: If ASNCR[1:0]=00: tNEWCRLock = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x tI3CCLK If ASNCR[1:0]=01: tNEWCRLock = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x 100 x tI3CCLK If ASNCR[1:0]=10: tNEWCRLock = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x 2000 x tI3CCLK If ASNCR[1:0]=11: tNEWCRLock = (AVAL[7:0] + 1) x 50000 x tI3CCLK
0x50005CA4 C   FIELD 08w02 ASNCR (rw): activity state of the new controller (when I3C is acting asactive- controller) This field indicates the time to wait before being accessed as new target, refer to the other field AVAL[7:0]. This field can be modified only when the I3C is acting as controller.
0x50005CA4 C   FIELD 16w07 FREE (rw): number of kernel clocks cycles that is used to set some MIPI timings like bus free condition time (when the I3C is acting as controller) When the I3C is acting as controller: for I3C start timing: it must wait for (bus free condition) time to be elapsed after a stop and before a start, refer to MIPI timings (I3C) tCAS and (I2C) tBUF. These timings are defined by: tBUF= tCAS = [ (FREE[6:0] + 1) x 2(0,5 + SDA_HD)] x tI3CCLK Note: for pure I3C bus: tCASmin= 38,4 ns. Note: for pure I3C bus: tCASmax=1s, 100s, 2ms, 50ms for respectively ENTAS0,1,2, and 3. Note: for mixed bus with I2C fm+ device: tBUFmin = 0,5 s. Note: for mixed bus with I2C fm device: tBUFmin = 1,3 s. for I3C repeated start timing: it must wait for time to be elapsed after a repeated start (i.e. SDA is de-asserted) and before driving SCL low, refer to. MIPI timing tCASr. This timing is defined by: tCASr = [ (FREE[6:0] + 1) x 2(0,5 + SDA_HD)] x tI3CCLK for I3C stop timing: it must wait for time to be elapsed after that the SCL clock is driven high and before the stop condition (i.e. SDA is asserted). This timing is defined by: tCBP = (FREE[6:0] + 1) x tI3CCLK for I3C repeated start timing (T-bit when controller ends read with repeated start followed by stop): it must wait for time to be elapsed after that the SCL clock is driven high and before the repeated start condition (i.e. SDA is de-asserted). This timing is defined by: tCBSr = (FREE[6:0] + 1) x tI3CCLK
0x50005CA4 C   FIELD 28w01 SDA_HD (rw): SDA hold time (when the I3C is acting as controller), in number of kernel clocks cycles (refer to MIPI timing SDA hold time in push-pull tHD_PP):
0x50005CA8 B  REGISTER TIMINGR2: I3C timing register 2
0x50005CA8 C   FIELD 00w01 STALLT (rw): Controller clock stall on T-bit phase of Data enable The SCL is stalled during STALL x tSCLL_PP in the T-bit phase (before 9th bit). This allows the target to prepare data to be sent.
0x50005CA8 C   FIELD 01w01 STALLD (rw): controller clock stall on PAR phase of Data enable The SCL is stalled during STALL x tSCLL_PP in the T-bit phase (before 9th bit). This allows the target to read received data.
0x50005CA8 C   FIELD 02w01 STALLC (rw): controller clock stall on PAR phase of CCC enable The SCL is stalled during STALL x tSCLL_PP in the T-bit phase of common command code (before 9th bit). This allows the target to decode the command.
0x50005CA8 C   FIELD 03w01 STALLA (rw): controller clock stall enable on ACK phase The SCL is stalled (during tSCLL_STALLas defined by STALL) in the address ACK/NACK phase (before 9th bit). This allows the target to prepare data or the controller to respond to target interrupt.
0x50005CA8 C   FIELD 08w08 STALL (rw): controller clock stall time, in number of kernel clock cycles tSCLL_STALL = STALL x tI3CCLK
0x50005CC0 B  REGISTER BCR: I3C bus characteristics register
0x50005CC0 C   FIELD 00w01 BCR0 (rw): max data speed limitation
0x50005CC0 C   FIELD 02w01 BCR2 (rw): in-band interrupt (IBI) payload
0x50005CC0 C   FIELD 06w01 BCR6 (rw): controller capable
0x50005CC4 B  REGISTER DCR: I3C device characteristics register
0x50005CC4 C   FIELD 00w08 DCR (rw): device characteristics ID others: ID to describe the type of the I3C sensor/device Note: The latest MIPI DCR ID assignments are available at: https://www.mipi.org/MIPI_I3C_device_characteristics_register
0x50005CC8 B  REGISTER GETCAPR: I3C get capability register
0x50005CC8 C   FIELD 14w01 CAPPEND (rw): IBI MDB support for pending read notification This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and indicates the support (or not) of the pending read notification via the IBI MDB[7:0] value. This bit is used to return the GETCAP3 byte in response to the GETCAPS CCC format 1.
0x50005CCC B  REGISTER CRCAPR: I3C controller-role capability register
0x50005CCC C   FIELD 03w01 CAPDHOFF (rw): delayed controller-role hand-off This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and indicates if this target I3C may need additional time to process a controller-role hand-off requested by the current controller. This bit is used to return the CRCAP2 byte in response to the GETCAPS CCC format 2.
0x50005CCC C   FIELD 09w01 CAPGRP (rw): group management support (when acting as controller) This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and indicates if the I3C is able to support group management when it acts as a controller (after controller-role hand-off) via emitted DEFGRPA, RSTGRPA, and SETGRPA CCC. This bit is used to return the CRCAP1 byte in response to the GETCAPS CCC format 2.
0x50005CD0 B  REGISTER GETMXDSR: I3C get capability register
0x50005CD0 C   FIELD 00w02 HOFFAS (rw): controller hand-off activity state This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and indicates in which initial activity state the (other) current controller should expect the I3C bus after a controller-role hand-off to this controller-capable I3C, when returning the defining byte CRHDLY (0x91) to a GETMXDS CCC. This 2-bit field is used to return the CRHDLY1 byte in response to the GETCAPS CCC format 3, in order to state which is the activity state of this I3C when becoming controller after a controller-role hand-off, and consequently the time the former controller should wait before testing this I3C to be confirmed its ownership.
0x50005CD0 C   FIELD 08w02 FMT (rw): GETMXDS CCC format
0x50005CD0 C   FIELD 16w08 RDTURN (rw): programmed byte of the 3-byte MaxRdTurn (maximum read turnaround byte) This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and writes the value of the selected byte (via the FMT[1:0] field) of the 3-byte MaxRdTurn which is returned in response to the GETMXDS CCC format 2 to encode the maximum read turnaround time.
0x50005CD0 C   FIELD 24w01 TSCO (rw): clock-to-data turnaround time (tSCO) This bit is written by software during bus initialization (i.e. I3C_CFGR.EN=0) and is used to specify the clock-to-data turnaround time tSCO (vs the value of 12 ns). This bit is used by the hardware in response to the GETMXDS CCC to return the encoded clock-to-data turnaround time via the returned MaxRd[5:3] bits.
0x50005CD4 B  REGISTER EPIDR: I3C extended provisioned ID register
0x50005CD4 C   FIELD 12w04 MIPIID (rw): 4-bit MIPI Instance ID This field is written by software to set and identify individually each instance of this I3C IP with a specific number on a single I3C bus. This field represents the bits[15:12] of the 48-bit provisioned ID. Note: The bits[11:0] of the provisioned ID may be 0.
0x50005CD4 C   FIELD 16w01 IDTSEL (ro): provisioned ID type selector This field is set as 0 i.e. vendor fixed value. This field represents the bit[32] of the 48-bit provisioned ID. Note: The bits[31:16] of the provisioned ID may be 0.
0x50005CD4 C   FIELD 17w15 MIPIMID (ro): 15-bit MIPI manufacturer ID This read field is the 15-bit STMicroelectronics MIPI ID i.e. 0x0104. This field represents the bits[47:33] of the 48-bit provisioned ID.
0x50006000 A PERIPHERAL SEC_CRS
0x50006000 B  REGISTER CR: CRS control register
0x50006000 C   FIELD 00w01 SYNCOKIE (rw): SYNC event OK interrupt enable
0x50006000 C   FIELD 01w01 SYNCWARNIE (rw): SYNC warning interrupt enable
0x50006000 C   FIELD 02w01 ERRIE (rw): Synchronization or trimming error interrupt enable
0x50006000 C   FIELD 03w01 ESYNCIE (rw): Expected SYNC interrupt enable
0x50006000 C   FIELD 05w01 CEN (rw): Frequency error counter enable This bit enables the oscillator clock for the frequency error counter. When this bit is set, the CRS_CFGR register is write-protected and cannot be modified.
0x50006000 C   FIELD 06w01 AUTOTRIMEN (rw): Automatic trimming enable This bit enables the automatic hardware adjustment of TRIM bits according to the measured frequency error between two SYNC events. If this bit is set, the TRIM bits are read-only. The TRIM value can be adjusted by hardware by one or two steps at a time, depending on the measured frequency error value. Refer to for more details.
0x50006000 C   FIELD 07w01 SWSYNC (rw): Generate software SYNC event This bit is set by software in order to generate a software SYNC event. It is automatically cleared by hardware.
0x50006000 C   FIELD 08w06 TRIM (rw): HSI48 oscillator smooth trimming These bits provide a user-programmable trimming value to the HSI48 oscillator. They can be programmed to adjust to variations in voltage and temperature that influence the frequency of the HSI48 oscillator. The default value is 32, which corresponds to the middle of the trimming interval. The trimming step is specified in the product datasheet. A higher TRIM value corresponds to a higher output frequency. When the AUTOTRIMEN bit is set, this field is controlled by hardware and is read-only.
0x50006004 B  REGISTER CFGR: CRS configuration register
0x50006004 C   FIELD 00w16 RELOAD (rw): Counter reload value RELOAD is the value to be loaded in the frequency error counter with each SYNC event. Refer to for more details about counter behavior.
0x50006004 C   FIELD 16w08 FELIM (rw): Frequency error limit FELIM contains the value to be used to evaluate the captured frequency error value latched in the FECAP[15:0] bits of the CRS_ISR register. Refer to for more details about FECAP evaluation.
0x50006004 C   FIELD 24w03 SYNCDIV (rw): SYNC divider These bits are set and cleared by software to control the division factor of the SYNC signal.
0x50006004 C   FIELD 28w02 SYNCSRC (rw): SYNC signal source selection These bits are set and cleared by software to select the SYNC signal source (see CRS internal input/output signals for STM32U575/585): Note: When using USB LPM (Link Power Management) and the device is in Sleep mode, the periodic USB SOF is not generated by the host. No SYNC signal is therefore provided to the CRS to calibrate the HSI48 oscillator on the run. To guarantee the required clock precision after waking up from Sleep mode, the LSE or reference clock on the GPIOs must be used as SYNC signal.
0x50006004 C   FIELD 31w01 SYNCPOL (rw): SYNC polarity selection This bit is set and cleared by software to select the input polarity for the SYNC signal source.
0x50006008 B  REGISTER ISR: CRS interrupt and status register
0x50006008 C   FIELD 00w01 SYNCOKF (ro): SYNC event OK flag This flag is set by hardware when the measured frequency error is smaller than FELIM * 3. This means that either no adjustment of the TRIM value is needed or that an adjustment by one trimming step is enough to compensate the frequency error. An interrupt is generated if the SYNCOKIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the SYNCOKC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 01w01 SYNCWARNF (ro): SYNC warning flag This flag is set by hardware when the measured frequency error is greater than or equal to FELIM * 3, but smaller than FELIM * 128. This means that to compensate the frequency error, the TRIM value must be adjusted by two steps or more. An interrupt is generated if the SYNCWARNIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the SYNCWARNC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 02w01 ERRF (ro): Error flag This flag is set by hardware in case of any synchronization or trimming error. It is the logical OR of the TRIMOVF, SYNCMISS and SYNCERR bits. An interrupt is generated if the ERRIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software in reaction to setting the ERRC bit in the CRS_ICR register, which clears the TRIMOVF, SYNCMISS and SYNCERR bits.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 03w01 ESYNCF (ro): Expected SYNC flag This flag is set by hardware when the frequency error counter reached a zero value. An interrupt is generated if the ESYNCIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the ESYNCC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 08w01 SYNCERR (ro): SYNC error This flag is set by hardware when the SYNC pulse arrives before the ESYNC event and the measured frequency error is greater than or equal to FELIM * 128. This means that the frequency error is too big (internal frequency too low) to be compensated by adjusting the TRIM value, and that some other action has to be taken. An interrupt is generated if the ERRIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the ERRC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 09w01 SYNCMISS (ro): SYNC missed This flag is set by hardware when the frequency error counter reached value FELIM * 128 and no SYNC was detected, meaning either that a SYNC pulse was missed or that the frequency error is too big (internal frequency too high) to be compensated by adjusting the TRIM value, and that some other action has to be taken. At this point, the frequency error counter is stopped (waiting for a next SYNC) and an interrupt is generated if the ERRIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the ERRC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 10w01 TRIMOVF (ro): Trimming overflow or underflow This flag is set by hardware when the automatic trimming tries to over- or under-flow the TRIM value. An interrupt is generated if the ERRIE bit is set in the CRS_CR register. It is cleared by software by setting the ERRC bit in the CRS_ICR register.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 15w01 FEDIR (ro): Frequency error direction FEDIR is the counting direction of the frequency error counter latched in the time of the last SYNC event. It shows whether the actual frequency is below or above the target.
0x50006008 C   FIELD 16w16 FECAP (ro): Frequency error capture FECAP is the frequency error counter value latched in the time of the last SYNC event. Refer to for more details about FECAP usage.
0x5000600C B  REGISTER ICR: CRS interrupt flag clear register
0x5000600C C   FIELD 00w01 SYNCOKC (rw): SYNC event OK clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the SYNCOKF flag in the CRS_ISR register.
0x5000600C C   FIELD 01w01 SYNCWARNC (rw): SYNC warning clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the SYNCWARNF flag in the CRS_ISR register.
0x5000600C C   FIELD 02w01 ERRC (rw): Error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears TRIMOVF, SYNCMISS and SYNCERR bits and consequently also the ERRF flag in the CRS_ISR register.
0x5000600C C   FIELD 03w01 ESYNCC (rw): Expected SYNC clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ESYNCF flag in the CRS_ISR register.
0x50006400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_USART6
0x50006400 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50006400 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006400 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006400 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006400 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006400 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006400 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006400 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006400 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006400 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006400 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006404 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50006404 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50006404 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50006404 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006404 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006404 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50006408 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50006408 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50006408 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006408 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006408 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006408 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006408 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50006408 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50006408 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006408 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006408 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006408 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006408 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50006408 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006408 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x5000640C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x5000640C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50006410 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50006410 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50006410 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006414 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50006414 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50006414 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50006418 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50006418 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006418 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50006418 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50006418 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50006418 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x5000641C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x5000641C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x5000641C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000641C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x5000641C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50006420 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50006420 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006420 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006420 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006420 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50006420 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006420 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006424 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50006424 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50006428 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50006428 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x5000642C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x5000642C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50006800 A PERIPHERAL SEC_USART10
0x50006800 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50006800 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006800 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006800 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006800 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006800 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006800 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006800 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006800 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006800 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006800 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006804 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50006804 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50006804 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50006804 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006804 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006804 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50006808 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50006808 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50006808 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006808 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006808 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006808 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006808 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50006808 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50006808 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006808 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006808 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006808 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006808 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50006808 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006808 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x5000680C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x5000680C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50006810 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50006810 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50006810 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006814 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50006814 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50006814 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50006818 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50006818 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006818 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50006818 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50006818 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50006818 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x5000681C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x5000681C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x5000681C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000681C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x5000681C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50006820 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50006820 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006820 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006820 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006820 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50006820 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006820 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006824 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50006824 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50006828 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50006828 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x5000682C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x5000682C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50006C00 A PERIPHERAL SEC_USART11
0x50006C00 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C00 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C04 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C04 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50006C08 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50006C08 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50006C0C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x50006C0C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50006C10 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50006C10 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50006C10 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C14 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50006C14 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50006C14 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50006C18 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50006C18 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C18 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50006C18 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50006C18 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50006C18 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x50006C1C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x50006C1C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50006C20 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50006C20 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50006C24 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50006C24 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50006C28 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50006C28 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x50006C2C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x50006C2C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50007800 A PERIPHERAL SEC_UART7
0x50007800 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50007800 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007800 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007800 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007800 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007800 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007800 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007800 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50007800 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007800 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007800 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007804 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50007804 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50007804 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50007804 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007804 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007804 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50007808 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50007808 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50007808 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007808 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50007808 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50007808 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007808 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50007808 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50007808 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007808 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007808 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007808 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007808 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50007808 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007808 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x5000780C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x5000780C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50007810 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50007810 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50007810 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007814 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50007814 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50007814 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50007818 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50007818 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007818 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50007818 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50007818 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50007818 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x5000781C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x5000781C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x5000781C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000781C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x5000781C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50007820 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50007820 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007820 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007820 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007820 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50007820 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007820 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007824 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50007824 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50007828 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50007828 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x5000782C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x5000782C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50007C00 A PERIPHERAL SEC_UART8
0x50007C00 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C00 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C04 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C04 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50007C08 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50007C08 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50007C0C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x50007C0C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50007C10 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50007C10 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50007C10 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C14 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50007C14 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50007C14 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50007C18 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50007C18 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C18 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50007C18 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50007C18 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50007C18 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x50007C1C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x50007C1C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50007C20 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50007C20 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50007C24 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50007C24 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50007C28 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50007C28 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x50007C2C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x50007C2C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50008000 A PERIPHERAL SEC_UART9
0x50008000 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50008000 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008000 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008000 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008000 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008000 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008000 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008000 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50008000 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008000 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008000 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008004 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50008004 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50008004 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50008004 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008004 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008004 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50008008 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50008008 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50008008 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008008 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50008008 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50008008 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008008 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50008008 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50008008 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008008 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008008 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008008 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008008 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50008008 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008008 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x5000800C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x5000800C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50008010 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50008010 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50008010 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008014 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50008014 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50008014 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50008018 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50008018 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008018 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50008018 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50008018 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50008018 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x5000801C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x5000801C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x5000801C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000801C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x5000801C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50008020 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50008020 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008020 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008020 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008020 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50008020 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008020 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008024 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50008024 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50008028 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50008028 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x5000802C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x5000802C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50008400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_UART12
0x50008400 B  REGISTER CR1: USART control register 1 [alternate]
0x50008400 C   FIELD 00w01 UE (rw): USART enable When this bit is cleared, the USART prescalers and outputs are stopped immediately, and all current operations are discarded. The USART configuration is kept, but all the USART_ISR status flags are reset. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: To enter low-power mode without generating errors on the line, the TE bit must be previously reset and the software must wait for the TC bit in the USART_ISR to be set before resetting the UE bit. The DMA requests are also reset when UE = 0 so the DMA channel must be disabled before resetting the UE bit. In Smartcard mode, (SCEN = 1), the SCLK is always available when CLKEN = 1, regardless of the UE bit value.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 01w01 UESM (rw): USART enable in low-power mode When this bit is cleared, the USART cannot wake up the MCU from low-power mode. When this bit is set, the USART can wake up the MCU from low-power mode. This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: It is recommended to set the UESM bit just before entering low-power mode, and clear it when exiting low-power mode.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 02w01 RE (rw): Receiver enable This bit enables the receiver. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 03w01 TE (rw): Transmitter enable This bit enables the transmitter. It is set and cleared by software. Note: During transmission, a low pulse on the TE bit ('0' followed by '1') sends a preamble (idle line) after the current word, except in Smartcard mode. In order to generate an idle character, the TE must not be immediately written to '1'. To ensure the required duration, the software can poll the TEACK bit in the USART_ISR register. In Smartcard mode, when TE is set, there is a 1 bit-time delay before the transmission starts.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLEIE (rw): IDLE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 05w01 RXNEIE (rw): RXFIFO not empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 06w01 TCIE (rw): Transmission complete interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 07w01 TXEIE (rw): TXFIFO not full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 08w01 PEIE (rw): PE interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 09w01 PS (rw): Parity selection This bit selects the odd or even parity when the parity generation/detection is enabled (PCE bit set). It is set and cleared by software. The parity is selected after the current byte. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008400 C   FIELD 10w01 PCE (rw): Parity control enable This bit selects the hardware parity control (generation and detection). When the parity control is enabled, the computed parity is inserted at the MSB position (9th bit if M=1; 8th bit if M=0) and the parity is checked on the received data. This bit is set and cleared by software. Once it is set, PCE is active after the current byte (in reception and in transmission). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008400 C   FIELD 11w01 WAKE (rw): Receiver wakeup method This bit determines the USART wakeup method from Mute mode. It is set or cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008400 C   FIELD 12w01 M0 (rw): Word length This bit is used in conjunction with bit 28 (M1) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software (refer to bit 28 (M1)description). This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008400 C   FIELD 13w01 MME (rw): Mute mode enable This bit enables the USART Mute mode function. When set, the USART can switch between active and Mute mode, as defined by the WAKE bit. It is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 14w01 CMIE (rw): Character match interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 15w01 OVER8 (rw): Oversampling mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In LIN, IrDA and Smartcard modes, this bit must be kept cleared.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 16w05 DEDT (rw): Driver Enable deassertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the end of the last stop bit, in a transmitted message, and the de-activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). If the USART_TDR register is written during the DEDT time, the new data is transmitted only when the DEDT and DEAT times have both elapsed. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008400 C   FIELD 21w05 DEAT (rw): Driver Enable assertion time This 5-bit value defines the time between the activation of the DE (Driver Enable) signal and the beginning of the start bit. It is expressed in sample time units (1/8 or 1/16 bit time, depending on the oversampling rate). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008400 C   FIELD 26w01 RTOIE (rw): Receiver timeout interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50008400 C   FIELD 27w01 EOBIE (rw): End of Block interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008400 C   FIELD 28w01 M1 (rw): Word length This bit must be used in conjunction with bit 12 (M0) to determine the word length. It is set or cleared by software. M[1:0] = '00': 1 start bit, 8 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '01': 1 start bit, 9 Data bits, n Stop bit M[1:0] = '10': 1 start bit, 7 Data bits, n Stop bit This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: In 7-bits data length mode, the Smartcard mode, LIN master mode and auto baud rate (0x7F and 0x55 frames detection) are not supported.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 29w01 FIFOEN (rw): FIFO mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: FIFO mode can be used on standard UART communication, in SPI Master/Slave mode and in Smartcard modes only. It must not be enabled in IrDA and LIN modes.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 30w01 TXFEIE (rw): TXFIFO empty interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008400 C   FIELD 31w01 RXFFIE (rw): RXFIFO Full interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008404 B  REGISTER CR2: USART control register 2
0x50008404 C   FIELD 00w01 SLVEN (rw): Synchronous Slave mode enable When the SLVEN bit is set, the Synchronous slave mode is enabled. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 03w01 DIS_NSS (rw): When the DIS_NSS bit is set, the NSS pin input is ignored. Note: When SPI slave mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 04w01 ADDM7 (rw): 7-bit Address Detection/4-bit Address Detection This bit is for selection between 4-bit address detection or 7-bit address detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: In 7-bit and 9-bit data modes, the address detection is done on 6-bit and 8-bit address (ADD[5:0] and ADD[7:0]) respectively.
0x50008404 C   FIELD 05w01 LBDL (rw): LIN break detection length This bit is for selection between 11 bit or 10 bit break detection. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 06w01 LBDIE (rw): LIN break detection interrupt enable Break interrupt mask (break detection using break delimiter). Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 08w01 LBCL (rw): Last bit clock pulse This bit is used to select whether the clock pulse associated with the last data bit transmitted (MSB) has to be output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. The last bit is the 7th or 8th or 9th data bit transmitted depending on the 7 or 8 or 9 bit format selected by the M bit in the USART_CR1 register. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 09w01 CPHA (rw): Clock phase This bit is used to select the phase of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPOL bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship (see and ) This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 10w01 CPOL (rw): Clock polarity This bit enables the user to select the polarity of the clock output on the SCLK pin in Synchronous mode. It works in conjunction with the CPHA bit to produce the desired clock/data relationship This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Synchronous mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 11w01 CLKEN (rw): Clock enable This bit enables the user to enable the SCLK pin. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If neither Synchronous mode nor Smartcard mode is supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to . In Smartcard mode, in order to provide correctly the SCLK clock to the smartcard, the steps below must be respected: UE = 0 SCEN = 1 GTPR configuration CLKEN= 1 UE = 1
0x50008404 C   FIELD 12w02 STOP (rw): stop bits These bits are used for programming the stop bits. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 14w01 LINEN (rw): LIN mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. The LIN mode enables the capability to send LIN synchronous breaks (13 low bits) using the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR1 register, and to detect LIN Sync breaks. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 15w01 SWAP (rw): Swap TX/RX pins This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 16w01 RXINV (rw): RX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the RX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 17w01 TXINV (rw): TX pin active level inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This enables the use of an external inverter on the TX line. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 18w01 DATAINV (rw): Binary data inversion This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 19w01 MSBFIRST (rw): Most significant bit first This bit is set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008404 C   FIELD 20w01 ABREN (rw): Auto baud rate enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 21w02 ABRMOD (rw): Auto baud rate mode These bits are set and cleared by software. This bitfield can only be written when ABREN = 0 or the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If DATAINV=1 and/or MSBFIRST=1 the patterns must be the same on the line, for example 0xAA for MSBFIRST) If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 23w01 RTOEN (rw): Receiver timeout enable This bit is set and cleared by software. When this feature is enabled, the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register is set if the RX line is idle (no reception) for the duration programmed in the RTOR (receiver timeout register). Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008404 C   FIELD 24w08 ADD (rw): Address of the USART node These bits give the address of the USART node in Mute mode or a character code to be recognized in low-power or Run mode: In Mute mode: they are used in multiprocessor communication to wakeup from Mute mode with 4-bit/7-bit address mark detection. The MSB of the character sent by the transmitter should be equal to 1. In 4-bit address mark detection, only ADD[3:0] bits are used. In low-power mode: they are used for wake up from low-power mode on character match. When WUS[1:0] is programmed to 0b00 (WUF active on address match), the wakeup from low-power mode is performed when the received character corresponds to the character programmed through ADD[6:0] or ADD[3:0] bitfield (depending on ADDM7 bit), and WUF interrupt is enabled by setting WUFIE bit. The MSB of the character sent by transmitter should be equal to 1. In Run mode with Mute mode inactive (for example, end-of-block detection in ModBus protocol): the whole received character (8 bits) is compared to ADD[7:0] value and CMF flag is set on match. An interrupt is generated if the CMIE bit is set. These bits can only be written when the reception is disabled (RE = 0) or when the USART is disabled (UE = 0).
0x50008408 B  REGISTER CR3: USART control register 3
0x50008408 C   FIELD 00w01 EIE (rw): Error interrupt enable Error Interrupt Enable Bit is required to enable interrupt generation in case of a framing error, overrun error noise flag or SPI slave underrun error (FE=1 or ORE=1 or NE=1or UDR = 1 in the USART_ISR register).
0x50008408 C   FIELD 01w01 IREN (rw): IrDA mode enable This bit is set and cleared by software. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 02w01 IRLP (rw): IrDA low-power This bit is used for selecting between normal and low-power IrDA modes This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If IrDA mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 03w01 HDSEL (rw): Half-duplex selection Selection of Single-wire Half-duplex mode This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008408 C   FIELD 04w01 NACK (rw): Smartcard NACK enable This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 05w01 SCEN (rw): Smartcard mode enable This bit is used for enabling Smartcard mode. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 06w01 DMAR (rw): DMA enable receiver This bit is set/reset by software
0x50008408 C   FIELD 07w01 DMAT (rw): DMA enable transmitter This bit is set/reset by software
0x50008408 C   FIELD 08w01 RTSE (rw): RTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSE (rw): CTS enable This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0) Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 10w01 CTSIE (rw): CTS interrupt enable Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 11w01 ONEBIT (rw): One sample bit method enable This bit enables the user to select the sample method. When the one sample bit method is selected the noise detection flag (NE) is disabled. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0).
0x50008408 C   FIELD 12w01 OVRDIS (rw): Overrun Disable This bit is used to disable the receive overrun detection. the ORE flag is not set and the new received data overwrites the previous content of the USART_RDR register. When FIFO mode is enabled, the RXFIFO is bypassed and data are written directly in USART_RDR register. Even when FIFO management is enabled, the RXNE flag is to be used. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: This control bit enables checking the communication flow w/o reading the data
0x50008408 C   FIELD 13w01 DDRE (rw): DMA Disable on Reception Error This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: The reception errors are: parity error, framing error or noise error.
0x50008408 C   FIELD 14w01 DEM (rw): Driver enable mode This bit enables the user to activate the external transceiver control, through the DE signal. This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 15w01 DEP (rw): Driver enable polarity selection This bit can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the Driver Enable feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 17w03 SCARCNT (rw): Smartcard auto-retry count This bitfield specifies the number of retries for transmission and reception in Smartcard mode. In Transmission mode, it specifies the number of automatic retransmission retries, before generating a transmission error (FE bit set). In Reception mode, it specifies the number or erroneous reception trials, before generating a reception error (RXNE/RXFNE and PE bits set). This bitfield must be programmed only when the USART is disabled (UE=0). When the USART is enabled (UE=1), this bitfield may only be written to 0x0, in order to stop retransmission. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 20w02 WUS: Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt flag selection This bitfield specifies the event which activates the WUF (Wakeup from low-power mode flag). This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008408 C   FIELD 22w01 WUFIE (rw): Wakeup from low-power mode interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: WUFIE must be set before entering in low-power mode. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008408 C   FIELD 23w01 TXFTIE (rw): TXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008408 C   FIELD 24w01 TCBGTIE (rw): Transmission Complete before guard time, interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008408 C   FIELD 25w03 RXFTCFG (rw): Receive FIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x50008408 C   FIELD 28w01 RXFTIE (rw): RXFIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008408 C   FIELD 29w03 TXFTCFG (rw): TXFIFO threshold configuration Remaining combinations: Reserved
0x5000840C B  REGISTER BRR: USART baud rate register
0x5000840C C   FIELD 00w16 BRR (rw): USART baud rate BRR[15:4] BRR[15:4] correspond to USARTDIV[15:4] BRR[3:0] When OVER8 = 0, BRR[3:0] = USARTDIV[3:0]. When OVER8 = 1: BRR[2:0] = USARTDIV[3:0] shifted 1 bit to the right. BRR[3] must be kept cleared.
0x50008410 B  REGISTER GTPR: USART guard time and prescaler register
0x50008410 C   FIELD 00w08 PSC (rw): Prescaler value PSC[7:0] = IrDA Normal and Low-power baud rate This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to achieve the low-power frequency: The source clock is divided by the value given in the register (8 significant bits): ... PSC[4:0]: Prescaler value This bitfield is used for programming the prescaler for dividing the USART source clock to provide the Smartcard clock. The value given in the register (5 significant bits) is multiplied by 2 to give the division factor of the source clock frequency: ... This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: Bits [7:5] must be kept cleared if Smartcard mode is used. This bitfield is reserved and forced by hardware to '0' when the Smartcard and IrDA modes are not supported. Refer to .
0x50008410 C   FIELD 08w08 GT (rw): Guard time value This bitfield is used to program the Guard time value in terms of number of baud clock periods. This is used in Smartcard mode. The Transmission Complete flag is set after this guard time value. This bitfield can only be written when the USART is disabled (UE=0). Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008414 B  REGISTER RTOR: USART receiver timeout register
0x50008414 C   FIELD 00w24 RTO (rw): Receiver timeout value This bitfield gives the Receiver timeout value in terms of number of bit duration. In Standard mode, the RTOF flag is set if, after the last received character, no new start bit is detected for more than the RTO value. In Smartcard mode, this value is used to implement the CWT and BWT. See Smartcard chapter for more details. In the standard, the CWT/BWT measurement is done starting from the start bit of the last received character. Note: This value must only be programmed once per received character.
0x50008414 C   FIELD 24w08 BLEN (rw): Block Length This bitfield gives the Block length in Smartcard T=1 Reception. Its value equals the number of information characters + the length of the Epilogue Field (1-LEC/2-CRC)1. Examples: BLEN = 0 0 information characters + LEC BLEN = 1 0 information characters + CRC BLEN = 255 254 information characters + CRC (total 256 characters)) In Smartcard mode, the Block length counter is reset when TXE=0 (TXFE = 0 in case FIFO mode is enabled). This bitfield can be used also in other modes. In this case, the Block length counter is reset when RE=0 (receiver disabled) and/or when the EOBCF bit is written to 1. Note: This value can be programmed after the start of the block reception (using the data from the LEN character in the Prologue Field). It must be programmed only once per received block.
0x50008418 B  REGISTER RQR: USART request register
0x50008418 C   FIELD 00w01 ABRRQ (wo): auto baud rate request Writing 1 to this bit resets the ABRF and ABRE flags in the USART_ISR and requests an automatic baud rate measurement on the next received data frame. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008418 C   FIELD 01w01 SBKRQ (wo): Send break request Writing 1 to this bit sets the SBKF flag and request to send a BREAK on the line, as soon as the transmit machine is available. Note: When the application needs to send the break character following all previously inserted data, including the ones not yet transmitted, the software should wait for the TXE flag assertion before setting the SBKRQ bit.
0x50008418 C   FIELD 02w01 MMRQ (wo): Mute mode request Writing 1 to this bit puts the USART in Mute mode and resets the RWU flag.
0x50008418 C   FIELD 03w01 RXFRQ (wo): Receive data flush request Writing 1 to this bit empties the entire receive FIFO i.e. clears the bit RXFNE. This enables to discard the received data without reading them, and avoid an overrun condition.
0x50008418 C   FIELD 04w01 TXFRQ (wo): Transmit data flush request When FIFO mode is disabled, writing '1' to this bit sets the TXE flag. This enables to discard the transmit data. This bit must be used only in Smartcard mode, when data have not been sent due to errors (NACK) and the FE flag is active in the USART_ISR register. If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. When FIFO is enabled, TXFRQ bit is set to flush the whole FIFO. This sets the TXFE flag (Transmit FIFO empty, bit 23 in the USART_ISR register). Flushing the Transmit FIFO is supported in both UART and Smartcard modes. Note: In FIFO mode, the TXFNF flag is reset during the flush request until TxFIFO is empty in order to ensure that no data are written in the data register.
0x5000841C B  REGISTER ISR: USART interrupt and status register
0x5000841C C   FIELD 00w01 PE (ro): Parity error This bit is set by hardware when a parity error occurs in Reception mode. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the PECF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if PEIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 01w01 FE (ro): Framing error This bit is set by hardware when a de-synchronization, excessive noise or a break character is detected. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the FECF bit in the USART_ICR register. When transmitting data in Smartcard mode, this bit is set when the maximum number of transmit attempts is reached without success (the card NACKs the data frame). An interrupt is generated if EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 02w01 NE (ro): Noise detection flag This bit is set by hardware when noise is detected on a received frame. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the NFCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: This bit does not generate an interrupt as it appears at the same time as the RXFNE bit which itself generates an interrupt. An interrupt is generated when the NE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. When the line is noise-free, the NE flag can be disabled by programming the ONEBIT bit to 1 to increase the USART tolerance to deviations (Refer to Tolerance of the USART receiver to clock deviation on page 2317). This error is associated with the character in the USART_RDR.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 03w01 ORE (ro): Overrun error This bit is set by hardware when the data currently being received in the shift register is ready to be transferred into the USART_RDR register while RXFF = 1. It is cleared by a software, writing 1 to the ORECF, in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 or EIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: When this bit is set, the USART_RDR register content is not lost but the shift register is overwritten. An interrupt is generated if the ORE flag is set during multi buffer communication if the EIE bit is set. This bit is permanently forced to 0 (no overrun detection) when the bit OVRDIS is set in the USART_CR3 register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 04w01 IDLE (ro): Idle line detected This bit is set by hardware when an Idle Line is detected. An interrupt is generated if IDLEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the IDLECF in the USART_ICR register. Note: The IDLE bit is not set again until the RXFNE bit has been set (i.e. a new idle line occurs). If Mute mode is enabled (MME=1), IDLE is set if the USART is not mute (RWU=0), whatever the Mute mode selected by the WAKE bit. If RWU=1, IDLE is not set.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 05w01 RXFNE (ro): RXFIFO not empty RXFNE bit is set by hardware when the RXFIFO is not empty, meaning that data can be read from the USART_RDR register. Every read operation from the USART_RDR frees a location in the RXFIFO. RXFNE is cleared when the RXFIFO is empty. The RXFNE flag can also be cleared by writing 1 to the RXFRQ in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if RXFNEIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 06w01 TC (ro): Transmission complete This bit indicates that the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted out of the shift register. The TC flag behaves as follows: When TDN = 0, the TC flag is set when the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and when TXE/TXFE is set. When TDN is equal to the number of data in the TXFIFO, the TC flag is set when TXFIFO is empty and TDN is reached. When TDN is greater than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC remains cleared until the TXFIFO is filled again to reach the programmed number of data to be transferred. When TDN is less than the number of data in the TXFIFO, TC is set when TDN is reached even if the TXFIFO is not empty. An interrupt is generated if TCIE=1 in the USART_CR1 register. TC bit is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TCCF in the USART_ICR register or by writing to the USART_TDR register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 07w01 TXFNF (ro): TXFIFO not full TXFNF is set by hardware when TXFIFO is not full meaning that data can be written in the USART_TDR. Every write operation to the USART_TDR places the data in the TXFIFO. This flag remains set until the TXFIFO is full. When the TXFIFO is full, this flag is cleared indicating that data can not be written into the USART_TDR. An interrupt is generated if the TXFNFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register. Note: The TXFNF is kept reset during the flush request until TXFIFO is empty. After sending the flush request (by setting TXFRQ bit), the flag TXFNF should be checked prior to writing in TXFIFO (TXFNF and TXFE is set at the same time). This bit is used during single buffer transmission.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 08w01 LBDF (ro): LIN break detection flag This bit is set by hardware when the LIN break is detected. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the LBDCF in the USART_ICR. An interrupt is generated if LBDIE = 1 in the USART_CR2 register. Note: If the USART does not support LIN mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 09w01 CTSIF (ro): CTS interrupt flag This bit is set by hardware when the nCTS input toggles, if the CTSE bit is set. It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the CTSCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CTSIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 10w01 CTS (ro): CTS flag This bit is set/reset by hardware. It is an inverted copy of the status of the nCTS input pin. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 11w01 RTOF (ro): Receiver timeout This bit is set by hardware when the timeout value, programmed in the RTOR register has lapsed, without any communication. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the RTOCF bit in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if RTOIE=1 in the USART_CR2 register. In Smartcard mode, the timeout corresponds to the CWT or BWT timings. Note: If a time equal to the value programmed in RTOR register separates 2 characters, RTOF is not set. If this time exceeds this value + 2 sample times (2/16 or 2/8, depending on the oversampling method), RTOF flag is set. The counter counts even if RE = 0 but RTOF is set only when RE = 1. If the timeout has already elapsed when RE is set, then RTOF is set. If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 12w01 EOBF (ro): End of block flag This bit is set by hardware when a complete block has been received (for example T=1 Smartcard mode). The detection is done when the number of received bytes (from the start of the block, including the prologue) is equal or greater than BLEN + 4. An interrupt is generated if EOBIE = 1 in the USART_CR1 register. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to EOBCF in the USART_ICR register. Note: If Smartcard mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 13w01 UDR (ro): SPI slave underrun error flag In Slave transmission mode, this flag is set when the first clock pulse for data transmission appears while the software has not yet loaded any value into USART_TDR. This flag is reset by setting UDRCF bit in the USART_ICR register. Note: If the USART does not support the SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 14w01 ABRE (ro): Auto baud rate error This bit is set by hardware if the baud rate measurement failed (baud rate out of range or character comparison failed) It is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 15w01 ABRF (ro): Auto baud rate flag This bit is set by hardware when the automatic baud rate has been set (RXFNE is also set, generating an interrupt if RXFNEIE = 1) or when the auto baud rate operation was completed without success (ABRE=1) (ABRE, RXFNE and FE are also set in this case) It is cleared by software, in order to request a new auto baud rate detection, by writing 1 to the ABRRQ in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the auto baud rate feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 16w01 BUSY (ro): Busy flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It is active when a communication is ongoing on the RX line (successful start bit detected). It is reset at the end of the reception (successful or not).
0x5000841C C   FIELD 17w01 CMF (ro): Character match flag This bit is set by hardware, when a the character defined by ADD[7:0] is received. It is cleared by software, writing 1 to the CMCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if CMIE=1in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 18w01 SBKF (ro): Send break flag This bit indicates that a send break character was requested. It is set by software, by writing 1 to the SBKRQ bit in the USART_CR3 register. It is automatically reset by hardware during the stop bit of break transmission.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 19w01 RWU (ro): Receiver wakeup from Mute mode This bit indicates if the USART is in Mute mode. It is cleared/set by hardware when a wakeup/mute sequence is recognized. The Mute mode control sequence (address or IDLE) is selected by the WAKE bit in the USART_CR1 register. When wakeup on IDLE mode is selected, this bit can only be set by software, writing 1 to the MMRQ bit in the USART_RQR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 20w01 WUF (ro): Wakeup from low-power mode flag This bit is set by hardware, when a wakeup event is detected. The event is defined by the WUS bitfield. It is cleared by software, writing a 1 to the WUCF in the USART_ICR register. An interrupt is generated if WUFIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When UESM is cleared, WUF flag is also cleared. If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 21w01 TEACK (ro): Transmit enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Transmit Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used when an idle frame request is generated by writing TE=0, followed by TE=1 in the USART_CR1 register, in order to respect the TE=0 minimum period.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 22w01 REACK (ro): Receive enable acknowledge flag This bit is set/reset by hardware, when the Receive Enable value is taken into account by the USART. It can be used to verify that the USART is ready for reception before entering low-power mode. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x5000841C C   FIELD 23w01 TXFE (ro): TXFIFO Empty This bit is set by hardware when TXFIFO is Empty. When the TXFIFO contains at least one data, this flag is cleared. The TXFE flag can also be set by writing 1 to the bit TXFRQ (bit 4) in the USART_RQR register. An interrupt is generated if the TXFEIE bit =1 (bit 30) in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 24w01 RXFF (ro): RXFIFO Full This bit is set by hardware when the number of received data corresponds to RXFIFO size + 1 (RXFIFO full + 1 data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFFIE bit =1 in the USART_CR1 register.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 25w01 TCBGT (ro): Transmission complete before guard time flag This bit is set when the last data written in the USART_TDR has been transmitted correctly out of the shift register. It is set by hardware in Smartcard mode, if the transmission of a frame containing data is complete and if the smartcard did not send back any NACK. An interrupt is generated if TCBGTIE=1 in the USART_CR3 register. This bit is cleared by software, by writing 1 to the TCBGTCF in the USART_ICR register or by a write to the USART_TDR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and kept at reset value. If the USART supports the Smartcard mode and the Smartcard mode is enabled, the TCBGT reset value is '1'. Refer to on page 2297.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 26w01 RXFT (ro): RXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the threshold programmed in RXFTCFG in USART_CR3 register is reached. This means that there are (RXFTCFG1) data in the Receive FIFO and one data in the USART_RDR register. An interrupt is generated if the RXFTIE bit =1 (bit 27) in the USART_CR3 register. Note: When the RXFTCFG threshold is configured to '101', RXFT flag is set if 16 data are available i.e. 15 data in the RXFIFO and 1 data in the USART_RDR. Consequently, the 17th received data does not cause an overrun error. The overrun error occurs after receiving the 18th data.
0x5000841C C   FIELD 27w01 TXFT (ro): TXFIFO threshold flag This bit is set by hardware when the TXFIFO reaches the threshold programmed in TXFTCFG of USART_CR3 register i.e. the TXFIFO contains TXFTCFG empty locations. An interrupt is generated if the TXFTIE bit =1 (bit 31) in the USART_CR3 register.
0x50008420 B  REGISTER ICR: USART interrupt flag clear register
0x50008420 C   FIELD 00w01 PECF (wo): Parity error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the PE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 01w01 FECF (wo): Framing error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the FE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 02w01 NECF (wo): Noise detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the NE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 03w01 ORECF (wo): Overrun error clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the ORE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 04w01 IDLECF (wo): Idle line detected clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the IDLE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 05w01 TXFECF (wo): TXFIFO empty clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TXFE flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 06w01 TCCF (wo): Transmission complete clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TC flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 07w01 TCBGTCF (wo): Transmission complete before Guard time clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the TCBGT flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 08w01 LBDCF (wo): LIN break detection clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the LBDF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If LIN mode is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008420 C   FIELD 09w01 CTSCF (wo): CTS clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CTSIF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the hardware flow control feature is not supported, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008420 C   FIELD 11w01 RTOCF (wo): Receiver timeout clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the RTOF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the Receiver timeout feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 12w01 EOBCF (wo): End of block clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the EOBF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support Smartcard mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to .
0x50008420 C   FIELD 13w01 UDRCF (wo): SPI slave underrun clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the UDRF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support SPI slave mode, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to
0x50008420 C   FIELD 17w01 CMCF (wo): Character match clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the CMF flag in the USART_ISR register.
0x50008420 C   FIELD 20w01 WUCF (wo): Wakeup from low-power mode clear flag Writing 1 to this bit clears the WUF flag in the USART_ISR register. Note: If the USART does not support the wakeup from Stop feature, this bit is reserved and must be kept at reset value. Refer to page 2297.
0x50008424 B  REGISTER RDR: USART receive data register
0x50008424 C   FIELD 00w09 RDR (ro): Receive data value Contains the received data character. The RDR register provides the parallel interface between the input shift register and the internal bus (see ). When receiving with the parity enabled, the value read in the MSB bit is the received parity bit.
0x50008428 B  REGISTER TDR: USART transmit data register
0x50008428 C   FIELD 00w09 TDR (rw): Transmit data value Contains the data character to be transmitted. The USART_TDR register provides the parallel interface between the internal bus and the output shift register (see ). When transmitting with the parity enabled (PCE bit set to 1 in the USART_CR1 register), the value written in the MSB (bit 7 or bit 8 depending on the data length) has no effect because it is replaced by the parity. Note: This register must be written only when TXE/TXFNF=1.
0x5000842C B  REGISTER PRESC: USART prescaler register
0x5000842C C   FIELD 00w04 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler The USART input clock can be divided by a prescaler factor: Remaining combinations: Reserved Note: When PRESCALER is programmed with a value different of the allowed ones, programmed prescaler value is equal to '1011' i.e. input clock divided by 256.
0x50008C00 A PERIPHERAL SEC_DTS
0x50008C00 B  REGISTER CFGR1: Temperature sensor configuration register 1
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 00w01 TS1_EN (rw): Temperature sensor 1 enable bit This bit is set and cleared by software. Note: Once enabled, the temperature sensor is active after a specific delay time. The TS1_RDY flag will be set when the sensor is ready.
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 04w01 TS1_START (rw): Start frequency measurement on temperature sensor 1 This bit is set and cleared by software.
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 08w04 TS1_INTRIG_SEL (rw): Input trigger selection bit for temperature sensor 1 These bits are set and cleared by software. They select which input triggers a temperature measurement. Refer to Section 19.3.10: Trigger input.
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 16w04 TS1_SMP_TIME (rw): Sampling time for temperature sensor 1 These bits allow increasing the sampling time to improve measurement precision. When the PCLK clock is selected as reference clock (REFCLK_SEL = 0), the measurement will be performed at TS1_SMP_TIME period of CLK_PTAT. When the LSE is selected as reference clock (REFCLK_SEL =1), the measurement will be performed at TS1_SMP_TIME period of LSE.
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 20w01 REFCLK_SEL (rw): Reference clock selection bit This bit is set and cleared by software. It indicates whether the reference clock is the high speed clock (PCLK) or the low speed clock (LSE).
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 21w01 Q_MEAS_OPT (rw): Quick measurement option bit This bit is set and cleared by software. It is used to increase the measurement speed by suppressing the calibration step. It is effective only when the LSE clock is used as reference clock (REFCLK_SEL=1).
0x50008C00 C   FIELD 24w07 HSREF_CLK_DIV (rw): High speed clock division ratio These bits are set and cleared by software. They can be used to define the division ratio for the main clock in order to obtain the internal frequency lower than 1 MHz required for the calibration. They are applicable only for calibration when PCLK is selected as reference clock (REFCLK_SEL=0). ...
0x50008C08 B  REGISTER T0VALR1: Temperature sensor T0 value register 1
0x50008C08 C   FIELD 00w16 TS1_FMT0 (ro): Engineering value of the frequency measured at T0 for temperature sensor 1 This value is expressed in 0.1 kHz.
0x50008C08 C   FIELD 16w02 TS1_T0 (ro): Engineering value of the T0 temperature for temperature sensor 1. Others: Reserved, must not be used.
0x50008C10 B  REGISTER RAMPVALR: Temperature sensor ramp value register
0x50008C10 C   FIELD 00w16 TS1_RAMP_COEFF (ro): Engineering value of the ramp coefficient for the temperature sensor 1. This value is expressed in Hz/C.
0x50008C14 B  REGISTER ITR1: Temperature sensor interrupt threshold register 1
0x50008C14 C   FIELD 00w16 TS1_LITTHD (rw): Low interrupt threshold for temperature sensor 1 These bits are set and cleared by software. They indicate the lowest value than can be reached before raising an interrupt signal.
0x50008C14 C   FIELD 16w16 TS1_HITTHD (rw): High interrupt threshold for temperature sensor 1 These bits are set and cleared by software. They indicate the highest value than can be reached before raising an interrupt signal.
0x50008C1C B  REGISTER DR: Temperature sensor data register
0x50008C1C C   FIELD 00w16 TS1_MFREQ (rw): Value of the counter output value for temperature sensor 1
0x50008C20 B  REGISTER SR: Temperature sensor status register
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 00w01 TS1_ITEF (ro): Interrupt flag for end of measurement on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK. This bit is set by hardware when a temperature measure is done. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS2_CITEF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_ITEFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 01w01 TS1_ITLF (ro): Interrupt flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK. This bit is set by hardware when the low threshold is set and reached. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS1_CITLF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_ITLFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 02w01 TS1_ITHF (ro): Interrupt flag for high threshold on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK This bit is set by hardware when the high threshold is set and reached. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS1_CITHF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_ITHFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 04w01 TS1_AITEF (ro): Asynchronous interrupt flag for end of measure on temperature sensor 1 This bit is set by hardware when a temperature measure is done. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS1_CAITEF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_AITEFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 05w01 TS1_AITLF (ro): Asynchronous interrupt flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1 This bit is set by hardware when the low threshold is reached. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS1_CAITLF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_AITLFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 06w01 TS1_AITHF (ro): Asynchronous interrupt flag for high threshold on temperature sensor 1 This bit is set by hardware when the high threshold is reached. It is cleared by software by writing 1 to the TS1_CAITHF bit in the DTS_ICIFR register. Note: This bit is active only when the TS1_AITHFEN bit is set
0x50008C20 C   FIELD 15w01 TS1_RDY (ro): Temperature sensor 1 ready flag This bit is set and reset by hardware. It indicates that a measurement is ongoing.
0x50008C24 B  REGISTER ITENR: Temperature sensor interrupt enable register
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 00w01 TS1_ITEEN (rw): Interrupt enable flag for end of measurement on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK. This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the synchronous interrupt for end of measurement.
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 01w01 TS1_ITLEN (rw): Interrupt enable flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK. This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the synchronous interrupt when the measure reaches or is below the low threshold.
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 02w01 TS1_ITHEN (rw): Interrupt enable flag for high threshold on temperature sensor 1, synchronized on PCLK. This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the interrupt when the measure reaches or is above the high threshold.
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 04w01 TS1_AITEEN (rw): Asynchronous interrupt enable flag for end of measurement on temperature sensor 1 This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the asynchronous interrupt for end of measurement (only when REFCLK_SEL = 1).
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 05w01 TS1_AITLEN (rw): Asynchronous interrupt enable flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1. This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the asynchronous interrupt when the temperature is below the low threshold (only when REFCLK_SEL= 1)
0x50008C24 C   FIELD 06w01 TS1_AITHEN (rw): Asynchronous interrupt enable flag on high threshold for temperature sensor 1. This bit are set and cleared by software. It enables the asynchronous interrupt when the temperature is above the high threshold (only when REFCLK_SEL= 1'')
0x50008C28 B  REGISTER ICIFR: Temperature sensor clear interrupt flag register
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 00w01 TS1_CITEF (rw): Interrupt clear flag for end of measurement on temperature sensor 1 Writing 1 to this bit clears the TS1_ITEF flag in the DTS_SR register.
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 01w01 TS1_CITLF (rw): Interrupt clear flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1 Writing 1 to this bit clears the TS1_ITLF flag in the DTS_SR register.
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 02w01 TS1_CITHF (rw): Interrupt clear flag for high threshold on temperature sensor 1 Writing this bit to 1 clears the TS1_ITHF flag in the DTS_SR register.
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 04w01 TS1_CAITEF (rw): Write once bit. Clear the asynchronous IT flag for End Of Measure for thermal sensor 1. Writing 1 clears the TS1_AITEF flag of the DTS_SR register.
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 05w01 TS1_CAITLF (rw): Asynchronous interrupt clear flag for low threshold on temperature sensor 1 Writing 1 to this bit clears the TS1_AITLF flag in the DTS_SR register.
0x50008C28 C   FIELD 06w01 TS1_CAITHF (rw): Asynchronous interrupt clear flag for high threshold on temperature sensor 1 Writing 1 to this bit clears the TS1_AITHF flag in the DTS_SR register.
