0x5001442C C   FIELD 00w20 ARR (rw): Auto-reload value ARR is the value to be loaded in the actual auto-reload register. Refer to the for more details about ARR update and behavior. The counter is blocked while the auto-reload value is null. Non-dithering mode (DITHEN = 0) The register holds the auto-reload value in ARR[15:0]. The ARR[19:16] bits are reset. Dithering mode (DITHEN = 1) The register holds the integer part in ARR[19:4]. The ARR[3:0] bitfield contains the dithered part.
