0x500220A8 C   FIELD 00w32 SECBB1 (rw): Secure/non-secure 8Kbytes flash Bank 1 sector attributes
0x500220AC B  REGISTER SECBB1R4: FLASH secure block based register for Bank 1
0x500220AC C   FIELD 00w32 SECBB1 (rw): Secure/non-secure 8Kbytes flash Bank 1 sector attributes
0x500220C0 B  REGISTER PRIVBB1R1: FLASH privilege block based register for Bank 1
0x500220C0 C   FIELD 00w32 PRIVBB1 (rw): Privileged/unprivileged 8-Kbyte flash Bank 1 sector attribute
0x500220C4 B  REGISTER PRIVBB1R2: FLASH privilege block based register for Bank 1
0x500220C4 C   FIELD 00w32 PRIVBB1 (rw): Privileged/unprivileged 8-Kbyte flash Bank 1 sector attribute
0x500220C8 B  REGISTER PRIVBB1R3: FLASH privilege block based register for Bank 1
0x500220C8 C   FIELD 00w32 PRIVBB1 (rw): Privileged/unprivileged 8-Kbyte flash Bank 1 sector attribute
0x500220CC B  REGISTER PRIVBB1R4: FLASH privilege block based register for Bank 1
0x500220CC C   FIELD 00w32 PRIVBB1 (rw): Privileged/unprivileged 8-Kbyte flash Bank 1 sector attribute
0x500220E0 B  REGISTER SECWM1R_CUR: FLASH security watermark for Bank 1
0x500220E0 C   FIELD 00w07 SECWM1_STRT (ro): Bank1 security WM area 1 start sector
0x500220E0 C   FIELD 16w07 SECWM1_END (ro): Bank1 security WM area 1 end sector
0x500220E4 B  REGISTER SECWM1R_PRG: FLASH security watermark for Bank 1
0x500220E4 C   FIELD 00w07 SECWM1_STRT (rw): Bank1 security WM area 1 start sector
0x500220E4 C   FIELD 16w07 SECWM1_END (rw): Bank1 security WM area 1 end sector
0x500220E8 B  REGISTER WRP1R_CUR: FLASH write sector group protection for Bank 1
0x500220E8 C   FIELD 00w32 WRPSG1 (ro): Bank 1 sector group protection option status byte Each FLASH_WRP1R_CUR bit reflects the write protection status of the corresponding group of four consecutive sectors in bank 1 (0: the group is write protected; 1: the group is not write protected) Bit 0: Group embedding sectors 0 to 3 Bit 1: Group embedding sectors 4 to 7 Bit N: Group embedding sectors 4 x N to 4 x N + 3 Bit 31: Group embedding sectors 124 to 127
0x500220EC B  REGISTER WRP1R_PRG: FLASH write sector group protection for Bank 1
0x500220EC C   FIELD 00w32 WRPSG1 (rw): Bank1 sector group protection option status byte Setting WRPSG1 bits to 0 write protects the corresponding group of four consecutive sectors in bank 1 (0: the group is write protected; 1: the group is not write protected) Bit 0: Group embedding sectors 0 to 3 Bit 1: Group embedding sectors 4 to 7 Bit N: Group embedding sectors 4 x N to 4 x N + 3 Bit 31: Group embedding sectors 124 to 127
0x500220F0 B  REGISTER EDATA1R_CUR: FLASH data sector configuration Bank 1
0x500220F0 C   FIELD 00w03 EDATA1_STRT (ro): EDATA1_STRT contains the start sectors of the flash high-cycle data area in Bank1 There is no hardware effect to those bits. They shall be managed by ST tools in Flasher. ...
0x500220F0 C   FIELD 15w01 EDATA1_EN (ro): Bank1 flash high-cycle data enable
0x500220F4 B  REGISTER EDATA1R_PRG: FLASH data sector configuration Bank 1
0x500220F4 C   FIELD 00w03 EDATA1_STRT (rw): EDATA1_STRT contains the start sectors of the flash high-cycle data area in Bank 1 There is no hardware effect to those bits. They shall be managed by ST tools in Flasher. ... Note: 111: The eight last sectors of the Bank 1 are reserved for flash high-cycle data
0x500220F4 C   FIELD 15w01 EDATA1_EN (rw): Bank 1 flash high-cycle data enable
0x500220F8 B  REGISTER HDP1R_CUR: FLASH HDP Bank 1 configuration
0x500220F8 C   FIELD 00w07 HDP1_STRT (ro): HDPL barrier start set in number of 8-Kbyte sectors
0x500220F8 C   FIELD 16w07 HDP1_END (ro): HDPL barrier end set in number of 8-Kbyte sectors
0x500220FC B  REGISTER HDP1R_PRG: FLASH HDP Bank 1 configuration
0x500220FC C   FIELD 00w07 HDP1_STRT (rw): HDPL barrier start set in number of 8-Kbyte sectors
0x500220FC C   FIELD 16w07 HDP1_END (rw): HDPL barrier end set in number of 8-Kbyte sectors
0x50022100 B  REGISTER ECCCORR: FLASH ECC correction register
0x50022100 C   FIELD 00w16 ADDR_ECC (ro): ECC error address When an ECC error occurs (for single correction) during a read operation, the ADDR_ECC contains the address that generated the error. ADDR_ECC is reset when the flag error is reset. The flash interface programs the address in this register only when no ECC error flags are set. This means that only the first address that generated an ECC error is saved. The address in ADDR_ECC is relative to the flash memory area where the error occurred (user flash memory, system flash memory, data area, read-only/OTP area).
0x50022100 C   FIELD 20w01 OBK_ECC (ro): Single ECC error corrected in flash OB Keys storage area. It indicates the OBK storage concerned by ECC error.
0x50022100 C   FIELD 21w01 EDATA_ECC (ro): ECC fail for corrected ECC error in flash high-cycle data area It indicates if flash high-cycle data area is concerned by ECC error.
0x50022100 C   FIELD 22w01 BK_ECC (ro): ECC fail bank for corrected ECC error It indicates which bank is concerned by ECC error
0x50022100 C   FIELD 23w01 SYSF_ECC (ro): ECC fail for corrected ECC error in system flash memory It indicates if system flash memory is concerned by ECC error.
0x50022100 C   FIELD 24w01 OTP_ECC (ro): OTP ECC error bit This bit is set to 1 when one single ECC correction occurred during the last successful read operation from the read-only/ OTP area. The address of the ECC error is available in ADDR_ECC bitfield.
0x50022100 C   FIELD 25w01 ECCCIE (rw): ECC single correction error interrupt enable bit When ECCCIE bit is set to 1, an interrupt is generated when an ECC single correction error occurs during a read operation.
0x50022100 C   FIELD 30w01 ECCC (rw): ECC correction set by hardware when single ECC error has been detected and corrected. Cleared by writing 1.
0x50022104 B  REGISTER ECCDETR: FLASH ECC detection register
0x50022104 C   FIELD 00w16 ADDR_ECC (ro): ECC error address When an ECC error occurs (double detection) during a read operation, the ADDR_ECC contains the address that generated the error. ADDR_ECC is reset when the flag error is reset. The flash interface programs the address in this register only when no ECC error flags are set. This means that only the first address that generated an double ECC error is saved. The address in ADDR_ECC is relative to the flash memory area where the error occurred (user flash memory, system flash memory, data area, read-only/OTP area).
0x50022104 C   FIELD 20w01 OBK_ECC (ro): ECC fail double ECC error in flash OB Keys storage area. It indicates the OBK storage concerned by ECC error.
0x50022104 C   FIELD 21w01 EDATA_ECC (ro): ECC fail double ECC error in flash high-cycle data area It indicates if flash high-cycle data area is concerned by ECC error.
0x50022104 C   FIELD 22w01 BK_ECC (ro): ECC fail bank for double ECC error It indicates which bank is concerned by ECC error
0x50022104 C   FIELD 23w01 SYSF_ECC (ro): ECC fail for double ECC error in system flash memory It indicates if system flash memory is concerned by ECC error.
0x50022104 C   FIELD 24w01 OTP_ECC (ro): OTP ECC error bit This bit is set to 1 when double ECC detection occurred during the last read operation from the read-only/ OTP area. The address of the ECC error is available in ADDR_ECC bitfield.
0x50022104 C   FIELD 31w01 ECCD (rw): ECC detection Set by hardware when two ECC error has been detected. When this bit is set, a NMI is generated. Cleared by writing 1. Needs to be cleared in order to detect subsequent double ECC errors.
0x50022108 B  REGISTER ECCDR: FLASH ECC data
0x50022108 C   FIELD 00w16 DATA_ECC (ro): ECC error data When an double detection ECC error occurs on special areas with 6-bit ECC on 16-bit data (data area, read-only/OTP area), the failing data is read to this register. By checking if it is possible to determine whether the failure was on a real data, or due to access to uninitialized memory.
