0x52028440 B  REGISTER SHSR1: DAC channel1 sample and hold sample time register
0x52028440 C   FIELD 00w10 TSAMPLE (rw): DAC channel1 sample time (only valid in Sample and hold mode) These bits can be written when the DAC channel1 is disabled or also during normal operation. in the latter case, the write can be done only when BWST1 of DAC_SR register is low, If BWST1 = 1, the write operation is ignored.
0x52028444 B  REGISTER SHSR2: DAC channel2 sample and hold sample time register
0x52028444 C   FIELD 00w10 TSAMPLE (rw): DAC channel1 sample time (only valid in Sample and hold mode) These bits can be written when the DAC channel1 is disabled or also during normal operation. in the latter case, the write can be done only when BWST1 of DAC_SR register is low, If BWST1 = 1, the write operation is ignored.
0x52028448 B  REGISTER SHHR: DAC sample and hold time register
0x52028448 C   FIELD 00w10 THOLD1 (rw): DAC channel1 hold time (only valid in Sample and hold mode)
0x52028448 C   FIELD 16w10 THOLD2 (rw): DAC channel2 hold time (only valid in Sample and hold mode)
0x5202844C B  REGISTER SHRR: DAC sample and hold refresh time register
0x5202844C C   FIELD 00w08 TREFRESH1 (rw): DAC channel1 refresh time (only valid in Sample and hold mode)
0x5202844C C   FIELD 16w08 TREFRESH2 (rw): DAC channel2 refresh time (only valid in Sample and hold mode)
0x5202C000 A PERIPHERAL SEC_DCMI
0x5202C000 B  REGISTER CR: DCMI control register
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 00w01 CAPTURE (rw): Capture enable The camera interface waits for the first start of frame, then a DMA request is generated to transfer the received data into the destination memory. In snapshot mode, the CAPTURE bit is automatically cleared at the end of the first frame received. In continuous grab mode, if the software clears this bit while a capture is ongoing, the bit is effectively cleared after the frame end. Note: The DMA controller and all DCMI configuration registers must be programmed correctly before enabling this bit.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 01w01 CM (rw): Capture mode
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 02w01 CROP (rw): Crop feature
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 03w01 JPEG (rw): JPEG format
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 04w01 ESS (rw): Embedded synchronization select Note: Valid only for 8-bit parallel data. HSPOL/VSPOL are ignored when the ESS bit is set. This bit is disabled in JPEG mode.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 05w01 PCKPOL (rw): Pixel clock polarity This bit configures the capture edge of the pixel clock.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 06w01 HSPOL (rw): Horizontal synchronization polarity This bit indicates the level on the DCMI_HSYNC pin when the data are not valid on the parallel interface.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 07w01 VSPOL (rw): Vertical synchronization polarity This bit indicates the level on the DCMI_VSYNC pin when the data are not valid on the parallel interface.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 08w02 FCRC (rw): Frame capture rate control These bits define the frequency of frame capture. They are meaningful only in Continuous grab mode. They are ignored in snapshot mode.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 10w02 EDM (rw): Extended data mode
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 14w01 ENABLE (rw): DCMI enable Note: The DCMI configuration registers must be programmed correctly before enabling this bit.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 16w02 BSM (rw): Byte Select mode Note: This mode only works for EDM[1:0] = 00. For all other EDM values, this field must be programmed to the reset value.
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 18w01 OEBS (rw): Odd/Even Byte Select (Byte Select Start) This bit works in conjunction with BSM field (BSM different 00).
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 19w01 LSM (rw): Line Select mode
0x5202C000 C   FIELD 20w01 OELS (rw): Odd/Even Line Select (Line Select Start) This bit works in conjunction with the LSM field (LSM = 1).
0x5202C004 B  REGISTER SR: DCMI status register
0x5202C004 C   FIELD 00w01 HSYNC (ro): Horizontal synchronization This bit gives the state of the DCMI_HSYNC pin with the correct programmed polarity. When embedded synchronization codes are used, the meaning of this bit is the following: In case of embedded synchronization, this bit is meaningful only if the CAPTURE bit in DCMI_CR is set.
0x5202C004 C   FIELD 01w01 VSYNC (ro): Vertical synchronization This bit gives the state of the DCMI_VSYNC pin with the correct programmed polarity. When embedded synchronization codes are used, the meaning of this bit is the following: In case of embedded synchronization, this bit is meaningful only if the CAPTURE bit in DCMI_CR is set.
0x5202C004 C   FIELD 02w01 FNE (ro): FIFO not empty This bit gives the status of the FIFO.
0x5202C008 B  REGISTER RIS: DCMI raw interrupt status register
0x5202C008 C   FIELD 00w01 FRAME_RIS (ro): Capture complete raw interrupt status This bit is set when a frame or window has been captured. In case of a cropped window, this bit is set at the end of line of the last line in the crop. It is set even if the captured frame is empty (e.g. window cropped outside the frame). The bit is cleared by setting the FRAME_ISC bit of the DCMI_ICR register.
0x5202C008 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_RIS (ro): Overrun raw interrupt status The bit is cleared by setting the OVR_ISC bit of the DCMI_ICR register.
0x5202C008 C   FIELD 02w01 ERR_RIS (ro): Synchronization error raw interrupt status This bit is valid only in the embedded synchronization mode. It is cleared by setting the ERR_ISC bit of the DCMI_ICR register. Note: This bit is available only in embedded synchronization mode.
0x5202C008 C   FIELD 03w01 VSYNC_RIS (ro): DCMI_VSYNC raw interrupt status This bit is set when the DCMI_VSYNC signal changes from the inactive state to the active state. In the case of embedded synchronization, this bit is set only if the CAPTURE bit is set in DCMI_CR. It is cleared by setting the VSYNC_ISC bit of the DCMI_ICR register.
0x5202C008 C   FIELD 04w01 LINE_RIS (ro): Line raw interrupt status This bit gets set when the DCMI_HSYNC signal changes from the inactive state to the active state. It goes high even if the line is not valid. In the case of embedded synchronization, this bit is set only if the CAPTURE bit in DCMI_CR is set. It is cleared by setting the LINE_ISC bit of the DCMI_ICR register.
0x5202C00C B  REGISTER IER: DCMI interrupt enable register
0x5202C00C C   FIELD 00w01 FRAME_IE (rw): Capture complete interrupt enable
0x5202C00C C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_IE (rw): Overrun interrupt enable
0x5202C00C C   FIELD 02w01 ERR_IE (rw): Synchronization error interrupt enable Note: This bit is available only in embedded synchronization mode.
0x5202C00C C   FIELD 03w01 VSYNC_IE (rw): DCMI_VSYNC interrupt enable The active state of the DCMI_VSYNC signal is defined by the VSPOL bit.
0x5202C00C C   FIELD 04w01 LINE_IE (rw): Line interrupt enable
0x5202C010 B  REGISTER MIS: DCMI masked interrupt status register
0x5202C010 C   FIELD 00w01 FRAME_MIS (ro): Capture complete masked interrupt status This bit gives the status of the masked capture complete interrupt
0x5202C010 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_MIS (ro): Overrun masked interrupt status This bit gives the status of the masked overflow interrupt.
0x5202C010 C   FIELD 02w01 ERR_MIS (ro): Synchronization error masked interrupt status This bit gives the status of the masked synchronization error interrupt. Note: This bit is available only in embedded synchronization mode.
0x5202C010 C   FIELD 03w01 VSYNC_MIS (ro): VSYNC masked interrupt status This bit gives the status of the masked VSYNC interrupt. The active state of the DCMI_VSYNC signal is defined by the VSPOL bit.
0x5202C010 C   FIELD 04w01 LINE_MIS (ro): Line masked interrupt status This bit gives the status of the masked line interrupt.
0x5202C014 B  REGISTER ICR: DCMI interrupt clear register
0x5202C014 C   FIELD 00w01 FRAME_ISC (wo): Capture complete interrupt status clear Setting this bit clears the FRAME_RIS flag in the DCMI_RIS register.
0x5202C014 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_ISC (wo): Overrun interrupt status clear Setting this bit clears the OVR_RIS flag in the DCMI_RIS register.
0x5202C014 C   FIELD 02w01 ERR_ISC (wo): Synchronization error interrupt status clear Setting this bit clears the ERR_RIS flag in the DCMI_RIS register. Note: This bit is available only in embedded synchronization mode.
0x5202C014 C   FIELD 03w01 VSYNC_ISC (wo): Vertical Synchronization interrupt status clear Setting this bit clears the VSYNC_RIS flag in the DCMI_RIS register.
0x5202C014 C   FIELD 04w01 LINE_ISC (wo): line interrupt status clear Setting this bit clears the LINE_RIS flag in the DCMI_RIS register.
0x5202C018 B  REGISTER ESCR: DCMI embedded synchronization code register
0x5202C018 C   FIELD 00w08 FSC (rw): Frame start delimiter code This byte specifies the code of the frame start delimiter. The code consists of 4 bytes in the form of 0xFF, 0x00, 0x00, FSC. If FSC is programmed to 0xFF, no frame start delimiter is detected. But, the first occurrence of LSC after an FEC code is interpreted as a start of frame delimiter.
0x5202C018 C   FIELD 08w08 LSC (rw): Line start delimiter code This byte specifies the code of the line start delimiter. The code consists of 4 bytes in the form of 0xFF, 0x00, 0x00, LSC.
0x5202C018 C   FIELD 16w08 LEC (rw): Line end delimiter code This byte specifies the code of the line end delimiter. The code consists of 4 bytes in the form of 0xFF, 0x00, 0x00, LEC.
0x5202C018 C   FIELD 24w08 FEC (rw): Frame end delimiter code This byte specifies the code of the frame end delimiter. The code consists of 4 bytes in the form of 0xFF, 0x00, 0x00, FEC. If FEC is programmed to 0xFF, all the unused codes (0xFF0000XY) are interpreted as frame end delimiters.
0x5202C01C B  REGISTER ESUR: DCMI embedded synchronization unmask register
0x5202C01C C   FIELD 00w08 FSU (rw): Frame start delimiter unmask This byte specifies the mask to be applied to the code of the frame start delimiter.
0x5202C01C C   FIELD 08w08 LSU (rw): Line start delimiter unmask This byte specifies the mask to be applied to the code of the line start delimiter.
0x5202C01C C   FIELD 16w08 LEU (rw): Line end delimiter unmask This byte specifies the mask to be applied to the code of the line end delimiter.
0x5202C01C C   FIELD 24w08 FEU (rw): Frame end delimiter unmask This byte specifies the mask to be applied to the code of the frame end delimiter.
0x5202C020 B  REGISTER CWSTRT: DCMI crop window start
0x5202C020 C   FIELD 00w14 HOFFCNT (rw): Horizontal offset count This value gives the number of pixel clocks to count before starting a capture.
0x5202C020 C   FIELD 16w13 VST (rw): Vertical start line count The image capture starts with this line number. Previous line data are ignored. ....
0x5202C024 B  REGISTER CWSIZE: DCMI crop window size
0x5202C024 C   FIELD 00w14 CAPCNT (rw): Capture count This value gives the number of pixel clocks to be captured from the starting point on the same line. It value must corresponds to word-aligned data for different widths of parallel interfaces. 0x0000 = 1 pixel 0x0001 = 2 pixels 0x0002 = 3 pixels ....
0x5202C024 C   FIELD 16w14 VLINE (rw): Vertical line count This value gives the number of lines to be captured from the starting point. ....
0x5202C028 B  REGISTER DR: DCMI data register
0x5202C028 C   FIELD 00w08 BYTE0 (ro): Data byte 0
0x5202C028 C   FIELD 08w08 BYTE1 (ro): Data byte 1
0x5202C028 C   FIELD 16w08 BYTE2 (ro): Data byte 2
0x5202C028 C   FIELD 24w08 BYTE3 (ro): Data byte 3
0x5202C400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_PSSI
0x5202C400 B  REGISTER CR: PSSI control register
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 05w01 CKPOL (rw): Parallel data clock polarity This bit configures the capture edge of the parallel clock or the edge used for driving outputs, depending on OUTEN.
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 06w01 DEPOL (rw): Data enable (PSSI_DE) polarity This bit indicates the level on the PSSI_DE pin when the data are not valid on the parallel interface.
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 08w01 RDYPOL (rw): Ready (PSSI_RDY) polarity This bit indicates the level on the PSSI_RDY pin when the data are not valid on the parallel interface.
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 10w02 EDM (rw): Extended data mode
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 14w01 ENABLE (rw): PSSI enable The contents of the FIFO are flushed when ENABLE is cleared to 0. Note: When ENABLE=1, the content of PSSI_CR must not be changed, except for the ENABLE bit itself. All configuration bits can change as soon as ENABLE changes from 0 to 1. The DMA controller and all PSSI configuration registers must be programmed correctly before setting the ENABLE bit to 1. The ENABLE bit and the DCMI ENABLE bit (bit 15 of DCMI_CR) must not be set to 1 at the same time.
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 18w03 DERDYCFG (rw): Data enable and ready configuration When the PSSI_RDY function is mapped to the PSSI_DE pin (settings 101 or 111), it is still the RDYPOL bit which determines its polarity. Similarly, when the PSSI_DE function is mapped to the PSSI_RDY pin (settings 110 or 111), it is still the DEPOL bit which determines its polarity.
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 30w01 DMAEN (rw): DMA enable bit
0x5202C400 C   FIELD 31w01 OUTEN (rw): Data direction selection bit
0x5202C404 B  REGISTER SR: PSSI status register
0x5202C404 C   FIELD 02w01 RTT4B (ro): FIFO is ready to transfer four bytes
0x5202C404 C   FIELD 03w01 RTT1B (ro): FIFO is ready to transfer one byte
0x5202C408 B  REGISTER RIS: PSSI raw interrupt status register
0x5202C408 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_RIS (ro): Data buffer overrun/underrun raw interrupt status This bit is cleared by writing a 1 to the OVR_ISC bit in PSSI_ICR.
0x5202C40C B  REGISTER IER: PSSI interrupt enable register
0x5202C40C C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_IE (rw): Data buffer overrun/underrun interrupt enable
0x5202C410 B  REGISTER MIS: PSSI masked interrupt status register
0x5202C410 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_MIS (ro): Data buffer overrun/underrun masked interrupt status This bit is set to 1 only when PSSI_IER/OVR_IE and PSSI_RIS/OVR_RIS are both set to 1.
0x5202C414 B  REGISTER ICR: PSSI interrupt clear register
0x5202C414 C   FIELD 01w01 OVR_ISC (wo): Data buffer overrun/underrun interrupt status clear Writing this bit to 1 clears the OVR_RIS bit in PSSI_RIS.
0x5202C428 B  REGISTER DR: PSSI data register
0x5202C428 C   FIELD 00w08 BYTE0 (rw): Data byte 0
0x5202C428 C   FIELD 08w08 BYTE1 (rw): Data byte 1
0x5202C428 C   FIELD 16w08 BYTE2 (rw): Data byte 2
0x5202C428 C   FIELD 24w08 BYTE3 (rw): Data byte 3
0x520C0400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_HASH
0x520C0400 B  REGISTER CR: HASH control register
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 02w01 INIT (rw): Initialize message digest calculation Writing this bit to 1 resets the hash processor core, so that the HASH is ready to compute the message digest of a new message. Writing this bit to 0 has no effect. Reading this bit always returns 0.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 03w01 DMAE (rw): DMA enable After this bit is set, it is cleared by hardware while the last data of the message is written into the hash processor. Setting this bit to 0 while a DMA transfer is ongoing does not abort the current transfer. Instead, the DMA interface of the HASH remains internally enabled until the transfer is completed or INIT is written to 1. Setting INIT bit to 1 does not clear DMAE bit.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 04w02 DATATYPE (rw): Data type selection This bitfield defines the format of the data entered into the HASH_DIN register:
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 06w01 MODE (rw): Mode selection This bit selects the normal or the keyed HMAC mode for the selected algorithm: This selection is only taken into account when the INIT bit is set. Changing this bit during a computation has no effect.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 08w04 NBW (ro): Number of words already pushed Refer to NBWP[3:0] bitfield of HASH_SR for a description of NBW[3:0] bitfield. This bit is read-only.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 12w01 DINNE (ro): DIN not empty Refer to DINNE bit of HASH_SR for a description of DINNE bit. This bit is read-only.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 13w01 MDMAT (rw): Multiple DMA transfers This bit is set when hashing large files when multiple DMA transfers are needed.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 16w01 LKEY (rw): Long key selection The application must set this bit if the HMAC key is greater than the block size corresponding to the hash algorithm (see algorithms for details). For example the block size is 64 bytes for SHA2-256. This selection is only taken into account when the INIT and MODE bits are set (HMAC mode selected). Changing this bit during a computation has no effect.
0x520C0400 C   FIELD 17w04 ALGO (rw): Algorithm selection These bits select the hash algorithm: This selection is only taken into account when the INIT bit is set. Changing this bitfield during a computation has no effect. When the ALGO bitfield is updated and INIT bit is set, NBWE in HASH_SR is automatically updated to 0x11.
0x520C0404 B  REGISTER DIN: HASH data input register
0x520C0404 C   FIELD 00w32 DATAIN (wo): Data input Writing this register pushes the current register content into the FIFO, and the register takes the new value presented on the AHB bus. Reading this register returns zeros.
0x520C0408 B  REGISTER STR: HASH start register
0x520C0408 C   FIELD 00w05 NBLW (rw): Number of valid bits in the last word When the last word of the message bit string is written to HASH_DIN register, the hash processor takes only the valid bits, specified as below, after internal data swapping: ... The above mechanism is valid only if DCAL = 0. If NBLW bits are written while DCAL is set to 1, the NBLW bitfield remains unchanged. In other words it is not possible to configure NBLW and set DCAL at the same time. Reading NBLW bits returns the last value written to NBLW.
0x520C0408 C   FIELD 08w01 DCAL (rw): Digest calculation Writing this bit to 1 starts the message padding using the previously written value of NBLW, and starts the calculation of the final message digest with all the data words written to the input FIFO since the INIT bit was last written to 1. Reading this bit returns 0.
0x520C040C B  REGISTER HRA0: HASH aliased digest register 0
0x520C040C C   FIELD 00w32 Hx (ro): Hash data x Refer to introduction.
0x520C0410 B  REGISTER HRA1: HASH aliased digest register 1
0x520C0410 C   FIELD 00w32 Hx (ro): Hash data x Refer to introduction.
0x520C0414 B  REGISTER HRA2: HASH aliased digest register 2
0x520C0414 C   FIELD 00w32 Hx (ro): Hash data x Refer to introduction.
0x520C0418 B  REGISTER HRA3: HASH aliased digest register 3
0x520C0418 C   FIELD 00w32 Hx (ro): Hash data x Refer to introduction.
0x520C041C B  REGISTER HRA4: HASH aliased digest register 4
0x520C041C C   FIELD 00w32 Hx (ro): Hash data x Refer to introduction.
0x520C0420 B  REGISTER IMR: HASH interrupt enable register
0x520C0420 C   FIELD 00w01 DINIE (rw): Data input interrupt enable
0x520C0420 C   FIELD 01w01 DCIE (rw): Digest calculation completion interrupt enable
0x520C0424 B  REGISTER SR: HASH status register
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 00w01 DINIS (rw): Data input interrupt status This bit is set by hardware when the FIFO is ready to get a new block (16 locations are free). It is cleared by writing it to 0 or by writing the HASH_DIN register. When DINIS = 0, HASH_CSRx registers reads as zero.
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 01w01 DCIS (rw): Digest calculation completion interrupt status This bit is set by hardware when a digest becomes ready (the whole message has been processed). It is cleared by writing it to 0 or by writing the INIT bit to 1 in the HASH_CR register.
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 02w01 DMAS (ro): DMA Status This bit provides information on the DMA interface activity. It is set with DMAE and cleared when DMAE = 0 and no DMA transfer is ongoing. No interrupt is associated with this bit.
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 03w01 BUSY (ro): Busy bit
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 09w05 NBWP (ro): Number of words already pushed This bitfield is the exact number of words in the message that have already been pushed into the FIFO. NBWP is incremented by 1 when a write access is performed to the HASH_DIN register. When a digest calculation starts, NBWP is updated to NBWP- block size (in words), and NBWP goes to zero when the INIT bit is written to 1.
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 15w01 DINNE (ro): DIN not empty This bit is set when the HASH_DIN register holds valid data (that is after being written at least once). It is cleared when either the INIT bit (initialization) or the DCAL bit (completion of the previous message processing) is written to 1.
0x520C0424 C   FIELD 16w05 NBWE (ro): Number of words expected This bitfield reflects the number of words in the message that must be pushed into the FIFO to trigger a partial computation. NBWE is decremented by 1 when a write access is performed to the HASH_DIN register. NBWE is set to the expected block size +1 in words (0x11) when INIT bit is set in HASH_CR. It is set to the expected block size (0x10) when the partial digest calculation ends.
