0x54020800 A PERIPHERAL SEC_PWR
0x54020800 B  REGISTER PMCR: PWR power mode control register
0x54020800 C   FIELD 00w01 LPMS (rw): low-power mode selection This bit defines the Deepsleep mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 02w02 SVOS (rw): system Stop mode voltage scaling selection These bits control the Vsub CORE/sub voltage level in system Stop mode, to obtain the best trade-off between power consumption and performance.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 07w01 CSSF (rw): clear Standby and Stop flags (always read as 0) This bit is cleared to 0 by hardware.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 09w01 FLPS (rw): Flash memory low-power mode in Stop mode This bit is used to obtain the best trade-off between low-power consumption and restart time when exiting from Stop mode. When it is set, the Flash memory enters low-power mode when the CPU domain is in Stop mode. Note: When system enters stop mode with SVOS5 enabled, Flash memory is automatically forced in low-power mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 12w01 BOOSTE (rw): analog switch Vsub BOOST/sub control This bit enables the booster to guarantee the analog switch AC performance when the Vsub DD/sub supply voltage is below 2.7 V (reduction of the total harmonic distortion to have the same switch performance over the full supply voltage range) The Vsub DD/sub supply voltage can be monitored through the PVD and the PLS bits.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 13w01 AVD_READY (rw): analog voltage ready This bit is only used when the analog switch boost needs to be enabled (see BOOSTE bit). It must be set by software when the expected Vsub DDA/sub analog supply level is available. The correct analog supply level is indicated by the AVDO bit (PWR_VMSR register) after setting the AVDEN bit (PWR_VMCR register) and selecting the supply level to be monitored (ALS bits).
0x54020800 C   FIELD 16w01 ETHERNETSO (rw): ETHERNET RAM shut-off in Stop mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 23w01 SRAM3SO (rw): AHB SRAM3 shut-off in Stop mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 24w01 SRAM2_16SO (rw): AHB SRAM2 16-Kbyte shut-off in Stop mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 25w01 SRAM2_48SO (rw): AHB SRAM2 48-Kbyte shut-off in Stop mode.
0x54020800 C   FIELD 26w01 SRAM1SO (rw): AHB SRAM1 shut-off in Stop mode
0x54020804 B  REGISTER PMSR: PWR status register
0x54020804 C   FIELD 05w01 STOPF (ro): Stop flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by any reset or by setting the CSSF bit.
0x54020804 C   FIELD 06w01 SBF (ro): System standby flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a POR or by setting the CSSF bit.
0x54020810 B  REGISTER VOSCR: PWR voltage scaling control register
0x54020810 C   FIELD 04w02 VOS (rw): voltage scaling selection according to performance These bits control the Vsub CORE/sub voltage level and allow to obtain the best trade-off between power consumption and performance: - In bypass mode, these bits must also be set according to the external provided core voltage level and related performance. - When increasing the performance, the voltage scaling must be changed before increasing the system frequency. - When decreasing performance, the system frequency must first be decreased before changing the voltage scaling.
0x54020814 B  REGISTER VOSSR: PWR voltage scaling status register
0x54020814 C   FIELD 03w01 VOSRDY (ro): Ready bit for Vsub CORE/sub voltage scaling output selection.
0x54020814 C   FIELD 13w01 ACTVOSRDY (ro): Voltage level ready for currently used VOS
0x54020814 C   FIELD 14w02 ACTVOS (ro): voltage output scaling currently applied to Vsub CORE/sub This field provides the last VOS value.
0x54020820 B  REGISTER BDCR: PWR Backup domain control register
0x54020820 C   FIELD 00w01 BREN (rw): Backup RAM retention in Standby and Vsub BAT/sub modes When this bit set, the backup regulator (used to maintain the backup RAM content in Standby and Vsub BAT/sub modes) is enabled. If BREN is cleared, the backup regulator is switched off. The backup RAM can still be used in Run and Stop modes. However its content is lost in Standby and Vsub BAT/sub modes. If BREN is set, the application must wait till the backup regulator ready flag (BRRDY) is set to indicate that the data written into the SRAM is maintained in Standby and Vsub BAT/sub modes.
0x54020820 C   FIELD 01w01 MONEN (rw): Backup domain voltage and temperature monitoring enable
0x54020820 C   FIELD 08w01 VBE (rw): Vsub BAT/sub charging enable Note: Reset only by POR,.
0x54020820 C   FIELD 09w01 VBRS (rw): Vsub BAT/sub charging resistor selection
0x54020824 B  REGISTER DBPCR: PWR Backup domain control register
0x54020824 C   FIELD 00w01 DBP (rw): Disable Backup domain write protection In reset state, all registers and SRAM in Backup domain are protected against parasitic write access. This bit must be set to enable write access to these registers.
0x54020828 B  REGISTER BDSR: PWR Backup domain status register
0x54020828 C   FIELD 16w01 BRRDY (ro): backup regulator ready This bit is set by hardware to indicate that the backup regulator is ready.
0x54020828 C   FIELD 20w01 VBATL (ro): Vsub BAT/sub level monitoring versus low threshold
0x54020828 C   FIELD 21w01 VBATH (ro): Vsub BAT/sub level monitoring versus high threshold
0x54020828 C   FIELD 22w01 TEMPL (ro): temperature level monitoring versus low threshold
0x54020828 C   FIELD 23w01 TEMPH (ro): temperature level monitoring versus high threshold
0x5402082C B  REGISTER UCPDR: PWR USB Type-C power delivery register
0x5402082C C   FIELD 00w01 UCPD_DBDIS (rw): USB Type-C and power delivery dead battery disable After exiting reset, the USB Type-C 'dead battery' behavior is enabled, which may have a pull-down effect on CC1 and CC2 pins. It is recommended to disable it in all case, either to stop this pull-down or to hand over control to the UCPD (which should therefore be initialized before doing the disable).
0x5402082C C   FIELD 01w01 UCPD_STBY (rw): USB Type-c and Power delivery Standby mode When set, this bit is used to memorize the UCPD configuration in Standby mode. This bit must be written to 1 just before entering Standby mode when using UCPD, and it must be written to 0 after exiting the standby mode and before writing any UCPD register.
0x54020830 B  REGISTER SCCR: PWR supply configuration control register
0x54020830 C   FIELD 00w01 BYPASS (rwonce): power management unit bypass
0x54020830 C   FIELD 08w01 LDOEN (ro): LDO enable The value is set by hardware when the package uses the LDO regulator.
0x54020830 C   FIELD 09w01 SMPSEN (ro): SMPS enable The value is set by hardware when the package uses the SMPS regulator.
0x54020834 B  REGISTER VMCR: PWR voltage monitor control register
0x54020834 C   FIELD 00w01 PVDE (rw): PVD enable
0x54020834 C   FIELD 01w03 PLS (rw): programmable voltage detector (PVD) level selection These bits select the voltage threshold detected by the PVD.
0x54020834 C   FIELD 08w01 AVDEN (rw): peripheral voltage monitor on Vsub DDA/sub enable
0x54020834 C   FIELD 09w02 ALS (rw): analog voltage detector (AVD) level selection These bits select the voltage threshold detected by the AVD.
0x54020838 B  REGISTER USBSCR: PWR USB supply control register
0x54020838 C   FIELD 24w01 USB33DEN (rw): Vsub DDUSB/sub voltage level detector enable
0x54020838 C   FIELD 25w01 USB33SV (rw): independent USB supply valid This bit is used to validate the Vsub DDUSB/sub supply for electrical and logical isolation purpose. Setting this bit is mandatory to use the USBFS peripheral. If Vsub DDUSB/sub is not always present in the application, the Vsub DDUSB/sub voltage monitor can be used to determine whether this supply is ready or not.
0x5402083C B  REGISTER VMSR: PWR voltage monitor status register
0x5402083C C   FIELD 19w01 AVDO (ro): analog voltage detector output on Vsub DDA/sub This bit is set and cleared by hardware. It is valid only if AVD on VDDA is enabled by the AVDEN bit. Note: Since the AVD is disabled in Standby mode, this bit is equal to 0 after standby or reset until the AVDEN bit is set.
0x5402083C C   FIELD 20w01 VDDIO2RDY (ro): voltage detector output on Vsub DDIO2/sub This bit is set and cleared by hardware.
0x5402083C C   FIELD 22w01 PVDO (ro): programmable voltage detect output This bit is set and cleared by hardware. It is valid only if the PVD has been enabled by the PVDE bit. Note: Since the PVD is disabled in Standby mode, this bit is equal to 0 after Standby or reset until the PVDE bit is set.
0x5402083C C   FIELD 24w01 USB33RDY (ro): Vsub DDUSB/sub ready
0x54020840 B  REGISTER WUSCR: PWR wakeup status clear register
0x54020840 C   FIELD 00w01 CWUF1 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 01w01 CWUF2 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 02w01 CWUF3 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 03w01 CWUF4 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 04w01 CWUF5 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 05w01 CWUF6 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 06w01 CWUF7 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020840 C   FIELD 07w01 CWUF8 (wo): clear wakeup pin flag for WUFx These bits are always read as 0.
0x54020844 B  REGISTER WUSR: PWR wakeup status register
0x54020844 C   FIELD 00w01 WUF1 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 01w01 WUF2 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 02w01 WUF3 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 03w01 WUF4 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 04w01 WUF5 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 05w01 WUF6 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 06w01 WUF7 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020844 C   FIELD 07w01 WUF8 (ro): wakeup pin WUFx flag This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a RESET pin or by setting the CWUFx bit in PWR_WUSCR register.
0x54020848 B  REGISTER WUCR: PWR wakeup configuration register
0x54020848 C   FIELD 00w01 WUPEN1 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 01w01 WUPEN2 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 02w01 WUPEN3 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 03w01 WUPEN4 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 04w01 WUPEN5 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 05w01 WUPEN6 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 06w01 WUPEN7 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 07w01 WUPEN8 (rw): enable wakeup pin WUPx These bits are set and cleared by software. Note: an additional wakeup event is detected if WUPx pin is enabled (by setting the WUPENx bit) when WUPx pin level is already high when WUPPx selects rising edge, or low when WUPPx selects falling edge.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 08w01 WUPP1 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 09w01 WUPP2 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 10w01 WUPP3 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 11w01 WUPP4 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 12w01 WUPP5 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 13w01 WUPP6 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 14w01 WUPP7 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 15w01 WUPP8 (rw): wakeup pin polarity bit for WUPx These bits define the polarity used for event detection on WUPx external wakeup pin.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 16w02 WUPPUPD1 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 18w02 WUPPUPD2 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 20w02 WUPPUPD3 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 22w02 WUPPUPD4 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 24w02 WUPPUPD5 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 26w02 WUPPUPD6 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 28w02 WUPPUPD7 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020848 C   FIELD 30w02 WUPPUPD8 (rw): wakeup pin pull configuration for WKUPx These bits define the I/O pad pull configuration used when WUPENx = 1. The associated GPIO port pull configuration must be set to the same value or to 00. The wakeup pin pull configuration is kept in Standby mode.
0x54020850 B  REGISTER IORETR: PWR I/O retention register
0x54020850 C   FIELD 00w01 IORETEN (rw): IO retention enable: When entering into standby mode, the output is sampled, and apply to the output IO during the standby power mode. Note: the IO state is not retained if the DBG_STANDBY bit is set in DBGMCU_CR register.
0x54020850 C   FIELD 16w01 JTAGIORETEN (rw): IO retention enable for JTAG IOs when entering into standby mode, the output is sampled, and apply to the output IO during the standby power mode
0x54020900 B  REGISTER SECCFGR: PWR security configuration register
0x54020900 C   FIELD 00w01 WUP1SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 01w01 WUP2SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 02w01 WUP3SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 03w01 WUP4SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 04w01 WUP5SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 05w01 WUP6SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 06w01 WUP7SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 07w01 WUP8SEC (rw): WUPx secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 11w01 RETSEC (rw): retention secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 12w01 LPMSEC (rw): low-power modes secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 13w01 SCMSEC (rw): supply configuration and monitoring secure protection.
0x54020900 C   FIELD 14w01 VBSEC (rw): backup domain secure protection
0x54020900 C   FIELD 15w01 VUSBSEC (rw): voltage USB secure protection
0x54020904 B  REGISTER PRIVCFGR: PWR privilege configuration register
0x54020904 C   FIELD 00w01 SPRIV (rw): PWR secure functions privilege configuration Set and reset by software. This bit can be written only by a secure privileged access.
0x54020904 C   FIELD 01w01 NSPRIV (rw): PWR non-secure functions privilege configuration Set and reset by software. This bit can be written only by privileged access, secure or non-secure.
0x54020C00 A PERIPHERAL SEC_RCC
0x54020C00 B  REGISTER CR: RCC clock control register
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 00w01 HSION (rw): HSI clock enable Set and cleared by software. Set by hardware to force the HSI to ON when the product leaves Stop mode, if STOPWUCK = 1 or STOPKERWUCK = 1. Set by hardware to force the HSI to ON when the product leaves Standby mode or in case of a failure of the HSE which is used as the system clock source. This bit cannot be cleared if the HSI is used directly (via SW mux) as system clock, or if the HSI is selected as reference clock for PLL1 with PLL1 enabled (PLL1ON bit set to 1).
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 01w01 HSIRDY (ro): HSI clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the HSI oscillator is stable.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 02w01 HSIKERON (rw): HSI clock enable in Stop mode Set and reset by software to force the HSI to ON, even in Stop mode, in order to be quickly available as kernel clock for peripherals. This bit has no effect on the value of HSION.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 03w02 HSIDIV (rw): HSI clock divider Set and reset by software. These bits allow selecting a division ratio in order to configure the wanted HSI clock frequency. The HSIDIV cannot be changed if the HSI is selected as reference clock for at least one enabled PLL (PLLxON bit set to 1). In that case, the new HSIDIV value is ignored.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 05w01 HSIDIVF (ro): HSI divider flag Set and reset by hardware. As a write operation to HSIDIV has not an immediate effect on the frequency, this flag indicates the current status of the HSI divider. HSIDIVF goes immediately to 0 when HSIDIV value is changed, and is set back to 1 when the output frequency matches the value programmed into HSIDIV.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 08w01 CSION (rw): CSI clock enable Set and reset by software to enable/disable CSI clock for system and/or peripheral. Set by hardware to force the CSI to ON when the system leaves Stop mode, if STOPWUCK = 1 or STOPKERWUCK = 1. This bit cannot be cleared if the CSI is used directly (via SW mux) as system clock, or if the CSI is selected as reference clock for PLL1 with PLL1 enabled (PLL1ON bit set to 1).
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 09w01 CSIRDY (ro): CSI clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the CSI oscillator is stable. This bit is activated only if the RC is enabled by CSION (it is not activated if the CSI is enabled by CSIKERON or by a peripheral request).
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 10w01 CSIKERON (rw): CSI clock enable in Stop mode Set and reset by software to force the CSI to ON, even in Stop mode, in order to be quickly available as kernel clock for some peripherals. This bit has no effect on the value of CSION.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 12w01 HSI48ON (rw): HSI48 clock enable Set by software and cleared by software or by the hardware when the system enters to Stop or Standby mode.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 13w01 HSI48RDY (ro): HSI48 clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the HSI48 oscillator is stable.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 16w01 HSEON (rw): HSE clock enable Set and cleared by software. Cleared by hardware to stop the HSE when entering Stop or Standby mode. This bit cannot be cleared if the HSE is used directly (via SW mux) as system clock, or if the HSE is selected as reference clock for PLL1 with PLL1 enabled (PLL1ON bit set to 1).
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 17w01 HSERDY (ro): HSE clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the HSE oscillator is stable.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 18w01 HSEBYP (rw): HSE clock bypass Set and cleared by software to bypass the oscillator with an external clock. The external clock must be enabled with the HSEON bit to be used by the device. The HSEBYP bit can be written only if the HSE oscillator is disabled.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 19w01 HSECSSON (rw): HSE clock security system enable Set by software to enable clock security system on HSE. This bit is 'set only' (disabled by a system reset or when the system enters in Standby mode). When HSECSSON is set, the clock detector is enabled by hardware when the HSE is ready and disabled by hardware if an oscillator failure is detected.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 20w01 HSEEXT (rw): external high speed clock type in Bypass mode Set and reset by software to select the external clock type (analog or digital). The external clock must be enabled with the HSEON bit to be used by the device. The HSEEXT bit can be written only if the HSE oscillator is disabled.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 24w01 PLL1ON (rw): PLL1 enable Set and cleared by software to enable PLL1. Cleared by hardware when entering Stop or Standby mode. Note that the hardware prevents writing this bit to 0, if the PLL1 output is used as the system clock.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 25w01 PLL1RDY (ro): PLL1 clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the PLL1 is locked.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 26w01 PLL2ON (rw): PLL2 enable Set and cleared by software to enable PLL2. Cleared by hardware when entering Stop or Standby mode.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 27w01 PLL2RDY (ro): PLL2 clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the PLL is locked.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 28w01 PLL3ON (rw): PLL3 enable Set and cleared by software to enable PLL3. Cleared by hardware when entering Stop or Standby mode.
0x54020C00 C   FIELD 29w01 PLL3RDY (ro): PLL3 clock ready flag Set by hardware to indicate that the PLL3 is locked.
0x54020C10 B  REGISTER HSICFGR: RCC HSI calibration register
0x54020C10 C   FIELD 00w12 HSICAL (ro): HSI clock calibration Set by hardware by option byte loading during system reset nreset. Adjusted by software through trimming bits HSITRIM. This field represents the sum of engineering option byte calibration value and HSITRIM bits value.
0x54020C10 C   FIELD 16w07 HSITRIM (rw): HSI clock trimming Set by software to adjust calibration. HSITRIM field is added to the engineering option bytes loaded during reset phase (FLASH_HSI_OPT) in order to form the calibration trimming value. HSICAL = HSITRIM + FLASH_HSI_OPT. After a change of HSITRIM it takes one system clock cycle before the new HSITRIM value is updated Note: The reset value of the field is 0x40.
0x54020C14 B  REGISTER CRRCR: RCC clock recovery RC register
0x54020C14 C   FIELD 00w10 HSI48CAL (ro): Internal RC 48 MHz clock calibration Set by hardware by option-byte loading during system reset NRESET. Read-only.
0x54020C18 B  REGISTER CSICFGR: RCC CSI calibration register
0x54020C18 C   FIELD 00w08 CSICAL (rw): CSI clock calibration Set by hardware by option byte loading during system reset NRESET. Adjusted by software through trimming bits CSITRIM. This field represents the sum of engineering option byte calibration value and CSITRIM bits value.
0x54020C18 C   FIELD 16w06 CSITRIM (rw): CSI clock trimming Set by software to adjust calibration. CSITRIM field is added to the engineering option bytes loaded during reset phase (FLASH_CSI_OPT) in order to form the calibration trimming value. CSICAL = CSITRIM + FLASH_CSI_OPT. Note: The reset value of the field is 0x20.
0x54020C1C B  REGISTER CFGR1: RCC clock configuration register
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 00w02 SW (rw): system clock and trace clock switch Set and reset by software to select system clock and trace clock sources (sys_ck). Set by hardware in order to: - force the selection of the HSI or CSI (depending on STOPWUCK selection) when leaving a system Stop mode - force the selection of the HSI in case of failure of the HSE when used directly or indirectly as system clock others: reserved
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 03w02 SWS (ro): system clock switch status Set and reset by hardware to indicate which clock source is used as system clock. 000: HSI used as system clock (hsi_ck) (default after reset). others: reserved
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 06w01 STOPWUCK (rw): system clock selection after a wakeup from system Stop Set and reset by software to select the system wakeup clock from system Stop. The selected clock is also used as emergency clock for the clock security system (CSS) on HSE. 0: HSI selected as wakeup clock from system Stop (default after reset) STOPWUCK must not be modified when CSS is enabled (by HSECSSON bit) and the system clock is HSE (SWS = 10) or a switch on HSE is requested (SW =10).
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 07w01 STOPKERWUCK (rw): kernel clock selection after a wakeup from system Stop Set and reset by software to select the kernel wakeup clock from system Stop.
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 08w06 RTCPRE (rw): HSE division factor for RTC clock Set and cleared by software to divide the HSE to generate a clock for RTC. Caution: The software must set these bits correctly to ensure that the clock supplied to the RTC is lower than 1 MHz. These bits must be configured if needed before selecting the RTC clock source. ...
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 15w01 TIMPRE (rw): timers clocks prescaler selection This bit is set and reset by software to control the clock frequency of all the timers connected to APB1 and APB2 domains.
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 18w04 MCO1PRE (rw): MCO1 prescaler Set and cleared by software to configure the prescaler of the MCO1. Modification of this prescaler may generate glitches on MCO1. It is highly recommended to change this prescaler only after reset, before enabling the external oscillators and the PLLs. ...
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 22w03 MCO1SEL (rw): Microcontroller clock output 1 Set and cleared by software. Clock source selection may generate glitches on MCO1. It is highly recommended to configure these bits only after reset, before enabling the external oscillators and the PLLs. others: reserved
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 25w04 MCO2PRE (rw): MCO2 prescaler Set and cleared by software to configure the prescaler of the MCO2. Modification of this prescaler may generate glitches on MCO2. It is highly recommended to change this prescaler only after reset, before enabling the external oscillators and the PLLs. ...
0x54020C1C C   FIELD 29w03 MCO2SEL (rw): microcontroller clock output 2 Set and cleared by software. Clock source selection may generate glitches on MCO2. It is highly recommended to configure these bits only after reset, before enabling the external oscillators and the PLLs. others: reserved
0x54020C20 B  REGISTER CFGR2: RCC CPU domain clock configuration register 2
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 00w04 HPRE (rw): AHB prescaler Set and reset by software to control the division factor of rcc_hclk. Changing this division ratio has an impact on the frequency of all bus matrix clocks 0xxx: rcc_hclk = sys_ck (default after reset)
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 04w03 PPRE1 (rw): APB low-speed prescaler (APB1) Set and reset by software to control the division factor of rcc_pclk1. The clock is divided by the new prescaler factor from 1 to 16 cycles of rcc_hclk after PPRE write. 0xx: rcc_pclk1 = rcc_hclk1 (default after reset)
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 08w03 PPRE2 (rw): APB high-speed prescaler (APB2) Set and reset by software to control APB high-speed clocks division factor. The clocks are divided with the new prescaler factor from 1 to 16 APB cycles after PPRE2 write. 0xx: rcc_pclk2 = rcc_hclk1
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 12w03 PPRE3 (rw): APB low-speed prescaler (APB3) Set and reset by software to control APB low-speed clocks division factor. The clocks are divided with the new prescaler factor from 1 to 16 APB cycles after PPRE3 write. 0xx: rcc_pclk3 = rcc_hclk1
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 16w01 AHB1DIS (rw): AHB1 clock disable This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the AHB1 peripherals from RCC_AHB1ENR are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_AHB1ENR. When this bit is set, all the AHB1 peripherals clocks from RCC_AHB1ENR are off. enable control bits
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 17w01 AHB2DIS (rw): AHB2 clock disable This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the AHB2 peripherals from RCC_AHB2ENR are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_AHB2ENR. When this bit is set, all the AHB2 peripherals clocks from RCC_AHB2ENR are off. enable control bits
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 19w01 AHB4DIS (rw): AHB4 clock disable This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the AHB4 peripherals from RCC_AHB4ENR are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_AHB4ENR. When this bit is set, all the AHB4 peripherals clocks from RCC_AHB4ENR are off. enable control bits
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 20w01 APB1DIS (rw): APB1 clock disable value This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the APB1 peripherals (except IWDG) are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_APB1ENR. When this bit is set, all the APB1 peripherals clocks are off, except for IWDG. control bits
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 21w01 APB2DIS (rw): APB2 clock disable value This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the APB2 peripherals are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_APB2ENR. When this bit is set, all the APB2 peripherals clocks are off. control bits
0x54020C20 C   FIELD 22w01 APB3DIS (rw): APB3 clock disable value.Set and cleared by software This bit can be set in order to further reduce power consumption, when none of the APB3 peripherals are used and when their clocks are disabled in RCC_APB3ENR. When this bit is set, all the APB3 peripherals clocks are off. control bits
0x54020C28 B  REGISTER PLL1CFGR: RCC PLL clock source selection register
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 00w02 PLL1SRC (rw): DIVMx and PLLs clock source selection Set and reset by software to select the PLL clock source. These bits can be written only when all PLLs are disabled. In order to save power, when no PLL is used, the value of PLL1SRC must be set to '00'. 00: no clock send to DIVMx divider and PLLs (default after reset).
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 02w02 PLL1RGE (rw): PLL1 input frequency range Set and reset by software to select the proper reference frequency range used for PLL1. This bit must be written before enabling the PLL1.
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 04w01 PLL1FRACEN (rw): PLL1 fractional latch enable Set and reset by software to latch the content of FRACN1 into the sigma-delta modulator. In order to latch the FRACN1 value into the sigma-delta modulator, PLL1FRACEN must be set to 0, then set to 1. The transition 0 to 1 transfers the content of FRACN1 into the modulator.
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 05w01 PLL1VCOSEL (rw): PLL1 VCO selection Set and reset by software to select the proper VCO frequency range used for PLL1. This bit must be written before enabling the PLL1.
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 08w06 PLL1M (rw): prescaler for PLL1 Set and cleared by software to configure the prescaler of the PLL1. The hardware does not allow any modification of this prescaler when PLL1 is enabled (PLL1ON = 1 or PLL1RDY = 1). In order to save power when PLL1 is not used, the value of DIVM1 must be set to 0. ... ...
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 16w01 PLL1PEN (rw): PLL1 DIVP divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll1_p_ck output of the PLL1. This bit can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0). In order to save power, when the pll1_p_ck output of the PLL1 is not used, the pll1_p_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 17w01 PLL1QEN (rw): PLL1 DIVQ divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll1_q_ck output of the PLL1. In order to save power, when the pll1_q_ck output of the PLL1 is not used, the pll1_q_ck must be disabled. This bit can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0).
0x54020C28 C   FIELD 18w01 PLL1REN (rw): PLL1 DIVR divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll1_r_ck output of the PLL1. To save power, DIVR1EN and DIVR1 bits must be set to 0 when the pll1_r_ck is not used. This bit can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0).
0x54020C2C B  REGISTER PLL2CFGR: RCC PLL clock source selection register
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 00w02 PLL2SRC (rw): DIVMx and PLLs clock source selection Set and reset by software to select the PLL clock source. These bits can be written only when all PLLs are disabled. In order to save power, when no PLL is used, the value of PLL2SRC must be set to '00'.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 02w02 PLL2RGE (rw): PLL2 input frequency range Set and reset by software to select the proper reference frequency range used for PLL2. These bits must be written before enabling the PLL2.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 04w01 PLL2FRACEN (rw): PLL2 fractional latch enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll2_p_ck output of the PLL2. To save power, when the pll2_p_ck output of the PLL2 is not used, the pll2_p_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 05w01 PLL2VCOSEL (rw): PLL2 VCO selection Set and reset by software to select the proper VCO frequency range used for PLL2. This bit must be written before enabling the PLL2.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 08w06 PLL2M (rw): prescaler for PLL2 Set and cleared by software to configure the prescaler of the PLL2. The hardware does not allow any modification of this prescaler when PLL2 is enabled (PLL2ON = 1 or PLL2RDY = 1). In order to save power when PLL2 is not used, the value of DIVM2 must be set to 0. ... ...
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 16w01 PLL2PEN (rw): PLL2 DIVP divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll2_p_ck output of the PLL2. To save power, when the pll2_p_ck output of the PLL2 is not used, the pll2_p_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 17w01 PLL2QEN (rw): PLL2 DIVQ divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll2_q_ck output of the PLL2. To save power, when the pll2_q_ck output of the PLL2 is not used, the pll2_q_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C2C C   FIELD 18w01 PLL2REN (rw): PLL2 DIVR divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll2_r_ck output of the PLL2. To save power, DIVR2EN and DIVR2 bits must be set to 0 when the pll2_r_ck is not used.
0x54020C30 B  REGISTER PLL3CFGR: RCC PLL clock source selection register
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 00w02 PLL3SRC (rw): DIVMx and PLLs clock source selection Set and reset by software to select the PLL clock source. These bits can be written only when all PLLs are disabled. In order to save power, when no PLL is used, the value of PLL3SRC must be set to '00'.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 02w02 PLL3RGE (rw): PLL3 input frequency range Set and reset by software to select the proper reference frequency range used for PLL3. This bit must be written before enabling the PLL3.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 04w01 PLL3FRACEN (rw): PLL3 fractional latch enable Set and reset by software to latch the content of FRACN3 into the sigma-delta modulator. In order to latch the FRACN3 value into the sigma-delta modulator, PLL3FRACEN must be set to 0, then set to 1. The transition 0 to 1 transfers the content of FRACN3 into the modulator.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 05w01 PLL3VCOSEL (rw): PLL3 VCO selection Set and reset by software to select the proper VCO frequency range used for PLL3. This bit must be written before enabling the PLL3.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 08w06 PLL3M (rw): prescaler for PLL3 Set and cleared by software to configure the prescaler of the PLL3. The hardware does not allow any modification of this prescaler when PLL3 is enabled (PLL3ON = 1 or PLL3RDY = 1). In order to save power when PLL3 is not used, the value of DIVM2 must be set to 0. ... ...
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 16w01 PLL3PEN (rw): PLL3 DIVP divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll3_p_ck output of the PLL3. To save power, when the pll3_p_ck output of the PLL3 is not used, the pll3_p_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 17w01 PLL3QEN (rw): PLL3 DIVQ divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll3_q_ck output of the PLL3. To save power, when the pll3_q_ck output of the PLL3 is not used, the pll3_q_ck must be disabled.
0x54020C30 C   FIELD 18w01 PLL3REN (rw): PLL3 DIVR divider output enable Set and reset by software to enable the pll3_r_ck output of the PLL3. To save power, DIVR2EN and DIVR2 bits must be set to 0 when the pll3_r_ck is not used.
0x54020C34 B  REGISTER PLL1DIVR: RCC PLL1 dividers register
0x54020C34 C   FIELD 00w09 PLL1N (rw): Multiplication factor for PLL1VCO Set and reset by software to control the multiplication factor of the VCO. These bits can be written only when the PLL is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0). ... ... Others: reserved
0x54020C34 C   FIELD 09w07 PLL1P (rw): PLL1 DIVP division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll1_p_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0). Note that odd division factors are not allowed. ...
0x54020C34 C   FIELD 16w07 PLL1Q (rw): PLL1 DIVQ division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll1_q_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0). ...
0x54020C34 C   FIELD 24w07 PLL1R (rw): PLL1 DIVR division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll1_r_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL1ON = 0 and PLL1RDY = 0). ...
0x54020C38 B  REGISTER PLL1FRACR: RCC PLL1 fractional divider register
0x54020C38 C   FIELD 03w13 PLL1FRACN (rw): fractional part of the multiplication factor for PLL1 VCO Set and reset by software to control the fractional part of the multiplication factor of the VCO. These bits can be written at any time, allowing dynamic fine-tuning of the PLL1 VCO. The software must set correctly these bits to insure that the VCO output frequency is between its valid frequency range, that is: * 128 to 560 MHz if PLL1VCOSEL = 0 * 150 to 420 MHz if PLL1VCOSEL = 1 VCO output frequency = Fref1_ck x (PLL1N + (PLL1FRACN / 213)), with * PLL1N between 8 and 420 * PLL1FRACN can be between 0 and 213- 1 * The input frequency Fref1_ck must be between 1 and 16 MHz. To change the PLL1FRACN value on-the-fly even if the PLL is enabled, the application must proceed as follows: * Set the bit PLL1FRACEN to 0 * Write the new fractional value into PLL1FRACN * Set the bit PLL1FRACEN to 1
0x54020C3C B  REGISTER PLL2DIVR: RCC PLL1 dividers register
0x54020C3C C   FIELD 00w09 PLL2N (rw): Multiplication factor for PLL2VCO Set and reset by software to control the multiplication factor of the VCO. These bits can be written only when the PLL is disabled (PLL2ON = 0 and PLL2RDY = 0). ... ... Others: reserved
0x54020C3C C   FIELD 09w07 PLL2P (rw): PLL2 DIVP division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll2_p_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL2 is disabled (PLL2ON = 0 and PLL2RDY = 0). ...
0x54020C3C C   FIELD 16w07 PLL2Q (rw): PLL2 DIVQ division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll2_q_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL2 is disabled (PLL2ON = 0 and PLL2RDY = 0). ...
0x54020C3C C   FIELD 24w07 PLL2R (rw): PLL2 DIVR division factor Set and reset by software to control the frequency of the pll2_r_ck clock. These bits can be written only when the PLL1 is disabled (PLL2ON = 0 and PLL2RDY = 0). ...
0x54020C40 B  REGISTER PLL2FRACR: RCC PLL2 fractional divider register
0x54020C40 C   FIELD 03w13 PLL2FRACN (rw): fractional part of the multiplication factor for PLL2 VCO Set and reset by software to control the fractional part of the multiplication factor of the VCO. These bits can be written at any time, allowing dynamic fine-tuning of the PLL2 VCO. The software must set correctly these bits to insure that the VCO output frequency is between its valid frequency range, that is: * 128 to 560 MHz if PLL2VCOSEL = 0 * 150 to 420 MHz if PLL2VCOSEL = 1 VCO output frequency = Fref2_ck x (PLL2N + (PLL2FRACN / 213)), with * PLL2N between 8 and 420 * PLL2FRACN can be between 0 and 213- 1 * The input frequency Fref2_ck must be between 1 and 16 MHz. To change the PLL2FRACN value on-the-fly even if the PLL is enabled, the application must proceed as follows: * Set the bit PLL2FRACEN to 0 * Write the new fractional value into PLL2FRACN * Set the bit PLL2FRACEN to 1
