0x54020CE4 C   FIELD 26w02 I3C2SEL (rw): I3C2 kernel clock source selection
0x54020CE8 B  REGISTER CCIPR5: RCC kernel clock configuration register
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 00w03 ADCDACSEL (rw): ADC and DAC kernel clock source selection others: reserved, the kernel clock is disabled
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 03w01 DACSEL (rw): DAC hold clock
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 04w02 RNGSEL (rw): RNG kernel clock source selection
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 06w02 CECSEL (rw): HSMI-CEC kernel clock source selection
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 08w02 FDCANSEL (rw): FDCAN kernel clock source selection
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 16w03 SAI1SEL (rw): SAI1 kernel clock source selection others: reserved, the kernel clock is disabled
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 19w03 SAI2SEL (rw): SAI2 kernel clock source selection others: reserved, the kernel clock is disabled
0x54020CE8 C   FIELD 30w02 CKPERSEL (rw): per_ck clock source selection
0x54020CF0 B  REGISTER BDCR: RCC Backup domain control register
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 00w01 LSEON (rw): LSE oscillator enabled Set and reset by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 01w01 LSERDY (rw): LSE oscillator ready Set and reset by hardware to indicate when the LSE is stable. This bit needs 6 cycles of lse_ck clock to fall down after LSEON has been set to 0.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 02w01 LSEBYP (rw): LSE oscillator bypass Set and reset by software to bypass oscillator in debug mode. This bit must not be written when the LSE is enabled (by LSEON) or ready (LSERDY = 1)
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 03w02 LSEDRV (rw): LSE oscillator driving capability Set by software to select the driving capability of the LSE oscillator. These bit can be written only if LSE oscillator is disabled (LSEON = 0 and LSERDY = 0).
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 05w01 LSECSSON (rw): LSE clock security system enable Set by software to enable the clock security system on 32 kHz oscillator. LSECSSON must be enabled after LSE is enabled (LSEON enabled) and ready (LSERDY set by hardware) and after RTCSEL is selected. Once enabled, this bit cannot be disabled, except after a LSE failure detection (LSECSSD = 1). In that case the software must disable LSECSSON.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 06w01 LSECSSD (rw): LSE clock security system failure detection Set by hardware to indicate when a failure has been detected by the clock security system on the external 32 kHz oscillator.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 07w01 LSEEXT (rw): low-speed external clock type in bypass mode Set and reset by software to select the external clock type (analog or digital). The external clock must be enabled with the LSEON bit, to be used by the device. The LSEEXT bit can be written only if the LSE oscillator is disabled.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 08w02 RTCSEL (rw): RTC clock source selection Set by software to select the clock source for the RTC. These bits can be written only one time (except in case of failure detection on LSE). These bits must be written before LSECSSON is enabled. The VSWRST bit can be used to reset them, then it can be written one time again. If HSE is selected as RTC clock, this clock is lost when the system is in Stop mode or in case of a pin reset (NRST).
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 15w01 RTCEN (rw): RTC clock enable Set and reset by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 16w01 VSWRST (rw): VSwitch domain software reset Set and reset by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 24w01 LSCOEN (rw): Low-speed clock output (LSCO) enable Set and cleared by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 25w01 LSCOSEL (rw): Low-speed clock output selection Set and cleared by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 26w01 LSION (rw): LSI oscillator enable Set and cleared by software.
0x54020CF0 C   FIELD 27w01 LSIRDY (rw): LSI oscillator ready Set and cleared by hardware to indicate when the LSI oscillator is stable. After the LSION bit is cleared, LSIRDY goes low after three internal low-speed oscillator clock cycles. This bit is set when the LSI is used by IWDG or RTC, even if LSION = 0.
0x54020CF4 B  REGISTER RSR: RCC reset status register
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 23w01 RMVF (rw): remove reset flag Set and reset by software to reset the value of the reset flags.
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 26w01 PINRSTF (rw): pin reset flag (NRST) Reset by software by writing the RMVF bit. Set by hardware when a reset from pin occurs.
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 27w01 BORRSTF (rw): BOR reset flag Reset by software by writing the RMVF bit. Set by hardware when a BOR reset occurs (pwr_bor_rst).
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 28w01 SFTRSTF (rw): system reset from CPU reset flag Reset by software by writing the RMVF bit. Set by hardware when the system reset is due to CPU.The CPU can generate a system reset by writing SYSRESETREQ bit of AIRCR register of the core M33.
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 29w01 IWDGRSTF (rw): independent watchdog reset flag Reset by software by writing the RMVF bit. Set by hardware when an independent watchdog reset occurs.
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 30w01 WWDGRSTF (rw): window watchdog reset flag Reset by software by writing the RMVF bit. Set by hardware when a window watchdog reset occurs.
0x54020CF4 C   FIELD 31w01 LPWRRSTF (rw): Low-power reset flag Set by hardware when a reset occurs due to Stop or Standby mode entry, whereas the corresponding nRST_STOP, nRST_STBY option bit is cleared. Cleared by writing to the RMVF bit.
0x54020D10 B  REGISTER SECCFGR: RCC secure configuration register
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 00w01 HSISEC (rw): HSI clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 01w01 HSESEC (rw): HSE clock configuration bits, status bits and HSE_CSS security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 02w01 CSISEC (rw): CSI clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 03w01 LSISEC (rw): LSI clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 04w01 LSESEC (rw): LSE clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 05w01 SYSCLKSEC (rw): SYSCLK clock selection, STOPWUCK bit, clock output on MCO configuration security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 06w01 PRESCSEC (rw): AHBx/APBx prescaler configuration bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 07w01 PLL1SEC (rw): PLL1 clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 08w01 PLL2SEC (rw): PLL2 clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 09w01 PLL3SEC (rw): PLL3 clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 11w01 HSI48SEC (rw): HSI48 clock configuration and status bits security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 12w01 RMVFSEC (rw): Remove reset flag security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D10 C   FIELD 13w01 CKPERSELSEC (rw): per_ck selection security Set and reset by software.
0x54020D14 B  REGISTER PRIVCFGR: RCC privilege configuration register
0x54020D14 C   FIELD 00w01 SPRIV (rw): RCC secure functions privilege configuration Set and reset by software. This bit can be written only by a secure privileged access.
0x54020D14 C   FIELD 01w01 NSPRIV (rw): RCC non-secure functions privilege configuration Set and reset by software. This bit can be written only by privileged access, secure or non-secure.
0x54022000 A PERIPHERAL SEC_EXTI
0x54022000 B  REGISTER RTSR1: EXTI rising trigger selection register
0x54022000 C   FIELD 00w01 RT0 (rw): Rising trigger event configuration bit of configurable event input x When EXTI_SECCFGR.SECx is disabled, RTx can be accessed with non-secure and secure access. When EXTI_SECCFGR.SECx is enabled, RTx can only be accessed with secure access. Non-secure write to this bit x is discarded and non-secure read returns 0. When EXTI_PRIVCFGR.PRIVx is disabled, RTx can be accessed with unprivileged and privileged access. When EXTI_PRIVCFGR.PRIVx is enabled, RTx can only be accessed with privileged access. Unprivileged write to this bit x is discarded, unprivileged read returns 0.
