0x57000540 B  REGISTER SDCR1: SDRAM control registers 1
0x57000540 C   FIELD 00w02 NC (rw): Number of column address bits These bits define the number of bits of a column address.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 02w02 NR (rw): Number of row address bits These bits define the number of bits of a row address.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 04w02 MWID (rw): Memory data bus width. These bits define the memory device width.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 06w01 NB (rw): Number of internal banks This bit sets the number of internal banks.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 07w02 CAS (rw): CAS Latency This bits sets the SDRAM CAS latency in number of memory clock cycles
0x57000540 C   FIELD 09w01 WP (rw): Write protection This bit enables write mode access to the SDRAM bank.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 10w02 SDCLK (rw): SDRAM clock configuration These bits define the SDRAM clock period for both SDRAM banks and allow disabling the clock before changing the frequency. In this case the SDRAM must be re-initialized. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are don't care.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 12w01 RBURST (rw): Burst read This bit enables Burst read mode. The SDRAM controller anticipates the next read commands during the CAS latency and stores data in the Read FIFO. Note: The corresponding bit in the FMC_SDCR2 register is don't care.
0x57000540 C   FIELD 13w02 RPIPE (rw): Read pipe These bits define the delay, in clock cycles, for reading data after CAS latency. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register is read only.
0x57000544 B  REGISTER SDCR2: SDRAM control registers 2
0x57000544 C   FIELD 00w02 NC (=FMC.SDCR1.NC) (rw): Number of column address bits These bits define the number of bits of a column address.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 02w02 NR (=FMC.SDCR1.NR) (rw): Number of row address bits These bits define the number of bits of a row address.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 04w02 MWID (=FMC.SDCR1.MWID) (rw): Memory data bus width. These bits define the memory device width.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 06w01 NB (=FMC.SDCR1.NB) (rw): Number of internal banks This bit sets the number of internal banks.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 07w02 CAS (=FMC.SDCR1.CAS) (rw): CAS Latency This bits sets the SDRAM CAS latency in number of memory clock cycles
0x57000544 C   FIELD 09w01 WP (=FMC.SDCR1.WP) (rw): Write protection This bit enables write mode access to the SDRAM bank.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 10w02 SDCLK (=FMC.SDCR1.SDCLK) (rw): SDRAM clock configuration These bits define the SDRAM clock period for both SDRAM banks and allow disabling the clock before changing the frequency. In this case the SDRAM must be re-initialized. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register are don't care.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 12w01 RBURST (rw): Burst read This bit enables Burst read mode. The SDRAM controller anticipates the next read commands during the CAS latency and stores data in the Read FIFO. Note: The corresponding bit in the FMC_SDCR2 register is don't care.
0x57000544 C   FIELD 13w02 RPIPE (rw): Read pipe These bits define the delay, in clock cycles, for reading data after CAS latency. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDCR2 register is read only.
0x57000548 B  REGISTER SDTR1: SDRAM timing registers 1
0x57000548 C   FIELD 00w04 TMRD (rw): Load Mode Register to Active These bits define the delay between a Load Mode Register command and an Active or Refresh command in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x57000548 C   FIELD 04w04 TXSR (rw): Exit Self-refresh delay These bits define the delay from releasing the Self-refresh command to issuing the Activate command in number of memory clock cycles. .... Note: If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 must be programmed with the same TXSR timing corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
0x57000548 C   FIELD 08w04 TRAS (rw): Self refresh time These bits define the minimum Self-refresh period in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x57000548 C   FIELD 12w04 TRC (rw): Row cycle delay These bits define the delay between the Refresh command and the Activate command, as well as the delay between two consecutive Refresh commands. It is expressed in number of memory clock cycles. The TRC timing is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRC must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device. .... Note: TRC must match the TRC and TRFC (Auto Refresh period) timings defined in the SDRAM device datasheet. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDTR2 register are don't care.
0x57000548 C   FIELD 16w04 TWR (rw): Recovery delay These bits define the delay between a Write and a Precharge command in number of memory clock cycles. .... Note: TWR must be programmed to match the write recovery time (tsub WR/sub ) defined in the SDRAM datasheet, and to guarantee that: Note: TWR greater than or equal TRASTRCD and TWR greater than or equalTRCTRCDTRP Note: Example: TRAS= 4 cycles, TRCD= 2 cycles. So, TWR = 2 cycles. TWR must be programmed to 0x1. Note: If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 must be programmed with the same TWR timing corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device. Note: If only one SDRAM device is used, the TWR timing must be kept at reset value (0xF) for the not used bank.
0x57000548 C   FIELD 20w04 TRP (rw): Row precharge delay These bits define the delay between a Precharge command and another command in number of memory clock cycles. The TRP timing is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRP must be programmed with the timing of the slowest device. .... Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDTR2 register are don't care.
0x57000548 C   FIELD 24w04 TRCD (rw): Row to column delay These bits define the delay between the Activate command and a Read/Write command in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x5700054C B  REGISTER SDTR2: SDRAM timing registers 2
0x5700054C C   FIELD 00w04 TMRD (rw): Load Mode Register to Active These bits define the delay between a Load Mode Register command and an Active or Refresh command in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x5700054C C   FIELD 04w04 TXSR (rw): Exit Self-refresh delay These bits define the delay from releasing the Self-refresh command to issuing the Activate command in number of memory clock cycles. .... Note: If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 must be programmed with the same TXSR timing corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device.
0x5700054C C   FIELD 08w04 TRAS (rw): Self refresh time These bits define the minimum Self-refresh period in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x5700054C C   FIELD 12w04 TRC (rw): Row cycle delay These bits define the delay between the Refresh command and the Activate command, as well as the delay between two consecutive Refresh commands. It is expressed in number of memory clock cycles. The TRC timing is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRC must be programmed with the timings of the slowest device. .... Note: TRC must match the TRC and TRFC (Auto Refresh period) timings defined in the SDRAM device datasheet. Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDTR2 register are don't care.
0x5700054C C   FIELD 16w04 TWR (rw): Recovery delay These bits define the delay between a Write and a Precharge command in number of memory clock cycles. .... Note: TWR must be programmed to match the write recovery time (tsub WR/sub ) defined in the SDRAM datasheet, and to guarantee that: Note: TWR greater than or equal TRASTRCD and TWR greater than or equalTRCTRCDTRP Note: Example: TRAS= 4 cycles, TRCD= 2 cycles. So, TWR = 2 cycles. TWR must be programmed to 0x1. Note: If two SDRAM devices are used, the FMC_SDTR1 and FMC_SDTR2 must be programmed with the same TWR timing corresponding to the slowest SDRAM device. Note: If only one SDRAM device is used, the TWR timing must be kept at reset value (0xF) for the not used bank.
0x5700054C C   FIELD 20w04 TRP (rw): Row precharge delay These bits define the delay between a Precharge command and another command in number of memory clock cycles. The TRP timing is only configured in the FMC_SDTR1 register. If two SDRAM devices are used, the TRP must be programmed with the timing of the slowest device. .... Note: The corresponding bits in the FMC_SDTR2 register are don't care.
0x5700054C C   FIELD 24w04 TRCD (rw): Row to column delay These bits define the delay between the Activate command and a Read/Write command in number of memory clock cycles. ....
0x57000550 B  REGISTER SDCMR: SDRAM Command Mode register
0x57000550 C   FIELD 00w03 MODE (rw): Command mode These bits define the command issued to the SDRAM device. Note: When a command is issued, at least one Command Target Bank bit ( CTB1 or CTB2) must be set otherwise the command will be ignored. Note: If two SDRAM banks are used, the Auto-refresh and PALL command must be issued simultaneously to the two devices with CTB1 and CTB2 bits set otherwise the command will be ignored. Note: If only one SDRAM bank is used and a command is issued with it's associated CTB bit set, the other CTB bit of the the unused bank must be kept to 0.
0x57000550 C   FIELD 03w01 CTB2 (rw): Command Target Bank 2 This bit indicates whether the command will be issued to SDRAM Bank 2 or not.
0x57000550 C   FIELD 04w01 CTB1 (rw): Command Target Bank 1 This bit indicates whether the command will be issued to SDRAM Bank 1 or not.
0x57000550 C   FIELD 05w04 NRFS (rw): Number of Auto-refresh These bits define the number of consecutive Auto-refresh commands issued when MODE = '011'. ....
0x57000550 C   FIELD 09w13 MRD (rw): Mode Register definition This 13-bit field defines the SDRAM Mode Register content. The Mode Register is programmed using the Load Mode Register command.
0x57000554 B  REGISTER SDRTR: SDRAM refresh timer register
0x57000554 C   FIELD 00w01 CRE (wo): Clear Refresh error flag This bit is used to clear the Refresh Error Flag (RE) in the Status Register.
0x57000554 C   FIELD 01w13 COUNT (rw): Refresh Timer Count This 13-bit field defines the refresh rate of the SDRAM device. It is expressed in number of memory clock cycles. It must be set at least to 41 SDRAM clock cycles (0x29). Refresh rate = (COUNT + 1) x SDRAM frequency clock COUNT = (SDRAM refresh period / Number of rows)20
0x57000554 C   FIELD 14w01 REIE (rw): RES Interrupt Enable
0x57000558 B  REGISTER SDSR: SDRAM status register
0x57000558 C   FIELD 00w01 RE (ro): Refresh error flag An interrupt is generated if REIE = 1 and RE = 1
0x57000558 C   FIELD 01w02 MODES1 (ro): Status Mode for Bank 1 This bit defines the Status Mode of SDRAM Bank 1.
0x57000558 C   FIELD 03w02 MODES2 (ro): Status Mode for Bank 2 This bit defines the Status Mode of SDRAM Bank 2.
0x57000558 C   FIELD 05w01 BUSY (ro): Busy status This bit defines the status of the SDRAM controller after a Command Mode request 1; SDRAM Controller is not ready to accept a new request
0x57001400 A PERIPHERAL SEC_OCTOSPI
0x57001400 B  REGISTER CR: OCTOSPI control register
0x57001400 C   FIELD 00w01 EN (rw): Enable This bit enables the OCTOSPI. Note: The DMA request can be aborted without having received the ACK in case this EN bit is cleared during the operation. In case this bit is set to 0 during a DMA transfer, the REQ signal to DMA returns to inactive state without waiting for the ACK signal from DMA to be active.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 01w01 ABORT (rw): Abort request This bit aborts the ongoing command sequence. It is automatically reset once the abort is completed. This bit stops the current transfer. Note: This bit is always read as 0.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 02w01 DMAEN (rw): DMA enable In Indirect mode, the DMA can be used to input or output data via OCTOSPI_DR. DMA transfers are initiated when FTF is set. Note: Resetting the DMAEN bit while a DMA transfer is ongoing, breaks the handshake with the DMA. Do not write this bit during DMA operation.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 03w01 TCEN (rw): Timeout counter enable This bit is valid only when the Memory-mapped mode (FMODE[1:0] = 11) is selected. This bit enables the timeout counter.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 06w01 DMM (rw): Dual-memory configuration This bit activates the dual-memory configuration, where two external devices are used simultaneously to double the throughput and the capacity
0x57001400 C   FIELD 07w01 MSEL (rw): External memory select
0x57001400 C   FIELD 08w05 FTHRES (rw): FIFO threshold level This field defines, in Indirect mode, the threshold number of bytes in the FIFO that causes the FIFO threshold flag FTF in OCTOSPI_SR, to be set. ... Note: If DMAEN = 1, the DMA controller for the corresponding channel must be disabled before changing the FTHRES[4:0] value.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 16w01 TEIE (rw): Transfer error interrupt enable This bit enables the transfer error interrupt.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 17w01 TCIE (rw): Transfer complete interrupt enable This bit enables the transfer complete interrupt.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 18w01 FTIE (rw): FIFO threshold interrupt enable This bit enables the FIFO threshold interrupt.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 19w01 SMIE (rw): Status match interrupt enable This bit enables the status match interrupt.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 20w01 TOIE (rw): Timeout interrupt enable This bit enables the timeout interrupt.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 22w01 APMS (rw): Automatic status-polling mode stop This bit determines if the Automatic status-polling mode is stopped after a match.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 23w01 PMM (rw): Polling match mode This bit indicates which method must be used to determine a match during the Automatic status-polling mode.
0x57001400 C   FIELD 28w02 FMODE (rw): Functional mode This field defines the OCTOSPI functional mode of operation. If DMAEN = 1 already, then the DMA controller for the corresponding channel must be disabled before changing the FMODE[1:0] value. If FMODE[1:0] and FTHRES[4:0] are wrongly updated while DMAEN = 1, the DMA request signal automatically goes to inactive state.
0x57001408 B  REGISTER DCR1: OCTOSPI device configuration register 1
0x57001408 C   FIELD 00w01 CKMODE (rw): Mode 0/Mode 3 This bit indicates the level taken by the CLK between commands (when NCS = 1).
0x57001408 C   FIELD 01w01 FRCK (rw): Free running clock This bit configures the free running clock.
0x57001408 C   FIELD 03w01 DLYBYP (rw): Delay block bypass
0x57001408 C   FIELD 08w06 CSHT (rw): Chip-select high time CSHT + 1 defines the minimum number of CLK cycles where the chip-select (NCS) must remain high between commands issued to the external device. ...
0x57001408 C   FIELD 16w05 DEVSIZE (rw): Device size This field defines the size of the external device using the following formula: Number of bytes in device = 2[DEVSIZE+1]. DEVSIZE+1 is effectively the number of address bits required to address the external device. The device capacity can be up to 4 Gbytes (addressed using 32-bits) in Indirect mode, but the addressable space in Memory-mapped mode is limited to 256 Mbytes. In Regular-command protocol, if DMM = 1, DEVSIZE[4:0] indicates the total capacity of the two devices together.
0x57001408 C   FIELD 24w03 MTYP (rw): Memory type This bit indicates the type of memory to be supported. Note: In this mode, DQS signal polarity is inverted with respect to the memory clock signal. This is the default value and care must be taken to change MTYP[2:0] for memories different from Micron. Others: Reserved
0x5700140C B  REGISTER DCR2: OCTOSPI device configuration register 2
0x5700140C C   FIELD 00w08 PRESCALER (rw): Clock prescaler This field defines the scaler factor for generating the CLK based on the kernel clock (value + 1). 2: FCLK = FKERNEL/3 ... 255: FCLK = FKERNEL/256 For odd clock division factors, the CLK duty cycle is not 50 %. The clock signal remains low one cycle longer than it stays high.
0x5700140C C   FIELD 16w03 WRAPSIZE (rw): Wrap size This field indicates the wrap size to which the memory is configured. For memories which have a separate command for wrapped instructions, this field indicates the wrap-size associated with the command held in the OCTOSPI1_WPIR register. 110-111: Reserved
0x57001410 B  REGISTER DCR3: OCTOSPI device configuration register 3
0x57001410 C   FIELD 16w05 CSBOUND (rw): NCS boundary This field enables the transaction boundary feature. When active, a minimum value of 3 is recommended. The NCS is released on each boundary of 2CSBOUND bytes. others: NCS boundary set to 2CSBOUND bytes
0x57001414 B  REGISTER DCR4: OCTOSPI device configuration register 4
0x57001414 C   FIELD 00w32 REFRESH (rw): Refresh rate This field enables the refresh rate feature. The NCS is released every REFRESH + 1 clock cycles for writes, and REFRESH + 4 clock cycles for reads. Note: These two values can be extended with few clock cycles when refresh occurs during a byte transmission in Single-, Dual- or Quad-SPI mode, because the byte transmission must be completed. others: Maximum communication length is set to REFRESH + 1 clock cycles.
0x57001420 B  REGISTER SR: OCTOSPI status register
0x57001420 C   FIELD 00w01 TEF (ro): Transfer error flag This bit is set in Indirect mode when an invalid address is being accessed in Indirect mode. It is cleared by writing 1 to CTEF.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 01w01 TCF (ro): Transfer complete flag This bit is set in Indirect mode when the programmed number of data has been transferred or in any mode when the transfer has been aborted.It is cleared by writing 1 to CTCF.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 02w01 FTF (ro): FIFO threshold flag In Indirect mode, this bit is set when the FIFO threshold has been reached, or if there is any data left in the FIFO after the reads from the external device are complete. It is cleared automatically as soon as the threshold condition is no longer true. In Automatic status-polling mode, this bit is set every time the status register is read, and the bit is cleared when the data register is read.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 03w01 SMF (ro): Status match flag This bit is set in Automatic status-polling mode when the unmasked received data matches the corresponding bits in the match register (OCTOSPI_PSMAR). It is cleared by writing 1 to CSMF.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 04w01 TOF (ro): Timeout flag This bit is set when timeout occurs. It is cleared by writing 1 to CTOF.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 05w01 BUSY (ro): Busy This bit is set when an operation is ongoing. It is cleared automatically when the operation with the external device is finished and the FIFO is empty.
0x57001420 C   FIELD 08w06 FLEVEL (ro): FIFO level This field gives the number of valid bytes that are being held in the FIFO. FLEVEL = 0 when the FIFO is empty, and 32 when it is full. In Automatic status-polling mode, FLEVEL is zero.
0x57001424 B  REGISTER FCR: OCTOSPI flag clear register
0x57001424 C   FIELD 00w01 CTEF (wo): Clear transfer error flag Writing 1 clears the TEF flag in the OCTOSPI_SR register.
0x57001424 C   FIELD 01w01 CTCF (wo): Clear transfer complete flag Writing 1 clears the TCF flag in the OCTOSPI_SR register.
0x57001424 C   FIELD 03w01 CSMF (wo): Clear status match flag Writing 1 clears the SMF flag in the OCTOSPI_SR register.
0x57001424 C   FIELD 04w01 CTOF (wo): Clear timeout flag Writing 1 clears the TOF flag in the OCTOSPI_SR register.
0x57001440 B  REGISTER DLR: OCTOSPI data length register
0x57001440 C   FIELD 00w32 DL (rw): [31: 0]: Data length Number of data to be retrieved (value+1) in Indirect and Automatic status-polling modes. A value not greater than three (indicating 4 bytes) must be used for Automatic status-polling mode. All 1's in Indirect mode means undefined length, where OCTOSPI continues until the end of the memory, as defined by DEVSIZE. 0x0000_0000: 1 byte is to be transferred. 0x0000_0001: 2 bytes are to be transferred. 0x0000_0002: 3 bytes are to be transferred. 0x0000_0003: 4 bytes are to be transferred. ... 0xFFFF_FFFD: 4,294,967,294 (4G-2) bytes are to be transferred. 0xFFFF_FFFE: 4,294,967,295 (4G-1) bytes are to be transferred. 0xFFFF_FFFF: undefined length; all bytes, until the end of the external device, (as defined by DEVSIZE) are to be transferred. Continue reading indefinitely if DEVSIZE = 0x1F. DL[0] is stuck at 1 in dual-memory configuration (DMM = 1) even when 0 is written to this bit, thus assuring that each access transfers an even number of bytes. This field has no effect in Memory-mapped mode.
0x57001448 B  REGISTER AR: OCTOSPI address register
0x57001448 C   FIELD 00w32 ADDRESS (rw): Address Address to be sent to the external device. In HyperBus protocol, this field must be even as this protocol is 16-bit word oriented. In dual-memory configuration, AR[0] is forced to 1. Writes to this field are ignored when BUSY = 1 or when FMODE = 11 (Memory-mapped mode).
0x57001450 B  REGISTER DR: OCTOSPI data register
0x57001450 C   FIELD 00w32 DATA (rw): [31: 0]: Data Data to be sent/received to/from the external SPI device In Indirect-write mode, data written to this register is stored on the FIFO before it is sent to the external device during the data phase. If the FIFO is too full, a write operation is stalled until the FIFO has enough space to accept the amount of data being written. In Indirect-read mode, reading this register gives (via the FIFO) the data that was received from the external device. If the FIFO does not have as many bytes as requested by the read operation and if BUSY = 1, the read operation is stalled until enough data is present or until the transfer is complete, whichever happens first. In Automatic status-polling mode, this register contains the last data read from the external device (without masking). Word, half-word, and byte accesses to this register are supported. In Indirect-write mode, a byte write adds 1 byte to the FIFO, a half-word write 2 bytes, and a word write 4 bytes. Similarly, in Indirect-read mode, a byte read removes 1 byte from the FIFO, a halfword read 2 bytes, and a word read 4 bytes. Accesses in Indirect mode must be aligned to the bottom of this register: A byte read must read DATA[7:0] and a half-word read must read DATA[15:0].
0x57001480 B  REGISTER PSMKR: OCTOSPI polling status mask register
0x57001480 C   FIELD 00w32 MASK (rw): Status mask Mask to be applied to the status bytes received in Automatic status-polling mode For bit n:
0x57001488 B  REGISTER PSMAR: OCTOSPI polling status match register
0x57001488 C   FIELD 00w32 MATCH (rw): [31: 0]: Status match Value to be compared with the masked status register to get a match
0x57001490 B  REGISTER PIR: OCTOSPI polling interval register
0x57001490 C   FIELD 00w16 INTERVAL (rw): [15: 0]: Polling interval Number of CLK cycle between a read during the Automatic status-polling phases
0x57001500 B  REGISTER CCR: OCTOSPI communication configuration register
0x57001500 C   FIELD 00w03 IMODE (rw): Instruction mode This field defines the instruction phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001500 C   FIELD 03w01 IDTR (rw): Instruction double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the instruction phase.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 04w02 ISIZE (rw): Instruction size This bit defines instruction size.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 08w03 ADMODE (rw): Address mode This field defines the address phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001500 C   FIELD 11w01 ADDTR (rw): Address double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the address phase.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 12w02 ADSIZE (rw): Address size This field defines address size.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 16w03 ABMODE (rw): Alternate-byte mode This field defines the alternate-byte phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001500 C   FIELD 19w01 ABDTR (rw): Alternate bytes double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the alternate bytes phase. This field can be written only when BUSY = 0.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 20w02 ABSIZE (rw): Alternate bytes size This bit defines alternate bytes size.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 24w03 DMODE (rw): Data mode This field defines the data phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001500 C   FIELD 27w01 DDTR (rw): Data double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the data phase.
0x57001500 C   FIELD 29w01 DQSE (rw): DQS enable This bit enables the data strobe management.
0x57001508 B  REGISTER TCR: OCTOSPI timing configuration register
0x57001508 C   FIELD 00w05 DCYC (rw): Number of dummy cycles This field defines the duration of the dummy phase. In both SDR and DTR modes, it specifies a number of CLK cycles (0-31). It is recommended to have at least six dummy cycles when using memories with DQS activated.
0x57001508 C   FIELD 28w01 DHQC (rw): Delay hold quarter cycle
0x57001508 C   FIELD 30w01 SSHIFT (rw): Sample shift By default, the OCTOSPI samples data 1/2 of a CLK cycle after the data is driven by the external device. This bit allows the data to be sampled later in order to consider the external signal delays. The software must ensure that SSHIFT = 0 when the data phase is configured in DTR mode (when DDTR = 1.)
0x57001510 B  REGISTER IR: OCTOSPI instruction register
0x57001510 C   FIELD 00w32 INSTRUCTION (rw): Instruction Instruction to be sent to the external SPI device
0x57001520 B  REGISTER ABR: OCTOSPI alternate bytes register
0x57001520 C   FIELD 00w32 ALTERNATE (rw): [31: 0]: Alternate bytes Optional data to be sent to the external SPI device right after the address.
0x57001530 B  REGISTER LPTR: OCTOSPI low-power timeout register
0x57001530 C   FIELD 00w16 TIMEOUT (rw): [15: 0]: Timeout period After each access in Memory-mapped mode, the OCTOSPI prefetches the subsequent bytes and hold them in the FIFO. This field indicates how many CLK cycles the OCTOSPI waits after the clock becomes inactive and until it raises the NCS, putting the external device in a lower-consumption state.
0x57001540 B  REGISTER WPCCR: OCTOSPI wrap communication configuration register
0x57001540 C   FIELD 00w03 IMODE (rw): Instruction mode This field defines the instruction phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001540 C   FIELD 03w01 IDTR (rw): Instruction double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the instruction phase.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 04w02 ISIZE (rw): Instruction size This field defines instruction size.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 08w03 ADMODE (rw): Address mode This field defines the address phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001540 C   FIELD 11w01 ADDTR (rw): Address double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the address phase.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 12w02 ADSIZE (rw): Address size This field defines address size.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 16w03 ABMODE (rw): Alternate-byte mode This field defines the alternate byte phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001540 C   FIELD 19w01 ABDTR (rw): Alternate bytes double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the alternate bytes phase.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 20w02 ABSIZE (rw): Alternate bytes size This bit defines alternate bytes size.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 24w03 DMODE (rw): Data mode This field defines the data phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001540 C   FIELD 27w01 DDTR (rw): Data double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the data phase.
0x57001540 C   FIELD 29w01 DQSE (rw): DQS enable This bit enables the data strobe management.
0x57001548 B  REGISTER WPTCR: OCTOSPI wrap timing configuration register
0x57001548 C   FIELD 00w05 DCYC (rw): Number of dummy cycles This field defines the duration of the dummy phase. In both SDR and DTR modes, it specifies a number of CLK cycles (0-31). It is recommended to have at least 5 dummy cycles when using memories with DQS activated.
0x57001548 C   FIELD 28w01 DHQC (rw): Delay hold quarter cycle Add a quarter cycle delay on the outputs in DTR communication to match hold requirement.
0x57001548 C   FIELD 30w01 SSHIFT (rw): Sample shift By default, the OCTOSPI samples data 1/2 of a CLK cycle after the data is driven by the external device. This bit allows the data to be sampled later in order to consider the external signal delays. The firmware must assure that SSHIFT=0 when the data phase is configured in DTR mode (when DDTR = 1).
0x57001550 B  REGISTER WPIR: OCTOSPI wrap instruction register
0x57001550 C   FIELD 00w32 INSTRUCTION (rw): [31: 0]: Instruction Instruction to be sent to the external SPI device
0x57001560 B  REGISTER WPABR: OCTOSPI wrap alternate bytes register
0x57001560 C   FIELD 00w32 ALTERNATE (rw): [31: 0]: Alternate bytes Optional data to be sent to the external SPI device right after the address
0x57001580 B  REGISTER WCCR: OCTOSPI write communication configuration register
0x57001580 C   FIELD 00w03 IMODE (rw): Instruction mode This field defines the instruction phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001580 C   FIELD 03w01 IDTR (rw): Instruction double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the instruction phase.
0x57001580 C   FIELD 04w02 ISIZE (rw): Instruction size This bit defines instruction size:
0x57001580 C   FIELD 08w03 ADMODE (rw): Address mode This field defines the address phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001580 C   FIELD 11w01 ADDTR (rw): Address double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the address phase.
0x57001580 C   FIELD 12w02 ADSIZE (rw): Address size This field defines address size.
0x57001580 C   FIELD 16w03 ABMODE (rw): Alternate-byte mode This field defines the alternate-byte phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001580 C   FIELD 19w01 ABDTR (rw): Alternate bytes double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the alternate-bytes phase.
0x57001580 C   FIELD 20w02 ABSIZE (rw): Alternate bytes size This field defines alternate bytes size:
0x57001580 C   FIELD 24w03 DMODE (rw): Data mode This field defines the data phase mode of operation. 101-111: Reserved
0x57001580 C   FIELD 27w01 DDTR (rw): data double transfer rate This bit sets the DTR mode for the data phase.
0x57001580 C   FIELD 29w01 DQSE (rw): DQS enable This bit enables the data strobe management.
0x57001588 B  REGISTER WTCR: OCTOSPI write timing configuration register
0x57001588 C   FIELD 00w05 DCYC (rw): Number of dummy cycles This field defines the duration of the dummy phase. In both SDR and DTR modes, it specifies a number of CLK cycles (0-31). It is recommended to have at least 5 dummy cycles when using memories with DQS activated.
0x57001590 B  REGISTER WIR: OCTOSPI write instruction register
0x57001590 C   FIELD 00w32 INSTRUCTION (rw): Instruction Instruction to be sent to the external SPI device
0x570015A0 B  REGISTER WABR: OCTOSPI write alternate bytes register
0x570015A0 C   FIELD 00w32 ALTERNATE (rw): [31: 0]: Alternate bytes Optional data to be sent to the external SPI device right after the address
0x57001600 B  REGISTER HLCR: OCTOSPI HyperBus latency configuration register
0x57001600 C   FIELD 00w01 LM (rw): Latency mode This bit selects the Latency mode.
0x57001600 C   FIELD 01w01 WZL (rw): Write zero latency This bit enables zero latency on write operations.
0x57001600 C   FIELD 08w08 TACC (rw): [7: 0]: Access time Device access time expressed in number of communication clock cycles
0x57001600 C   FIELD 16w08 TRWR (rw): Read write recovery time Device read write recovery time expressed in number of communication clock cycles
INTERRUPT 000: WWDG (WWDG): Window Watchdog interrupt
INTERRUPT 004: TAMP (TAMP): TAMP global interrupt
INTERRUPT 005: RAMCFG (RAMCFG): RAM configuration global interrupt
INTERRUPT 006: FLASH (FLASH): FLASH non-secure global interrupt
INTERRUPT 007: FLASH_S (FLASH): FLASH secure global interrupt
INTERRUPT 008: GTZC (GTZC1_TZSC): GTZC global interrupt
INTERRUPT 009: RCC (RCC): RCC non-secure global interrupt
INTERRUPT 010: RCC_S (RCC): RCC secure global interrupt
INTERRUPT 011: EXTI0 (EXTI): EXTI Line0 interrupt
INTERRUPT 012: EXTI1 (EXTI): EXTI Line1 interrupt
INTERRUPT 013: EXTI2 (EXTI): EXTI Line2 interrupt
INTERRUPT 014: EXTI3 (EXTI): EXTI Line3 interrupt
INTERRUPT 015: EXTI4 (EXTI): EXTI Line4 interrupt
INTERRUPT 016: EXTI5 (EXTI): EXTI Line5 interrupt
INTERRUPT 017: EXTI6 (EXTI): EXTI Line6 interrupt
INTERRUPT 018: EXTI7 (EXTI): EXTI Line7 interrupt
INTERRUPT 019: EXTI8 (EXTI): EXTI Line8 interrupt
INTERRUPT 020: EXTI9 (EXTI): EXTI Line9 interrupt
INTERRUPT 021: EXTI10 (EXTI): EXTI Line10 interrupt
INTERRUPT 022: EXTI11 (EXTI): EXTI Line11 interrupt
INTERRUPT 023: EXTI12 (EXTI): EXTI Line12 interrupt
INTERRUPT 024: EXTI13 (EXTI): EXTI Line13 interrupt
INTERRUPT 025: EXTI14 (EXTI): EXTI Line14 interrupt
INTERRUPT 026: EXTI15 (EXTI): EXTI Line15 interrupt
INTERRUPT 027: GPDMA1_CH0 (GPDMA1): GPDMA1 channel 0 global interrupt
INTERRUPT 028: GPDMA1_CH1 (GPDMA1): GPDMA1 channel 1 global interrupt
INTERRUPT 029: GPDMA1_CH2 (GPDMA1): GPDMA1 channel 2 global interrupt
INTERRUPT 030: GPDMA1_CH3 (GPDMA1): GPDMA1 channel 3 global interrupt
INTERRUPT 031: GPDMA1_CH4 (GPDMA1): GPDMA1 channel 4 global interrupt
